  _quiz.push(
{"id":"s14x01","dom":"governance","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"PE投資先の取締役会で、リザーブドマター（投資家の事前承認が必要な事項）に通常含まれるものはどれか。","en":"Which item is normally included in the reserved matters (items needing prior investor approval) at a PE-backed company?"},"choices":[{"ja":"従業員が日常的に行う備品の購入や、事務用品の発注といった少額の業務","en":"Everyday purchases of equipment by employees and small orders of office supplies"},{"ja":"営業担当者ごとの訪問先と、商談の日程の調整","en":"Coordinating each salesperson's visits and meeting schedules"},{"ja":"一定額を超える借入や投資、M&A、CEOなど主要役員の選解任","en":"Borrowing or investment above set limits, M&A, and appointment or removal of key officers such as the CEO"},{"ja":"各部署の懇親会の開催日時の決定","en":"Deciding the dates of departmental social gatherings"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"リザーブドマターは、ファンドの投資価値を大きく左右する重要事項に限られる。一定額を超える借入・投資、買収・売却、CEOなどの選解任がその例である。日常の少額の業務まで承認を求めると、経営の機動力を損なう。","en":"Reserved matters are limited to important items that significantly affect the fund's investment value, such as borrowing or investment above a limit, M&A, and appointing or removing the CEO. Requiring approval for routine small matters would undermine managerial agility."}},
{"id":"s14x02","dom":"governance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ファンドが投資先から経営指導料（モニタリングフィー）を受け取る契約を結ぶ場合に、ガバナンス上とくに求められる対応はどれか。","en":"When a fund signs a contract to receive a monitoring fee from its portfolio company, which governance step is especially needed?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ファンドと投資先の合意だけで足りるので、取締役会への報告や開示は不要である","en":"Agreement between the fund and the company is enough, so no board reporting or disclosure is needed"},{"ja":"金額は投資先の業績にかかわらず、ファンドが自由に決めてよい","en":"The amount may be set freely by the fund regardless of the company's results"},{"ja":"貸し手に知られると融資条件が悪くなるので、契約の存在を伏せる","en":"Hide the contract because lenders learning of it would worsen loan terms"},{"ja":"利益相反として取締役会で開示・承認を得て、対価と役務を妥当な水準にする","en":"Treat it as a conflict of interest: disclose and obtain board approval, and keep the fee and services at a reasonable level"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"ファンドと投資先の間の対価の支払いは利益相反になりうる。取締役会で開示して承認を得て、役務に見合った妥当な金額にする。貸し手や他の株主に説明できない取り決めは、後で問題となる。","en":"Payments between the fund and the company can be a conflict of interest. Disclose them to the board, obtain approval, and set a fee that matches the services. An arrangement that cannot be explained to lenders or other shareholders causes trouble later."}},
{"id":"s14x03","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"PE投資先の取締役会に派遣される「オブザーバー」の位置づけとして最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which best describes the position of an \"observer\" sent to the board of a PE-backed company?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取締役ではなく、会議に出席して意見を述べられるが、議決権は持たない","en":"Not a director; may attend meetings and speak, but has no vote"},{"ja":"取締役と同じ議決権を持ち、取締役会の決議に参加できる一方で、会社に対する法的責任は負わない","en":"Has the same vote as a director and takes part in resolutions, but bears no legal responsibility to the company"},{"ja":"会社を代表して契約を結ぶ権限を持つ、代表取締役の補佐役である","en":"An assistant to the representative director with authority to sign contracts for the company"},{"ja":"監査役と同じ法定の権限を持ち、取締役の職務執行を監査する","en":"Holds the same statutory powers as an auditor and audits directors' execution of duties"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"オブザーバーは取締役ではなく、会議に出席して情報を得て意見を述べるが、議決権は持たない。少数の出資者が情報を得る手段として使われる。取締役と同じ議決権を持つ立場ではない。","en":"An observer is not a director; they attend meetings, receive information and speak, but cannot vote. This is often used by smaller investors to obtain information. It is not a position with a director's vote."}},
{"id":"s14x04","dom":"governance","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"PEが投資先に月次決算の早期化（例：翌月第5営業日までに確定）を求める主な理由はどれか。","en":"What is the main reason PE sponsors ask portfolio companies to speed up monthly closing (for example, finalizing by the fifth business day of the next month)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"法定の決算公告の期限が、翌月の第5営業日と定められているから","en":"The statutory deadline for publishing financial results is the fifth business day of the next month"},{"ja":"業績とKPIをすぐ把握して是正でき、財務制限条項のモニタリングにも使えるから","en":"It allows results and KPIs to be grasped and corrected quickly, and also supports monitoring of financial covenants"},{"ja":"決算を早く済ませれば、監査報酬を支払わなくてよくなるから","en":"Closing early removes the need to pay audit fees"},{"ja":"月次の数字は、取引先や従業員に毎月公開することが法律と金融機関との契約の両方で義務づけられているから","en":"The law requires monthly figures to be published every month to trading partners and employees"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"月次決算が早いほど、業績の悪化や計画との差を早く掴み、是正や追加施策に動ける。財務制限条項への抵触の兆しも早く見つけられる。月次の数字の公開義務や決算公告の期限が理由なのではない。","en":"The faster the monthly close, the sooner shortfalls against plan are noticed and corrective action taken, and signs of covenant breaches are found earlier. The reason is not a legal duty to publish monthly figures or a statutory deadline."}},
{"id":"s14x05","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"PE投資先で報酬委員会（または取締役会内の同等の機能）を設ける主な目的はどれか。","en":"What is the main purpose of setting up a compensation committee (or an equivalent board function) at a PE-backed company?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営陣の報酬を、経営陣自身が自由に決められるようにするため","en":"To let management freely decide its own pay"},{"ja":"従業員全員の給与額を、委員会の合議で個別に決めるため","en":"To decide every employee's salary individually by committee"},{"ja":"報酬の開示を避けるため、決定の過程と理由を取締役会や株主から切り離して秘匿するため","en":"To avoid disclosure of pay by separating the decision process from the board"},{"ja":"経営陣の報酬とMIPを、業績や株主利益に連動した基準で決めるため","en":"To set executive pay and the MIP using criteria tied to performance and shareholder interests"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"経営陣の報酬とMIPを、本人ではなく独立した立場の委員会が、業績と株主の利益に連動した基準で決めることで、利害の一致と公正さを保つ。経営陣自身に決めさせると、利益相反になる。","en":"Having an independent committee, rather than executives themselves, set executive pay and the MIP using criteria tied to performance and shareholder interests keeps incentives aligned and decisions fair. Letting executives decide their own pay creates a conflict of interest."}},
{"id":"s14x06","dom":"governance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"PEが複数の投資先の間で取引（共同調達や顧客紹介）を促す際の留意点として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate point to note when a PE sponsor encourages transactions between its portfolio companies (joint purchasing or customer referrals)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ファンドの意向で決めれば足りるので、価格は市場価格と異なっていてもよい","en":"The fund's wishes are enough, so prices may differ from market prices"},{"ja":"取引はすべて無償にして、片方の投資先の利益を犠牲にしても構わない","en":"Make every transaction free of charge, even at the expense of one company's profit"},{"ja":"独立当事者間と同等の条件で行い、少数株主や貸し手への影響に配慮する","en":"Deal on arm's-length terms and consider the effect on minority shareholders and lenders"},{"ja":"取引の存在は、売却の際の買い手には一切開示しなくてよい","en":"The existence of the transactions need never be disclosed to a buyer at exit"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"投資先同士の取引は、どちらかを犠牲にしないよう、独立当事者間と同等の条件で行い、少数株主や貸し手への影響を考える。売却時の買い手のデューデリジェンスで見つかるので、記録を整えておく。","en":"Transactions between portfolio companies should be on arm's-length terms so neither is sacrificed, with the effect on minority shareholders and lenders considered. Buyers will find them in due diligence at exit, so keep records in order."}},
{"id":"s14x07","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"内部通報制度の体制整備を公益通報者保護法が義務づけている事業者はどれか。","en":"Which businesses are required by the Whistleblower Protection Act to establish an internal whistleblowing system?"},"choices":[{"ja":"従業員の数や事業の規模にかかわらず、国内のすべての事業者","en":"All businesses in Japan, regardless of the number of employees or the scale of business"},{"ja":"常時使用する労働者が300人を超える事業者","en":"Businesses with more than 300 regularly employed workers"},{"ja":"上場会社に限られ、非上場会社は対象外","en":"Listed companies only, with unlisted companies excluded"},{"ja":"資本金が1億円を超える会社に限られる","en":"Only companies with capital over JPY 100 million"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"体制整備が義務となるのは、常時使用する労働者が300人を超える事業者で、300人以下は努力義務である（2026年10月時点）。上場の有無や資本金では決まらない。投資先の規模により、導入の優先度を判断する。","en":"The duty to establish a system applies to businesses with more than 300 regularly employed workers; those with 300 or fewer have a duty of best effort (as of October 2026). It does not depend on listing or capital. Judge priority by the portfolio company's size."}},
{"id":"s14x08","dom":"valuecreation","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"エントリー時のEBITDAが100億円、EV/EBITDAが8倍で、Exit時のEBITDAは150億円、倍率は8倍のままである。バリュークリエイションの分解で、EBITDA成長による価値の増加額はいくらか。","en":"EBITDA at entry is JPY 10 billion at 8x EV/EBITDA; EBITDA at exit is JPY 15 billion and the multiple stays at 8x. In a value creation bridge, how much value does EBITDA growth add?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50億円","en":"JPY 5 billion"},{"ja":"150億円","en":"JPY 15 billion"},{"ja":"400億円","en":"JPY 40 billion"},{"ja":"1,200億円","en":"JPY 120 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"EBITDA成長の寄与=(150−100)×エントリー倍率8=400億円。倍率の変化がないので、倍率の寄与は0である。EBITDAの増加額50億円や、Exit時の企業価値1,200億円を答えにしないこと。","en":"EBITDA growth contribution = (15 - 10) x entry multiple 8 = JPY 40bn. The multiple is unchanged, so the multiple contribution is zero. Do not answer with the EBITDA increase of 5bn or the exit enterprise value of 120bn."}},
{"id":"s14x09","dom":"valuecreation","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"エントリー時のEBITDAは100億円、倍率8倍、純有利子負債500億円（エクイティ300億円）。Exit時はEBITDA150億円、純有利子負債300億円で、倍率は8倍のまま。MOICはいくらか。","en":"At entry, EBITDA is JPY 10 billion at 8x with net debt of JPY 50 billion (equity of JPY 30 billion). At exit, EBITDA is JPY 15 billion and net debt is JPY 30 billion, with the multiple still 8x. What is the MOIC?"},"choices":[{"ja":"2.0倍","en":"2.0x"},{"ja":"3.0倍","en":"3.0x"},{"ja":"4.0倍","en":"4.0x"},{"ja":"1.5倍","en":"1.5x"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"Exit時のEV=150×8=1,200億円、エクイティ=1,200−300=900億円で、MOIC=900÷300=3.0倍。倍率が10倍なら(1,500−300)÷300=4.0倍になる。倍率の拡大に頼らなくても成立する計画かが頑健性の目安である。","en":"Exit EV = 150 x 8 = JPY 120bn, equity = 120 - 30 = JPY 90bn, so MOIC = 90 / 30 = 3.0x. At a 10x multiple it would be (150 - 30) / 30 = 4.0x. A plan that works without multiple expansion is more robust."}},
{"id":"s14x10","dom":"valuecreation","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"売上1,000億円、EBITDA100億円の会社が、販売数量を変えずに全製品を1%値上げできたとき、EBITDAはおよそいくら増えるか（コストは不変とする）。","en":"A company with sales of JPY 100 billion and EBITDA of JPY 10 billion raises prices on all products by 1% without changing volume. About how much does EBITDA rise (costs unchanged)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1億円","en":"JPY 100 million"},{"ja":"5億円","en":"JPY 500 million"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10 billion"},{"ja":"10億円","en":"JPY 1 billion"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"値上げ分はコストがかからずそのまま利益になるので、1,000億円×1%=10億円増える。EBITDA100億円に対して10%の増加になる。価格はEBITDAに直結する強いレバーだが、数量が減る影響も同時に検証する。","en":"The price increase drops straight to profit without added cost: JPY 100bn x 1% = JPY 1bn, a 10% increase on EBITDA of 10bn. Price is a powerful lever on EBITDA, but the volume effect must be tested at the same time."}},
{"id":"s14x11","dom":"valuecreation","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"SaaS企業のNRR（Net Revenue Retention、売上維持率）が110%であることの意味として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"What does it mean when a SaaS company's NRR (net revenue retention) is 110%?"},"choices":[{"ja":"解約や減額を差し引いても、既存顧客の売上が前年より10%増えている","en":"Even after churn and downgrades, revenue from existing customers is 10% higher than a year earlier"},{"ja":"新規顧客の獲得数が、前年より10%増えて、全体の売上も同じ割合で増えている","en":"The number of new customers is up 10% on last year and total sales rose at the same rate"},{"ja":"全顧客のうち、解約しなかった顧客の割合が110%である","en":"The share of customers that did not cancel is 110% of all customers"},{"ja":"売上の10%が、新規と既存の顧客から重複して計上されている","en":"10% of sales are double counted between new and existing customers"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"NRRは、前年の既存顧客から今年得た売上を前年の売上で割った値で、解約や減額を差し引き、追加購入や値上げを含める。110%なら新規顧客がゼロでも売上が10%伸びる。100%を超えるほど成長の質が高い。","en":"NRR is this year's revenue from last year's customers divided by their revenue last year, net of churn and downgrades and including upsell and price rises. At 110%, revenue grows 10% even with no new customers. The higher it is above 100%, the better the quality of growth."}},
{"id":"s14x12","dom":"valuecreation","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"投資委員会に示すベースケースを、経営陣の計画より保守的に置くことが多い理由として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Why is the base case presented to the investment committee often set more conservatively than management's plan?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営陣の計画は通常、実績より低めに作られているため、その分を上乗せする必要があるから","en":"Management plans are usually set below actual results, so an uplift must be added"},{"ja":"ベースケースを低く置くほど、ファンドの報酬が増えるから","en":"The lower the base case, the higher the fund's fees"},{"ja":"計画の楽観を割り引き、達成できなくても元本を守れるかを確認するため","en":"To discount plan optimism and check that capital is protected even if the plan is missed"},{"ja":"投資委員会は、数値の根拠より経営陣の熱意を重視するため","en":"The investment committee values management enthusiasm over the basis of the numbers"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"経営陣の計画は楽観に傾きやすいので、投資判断のベースケースは達成の確度を考えて割り引き、未達でも元本を守れるかを検証する。ベースケースの低さと報酬は関係せず、熱意でなく根拠のある数字で判断する。","en":"Management plans tend to be optimistic, so the base case for the investment decision is discounted for achievability, and tested for whether capital is protected if it is missed. Fees do not depend on how low the base case is, and decisions rest on substantiated numbers, not enthusiasm."}},
{"id":"s14x13","dom":"valuecreation","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"Exit直前に設備投資や保守費用を極端に抑えてEBITDAやFCFを良く見せた場合、買い手のデューデリジェンスではどうなりやすいか。","en":"If capex and maintenance spending are cut sharply just before exit to flatter EBITDA and FCF, what is likely to happen in the buyer's due diligence?"},"choices":[{"ja":"不足分がキャッチアップ投資として算定され、価格の引下げや調整につながりやすい","en":"The shortfall is quantified as catch-up investment and tends to lead to a price cut or adjustment"},{"ja":"買い手は直近の短期の数値だけを見るので、見せかけの改善がそのまま価格に反映される","en":"Buyers look only at recent short-term figures, so the apparent improvement flows straight into the price"},{"ja":"設備投資の抑制は、買い手にはまったく影響しないので、売り手の利益が増えるだけである","en":"Cutting capex does not affect the buyer at all, so the seller simply gains"},{"ja":"保守費用の削減は、会計基準上、売却益として計上される","en":"The saved maintenance cost is recorded as a gain on sale under accounting standards"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"買い手は設備の状態や過去の投資水準を調べ、先送りされた投資をキャッチアップ投資として価格から差し引く。短期の数値を良く見せる手法は見破られやすく、信頼も失う。継続的な投資で収益を高めるのが筋である。","en":"Buyers examine asset condition and past investment levels and deduct deferred spending as catch-up investment from the price. Flattering short-term figures is easily detected and also costs credibility. The sound approach is to raise earnings through sustained investment."}},
{"id":"s14x14","dom":"valuecreation","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"同じEBITDA成長でも、レバレッジが高いほどエクイティのIRRが高くなりやすい理由はどれか。","en":"Why does higher leverage tend to give a higher equity IRR for the same EBITDA growth?"},"choices":[{"ja":"借入が増えると、企業価値そのものが自動的に増えるので、エクイティの価値も同じ割合で増えるから","en":"More debt automatically raises enterprise value itself, so equity value rises at the same rate"},{"ja":"借入の利息は、株主への配当として扱われるから","en":"Interest on borrowings is treated as dividends to shareholders"},{"ja":"レバレッジが高いほど、事業のリスクが小さくなるから","en":"The higher the leverage, the lower the business risk"},{"ja":"借入コストが事業の収益率を下回る限り、少ない自己資金で価値の増加を得られるから","en":"As long as the cost of debt is below the return on the business, value gains are earned on less equity"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"借入コストが事業の収益率より低いと、同じ価値の増加を少ない自己資金で得られ、エクイティの収益率は高まる。ただし損失も拡大し、利払いと返済の負担が増える。借入で企業価値が自動的に増えるわけではない。","en":"When the cost of debt is below the return on the business, the same value gain is earned on less equity, so equity returns rise. Losses are also magnified and the burden of interest and repayment grows. Debt does not automatically raise enterprise value."}},
{"id":"s14x15","dom":"hundredday","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"カーブアウト（事業の切り出し）買収の初日（Day 1）までに、最低限動くようにしておくべきものはどれか。","en":"In a carve-out acquisition, what must at minimum be working by Day 1?"},"choices":[{"ja":"新しい企業理念を刷り込むための、全従業員向けの長期の研修プログラム","en":"A long training program for all employees to instill a new corporate philosophy"},{"ja":"給与の支払い、請求と入金、IT、主要な取引先との契約の承継","en":"Payroll, invoicing and collections, IT, and transfer of key customer contracts"},{"ja":"5年後を見据えた新ブランドの全面的な刷新","en":"A full renewal of the brand with a five-year horizon"},{"ja":"新しい本社ビルの建設の着工","en":"Starting construction of a new head office building"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"Day 1に事業が止まらないよう、給与、請求と入金、IT、主要契約の承継といった最低限の機能を先に整える。親会社からのサービスはTSAで補う。ブランド刷新や研修は、事業が安定してから進める。","en":"To keep the business running on Day 1, set up the minimum functions first: payroll, invoicing and collections, IT and transfer of key contracts. Services from the former parent are bridged by a TSA. Rebranding and training come after the business stabilizes."}},
{"id":"s14x16","dom":"hundredday","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"買収後の早い段階で「権限委譲表（DoA：Delegation of Authority）」を整える主な目的はどれか。","en":"What is the main purpose of putting a delegation of authority (DoA) table in place early after an acquisition?"},"choices":[{"ja":"決裁できる範囲を役職ごとに明確にし、統制と意思決定の速さを両立させるため","en":"To clarify what each position may approve, balancing control with decision speed"},{"ja":"すべての決裁を、金額の大小にかかわらず、ファンドの担当者一人に集中させるため","en":"To concentrate every approval, large or small, in one person at the fund"},{"ja":"現場の担当者に、金額の上限なしですべての契約の締結を認めるため","en":"To allow staff on the ground to sign all contracts with no monetary limit"},{"ja":"取締役会の議事録を作成する担当者を決めるため","en":"To decide who writes the board minutes"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"DoAは、金額や種類に応じて誰が決裁できるかを定める表である。重要事項は上位で統制し、日常の判断は現場に任せることで、統制と機動力を両立する。決裁の一極集中も、上限のない権限も、経営の質を下げる。","en":"A DoA defines who can approve what by amount and type. Important matters are controlled at higher levels while routine decisions stay with the front line, combining control and agility. Concentrating all approvals, or granting unlimited authority, degrades management."}},
{"id":"s14x17","dom":"hundredday","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"主要顧客との契約に、株主の異動があると相手方が契約を解除できるチェンジ・オブ・コントロール条項がある。買収の前後の実務として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"A key customer contract has a change-of-control clause allowing the counterparty to terminate if ownership changes. Which is the most appropriate practice around the acquisition?"},"choices":[{"ja":"条項の存在は契約上の細目にすぎないので、買収後もその確認をせずに放置する","en":"Treat the clause as a mere detail and leave it unchecked even after the acquisition"},{"ja":"条項を知らなかったことにして、相手方が気づくのを待つ","en":"Pretend not to know of the clause and wait for the counterparty to notice"},{"ja":"解除されると損失が大きいので、買収を取りやめる以外に方法はない","en":"Because termination would be costly, the only option is to cancel the acquisition"},{"ja":"クロージング前後に相手方の同意や放棄を取得し、影響を価格や条件に反映する","en":"Obtain the counterparty's consent or waiver around closing, and reflect the effect in price and terms"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"チェンジ・オブ・コントロール条項は、売上の大きい契約が失われる原因になる。DDで洗い出し、クロージング前後に同意や放棄を得る。得られない場合の影響は、価格や条件に織り込む。放置したり隠したりしてはならない。","en":"A change-of-control clause can cost a large contract. Identify it in due diligence and obtain consent or a waiver around closing. If it cannot be obtained, reflect the impact in price and terms. It must not be ignored or hidden."}},
{"id":"s14x18","dom":"hundredday","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"買収の発表直後に、全従業員に向けて経営陣が行うべきコミュニケーションとして最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Right after an acquisition is announced, which communication should management give to all employees?"},"choices":[{"ja":"個別の質問は受け付けず、詳細は後日の掲示だけで知らせる","en":"Take no individual questions and give details only by a later notice"},{"ja":"人員削減の予定がある場合でも、不安を避けるため全く触れず、あいまいな説明にとどめる","en":"Even if cuts are planned, avoid mentioning them to prevent anxiety and keep explanations vague"},{"ja":"新しい株主の方針と今後の見通しを、質問の機会も含めて早く、率直に伝える","en":"Explain the new shareholder's policy and outlook early and candidly, including a chance for questions"},{"ja":"取引先への発表を先に済ませ、従業員には数か月後に伝える","en":"Announce to trading partners first and tell employees several months later"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"発表直後は不安が最も高いので、新しい株主の方針や見通しを早く率直に伝え、質問の場を設ける。情報がないと憶測が広がり、中核人材の離職を招く。従業員への説明を後回しにしてはならない。","en":"Anxiety is highest right after the announcement, so explain the new owner's policy and outlook early and candidly, and open a forum for questions. Without information, rumors spread and core staff leave. Employees must not be told last."}},
{"id":"s14x19","dom":"hundredday","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"100日プランの終盤に、バリュークリエイション計画（VCP）を確定して取締役会で承認を得る意義として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Why does the board approve a finalized value creation plan (VCP) near the end of the 100-day plan?"},"choices":[{"ja":"計画を確定すると以後の修正が一切禁止されるので、経営陣の自由度が守られる","en":"Finalizing the plan prohibits any later revision, which protects management's freedom"},{"ja":"初動で得た実情を反映した目標とKPIを共有して、進捗管理の基準にするため","en":"To share targets and KPIs that reflect what was learned in the early phase and use them as the basis of progress tracking"},{"ja":"ファンドの投資委員会に提出した資料を、そのまま更新せずに再利用するため","en":"To reuse the material submitted to the investment committee without updating it"},{"ja":"取締役会の承認を得ると、金融機関への報告が不要になるため","en":"To make reporting to lenders unnecessary once the board approves"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"最初の100日でわかった実情をVCPの目標とKPIに反映し、取締役会で承認して関係者の共通の物差しにする。投資時の資料の再利用では、現場の実態とずれる。承認しても貸し手への報告義務はなくならない。","en":"What was learned in the first 100 days is built into the VCP targets and KPIs and approved by the board as a common yardstick. Reusing the investment-stage material would diverge from reality on the ground. Board approval does not remove reporting duties to lenders."}},
{"id":"s14x20","dom":"hundredday","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"買収後の100日で、売り手の表明保証に反する事実が見つかった。補償請求の観点で最も適切な対応はどれか。","en":"Within the first 100 days after acquisition, a fact contrary to the seller's representations and warranties is found. Which response is the most appropriate for an indemnity claim?"},"choices":[{"ja":"契約の通知期限と手続を確認し、証拠を整えて速やかに売り手へ通知する","en":"Check the notice deadline and procedure in the contract, assemble evidence and promptly notify the seller"},{"ja":"補償請求には期限がないので、事業が落ち着く数年後にまとめて請求するのが望ましい","en":"There is no deadline for indemnity claims, so it is best to claim all together several years later when the business has settled"},{"ja":"売り手との関係を壊さないよう、事実を伏せて自社で損失を吸収する","en":"To preserve the relationship with the seller, hide the fact and absorb the loss internally"},{"ja":"請求の可否は裁判所だけが決めるので、契約を確認せず直ちに提訴する","en":"Only a court can decide a claim, so sue immediately without reviewing the contract"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"表明保証違反の補償請求には、通知の期限や手続、請求額の下限などが契約で定められているのが通常である。見つけたら早く証拠を整えて通知し、期限を逃さないようにする。何もしないと権利を失いかねない。","en":"Indemnity claims for breach of warranties normally come with contractual notice deadlines, procedures and thresholds. Once found, assemble evidence and give notice early so as not to miss the deadline. Doing nothing risks losing the right."}},
{"id":"s14x21","dom":"hundredday","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"100日プランを進める際、PMO（Project Management Office）を設ける主な目的として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"What is the main purpose of setting up a PMO (Project Management Office) when running a 100-day plan?"},"choices":[{"ja":"施策の実行責任を現場から取り上げ、PMOの担当者だけですべて実施するため","en":"To take execution responsibility away from the front line and have PMO staff alone carry out everything"},{"ja":"進捗の報告を減らし、問題が起きた場合のみ経営陣に伝えるため","en":"To reduce progress reports and tell management only when problems occur"},{"ja":"施策の進捗・課題・依存関係を一元管理し、遅れを早めに見つけて支援するため","en":"To manage progress, issues and dependencies in one place and spot delays early to help"},{"ja":"ファンドの担当者が、現場の担当者を直接評価して処遇を決めるため","en":"So that the fund's staff can directly evaluate frontline staff and decide their treatment"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"PMOは、複数の施策の進捗、課題、相互の依存関係を一元的に管理し、遅れを早く見つけて支援する。実行の責任は現場の施策オーナーにあり、PMOが取り上げるものではない。報告を減らす役割でもない。","en":"A PMO manages the progress, issues and interdependencies of multiple initiatives centrally and helps by spotting delays early. Execution responsibility stays with the initiative owners and is not taken over by the PMO, nor does it exist to reduce reporting."}},
{"id":"s14x22","dom":"operations","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"EBITDA100億円、購買額（調達費）400億円の会社が、調達の見直しで購買額を3%削減できた。EBITDAはおよそ何%増えるか（他は不変）。","en":"A company with EBITDA of JPY 10 billion and purchasing spend of JPY 40 billion cuts spend by 3% through procurement review. By about what percent does EBITDA rise (all else equal)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"3%","en":"3%"},{"ja":"10%","en":"10%"},{"ja":"12%","en":"12%"},{"ja":"40%","en":"40%"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"削減額=400億円×3%=12億円で、コスト削減は全額がEBITDAの増加になる。12億÷100億=12%増。購買額が大きい会社では、小さな削減率でも利益を大きく動かせる。削減率の3%をそのまま使うのは誤りである。","en":"Savings = JPY 40bn x 3% = JPY 1.2bn, and the whole cost reduction drops into EBITDA: 1.2 / 10 = 12%. For companies with large purchasing spend, even a small percentage saving moves profit a lot. Using the 3% saving rate directly is wrong."}},
{"id":"s14x23","dom":"operations","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"満稼働時の売上が1,000億円、変動費率が60%、固定費が250億円の工場で、稼働率が70%から80%に上がると、EBITDAはいくら増えるか（固定費は不変）。","en":"A plant has sales of JPY 100 billion at full capacity, a variable cost ratio of 60% and fixed costs of JPY 25 billion. If utilization rises from 70% to 80%, by how much does EBITDA rise (fixed costs unchanged)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"10億円","en":"JPY 1 billion"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10 billion"},{"ja":"60億円","en":"JPY 6 billion"},{"ja":"40億円","en":"JPY 4 billion"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"稼働率70%のEBITDAは700×0.4−250=30億円、80%では800×0.4−250=70億円で、差は40億円。増える売上100億円に限界利益率40%を掛けた額と等しい。売上増100億円や変動費率60%を掛けた60億円は誤りである。","en":"At 70% utilization EBITDA is 700 x 0.4 - 250 = JPY 3bn; at 80% it is 800 x 0.4 - 250 = JPY 7bn, a difference of JPY 4bn, equal to the added sales of 10bn times the contribution margin of 40%. The 10bn sales increase, or 6bn using the variable cost ratio, is wrong."}},
{"id":"s14x24","dom":"operations","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある設備の時間稼働率が90%、性能稼働率が95%、良品率が98%のとき、OEE（総合設備効率）はおよそいくらか。","en":"A machine has an availability of 90%, a performance rate of 95% and a quality rate of 98%. What is its OEE (overall equipment effectiveness) approximately?"},"choices":[{"ja":"94.3%","en":"94.3%"},{"ja":"83.8%","en":"83.8%"},{"ja":"90.0%","en":"90.0%"},{"ja":"98.0%","en":"98.0%"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"OEE=時間稼働率×性能稼働率×良品率=0.90×0.95×0.98≒83.8%。3つを平均した94.3%は誤りである。各要素のロスが掛け合わさるため、個々の数字が高くても総合では低くなる。","en":"OEE = availability x performance x quality = 0.90 x 0.95 x 0.98, about 83.8%. Averaging the three (94.3%) is wrong. Losses compound multiplicatively, so the overall figure is lower even when each factor looks high."}},
{"id":"s14x25","dom":"operations","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"複数の投資先で共通して使う資材やサービスをまとめて調達する（共同調達）ことの主な効果はどれか。","en":"What is the main benefit of jointly procuring materials and services used in common across several portfolio companies?"},"choices":[{"ja":"購入量をまとめて交渉力を高め、単価を下げられる","en":"Pooling volumes raises bargaining power and lowers unit prices"},{"ja":"各社の購買担当者を一切不要にし、人件費を完全になくせる","en":"It makes every company's purchasing staff unnecessary and removes personnel costs completely"},{"ja":"仕入先との契約条件を全社で一律にするため、どの会社の事情も考慮しなくてよい","en":"Contract terms are the same for all companies, so no company's circumstances need be considered"},{"ja":"購入量が増えるので、使用量そのものが自動的に増えて収益が上がる","en":"Purchase volume grows, so usage itself rises automatically and earnings improve"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"購入量をまとめると仕入先への交渉力が高まり、単価や条件を改善できる。ただし各社の仕様や事情の違いは調整が必要で、購買担当が不要になるわけではない。使用量が増えて収益が上がる効果もない。","en":"Pooling volume strengthens bargaining power and improves prices and terms. Differences in specifications and circumstances still need adjusting, and purchasing staff do not become unnecessary. It also does not raise usage or earnings."}},
{"id":"s14x26","dom":"operations","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"営業の生産性を高めるために、PEが重視する指標の考え方として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate view of the metrics a PE sponsor emphasizes to raise sales productivity?"},"choices":[{"ja":"訪問件数だけを増やすことを目標とし、それが受注に結びついたかどうかは問わない","en":"Aim only to increase the number of visits, regardless of whether they lead to orders"},{"ja":"営業担当者の人数を増やすことだけを成果とする","en":"Treat only an increase in the number of salespeople as the result"},{"ja":"売上の総額だけを毎月確認し、案件の進み具合は見ない","en":"Check only total monthly sales without looking at the progress of deals"},{"ja":"案件数、段階ごとの転換率、受注単価など、受注までの流れを分解して管理する","en":"Break down and manage the flow to orders: number of deals, conversion at each stage and average deal size"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"売上を、案件数、段階ごとの転換率、受注単価などに分解すると、どこで失注しているか、どこを改善すれば成果が出るかが見える。訪問件数や人数だけを増やしても、受注に結びつかなければ生産性は上がらない。","en":"Decomposing sales into the number of deals, conversion at each stage and deal size shows where orders are lost and what to improve. Increasing visits or headcount alone does not raise productivity unless it turns into orders."}},
{"id":"s14x27","dom":"operations","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"設備投資が重い事業を評価するとき、EBITDAだけでなく「EBITDA−設備投資」も見る理由として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Why look at \"EBITDA minus capex\" as well as EBITDA when evaluating a capital-intensive business?"},"choices":[{"ja":"設備投資は、損益計算書の費用として全額が即時に計上され、EBITDAを直接減らすから","en":"Capex is expensed in full immediately in the income statement and directly reduces EBITDA"},{"ja":"EBITDAには設備投資が含まれず、キャッシュ創出力を過大に見せうるから","en":"EBITDA excludes capex and can overstate cash-generating power"},{"ja":"設備投資が多いほど、EBITDAが必ず減少するから","en":"The more capex, the more EBITDA always decreases"},{"ja":"EBITDAは、税金と利息の影響を含んでいるから","en":"EBITDA includes the effects of taxes and interest"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"EBITDAは設備投資を引く前の数字なので、更新や拡張の投資が重い事業では、実際に手元に残るキャッシュを過大に見せる。EBITDAから設備投資を引くと、返済や配当に回せる力に近づく。","en":"EBITDA is before capex, so in businesses with heavy replacement or expansion spending it overstates the cash actually left. Subtracting capex gets closer to the capacity available for debt service and distributions."}},
{"id":"s14x28","dom":"operations","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"仕入先の数を絞る（サプライヤーの集約）ことの狙いと注意点として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which best states the aim and the caution of consolidating the number of suppliers?"},"choices":[{"ja":"仕入先を1社に絞れば、価格交渉は不要になり、供給途絶の心配もなく、品質も自動的に安定する","en":"Narrowing to one supplier makes price negotiation unnecessary, removes any worry about supply interruption and stabilizes quality automatically"},{"ja":"仕入先を絞ると品質管理が難しくなるので、必ず増やすべきである","en":"Narrowing suppliers makes quality control harder, so the number must always be increased"},{"ja":"数量をまとめて単価と管理の手間を減らせるが、供給途絶の集中リスクに備える","en":"Volumes are pooled to cut unit prices and administrative effort, but prepare for the concentration risk of supply disruption"},{"ja":"仕入先の数は、コストにも調達の安定性にも影響しない","en":"The number of suppliers affects neither cost nor stability of supply"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"仕入先を集約すると数量が集まり、単価の低下と管理の手間の削減が見込める。一方、特定の仕入先に依存するため、供給の途絶に備えて代替の確保や在庫の水準を決めておく必要がある。","en":"Consolidating suppliers pools volume, reducing unit prices and administration. However, dependence on a few suppliers requires preparing for supply disruption through alternative sources and agreed inventory levels."}},
{"id":"s14x29","dom":"talent","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"総エクイティ100億円の内訳は、ファンドの優先株90億円（償還が優先、配当なし）と、普通株10億円（ファンド5億円、経営陣5億円）である。Exit時のエクイティ価値が150億円のとき、経営陣の投資倍率はいくらか。","en":"Total equity of JPY 10 billion consists of the fund's preferred shares of JPY 9 billion (redeemed first, no dividend) and common shares of JPY 1 billion (fund JPY 500 million, management JPY 500 million). If equity value at exit is JPY 15 billion, what is management's money multiple?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1.5倍","en":"1.5x"},{"ja":"3.0倍","en":"3.0x"},{"ja":"6.0倍","en":"6.0x"},{"ja":"12倍","en":"12x"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"優先株90億円が先に償還され、残りは60億円。普通株の50%を持つ経営陣は30億円を受け取り、30÷5=6.0倍になる。ファンド全体は(90+30)÷95≒1.26倍にとどまる。優先株の構造が経営陣への上振れの配分を大きくする。","en":"Preferred shares of JPY 9bn are redeemed first, leaving 6bn. Management, holding 50% of the common, receives 3bn: 3 / 0.5 = 6.0x. The fund overall gets only (9 + 3) / 9.5, about 1.26x. The preferred structure magnifies the upside allocated to management."}},
{"id":"s14x30","dom":"talent","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"MIPのバッド・リーバー条項の説明として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which best explains the bad leaver clause of a MIP?"},"choices":[{"ja":"不正や自己都合で退任した経営陣の株式を、低い価格で買い戻せる条項","en":"A clause allowing shares of executives who leave for misconduct or of their own accord to be bought back at a low price"},{"ja":"経営陣の在任中に会社の業績が悪化した場合に、報酬や持株比率を自動的に増額する条項","en":"A clause that automatically raises pay or shareholding when company performance worsens during tenure"},{"ja":"ファンドが株式を売却する際に、経営陣にも同じ条件での売却を義務づける条項","en":"A clause obliging management to sell on the same terms when the fund sells its shares"},{"ja":"経営陣が競合他社に転職することを、退任後も無期限に認める条項","en":"A clause allowing executives to join competitors indefinitely after leaving"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"バッド・リーバーは、不正や自己都合での退任など、会社に責めのある退任を指す。その場合は株式を取得価額や低い価格で買い戻せるようにして、在籍や誠実な勤務を促す。会社都合の退任はグッド・リーバーとして扱いが異なる。","en":"A bad leaver is someone who leaves in circumstances attributable to them, such as misconduct or a voluntary departure. Their shares can be bought back at cost or a low price, encouraging retention and good conduct. Departures at the company's initiative are good leavers and treated differently."}},
{"id":"s14x31","dom":"talent","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"PE投資先で、常勤CFOの採用までの間に、暫定的に外部のCFO（インテリムCFO）を起用する主な狙いはどれか。","en":"What is the main aim of appointing an external interim CFO at a PE-backed company until a permanent CFO is hired?"},"choices":[{"ja":"常勤CFOの採用を取りやめ、以後は恒久的に外部のCFOへ業務を委託する形へ切り替えるため","en":"To abandon hiring a permanent CFO and permanently outsource the work to an external CFO"},{"ja":"資金管理、報告体制、Exit準備を早く立ち上げ、常勤CFOへ円滑に引き継ぐため","en":"To set up cash management, reporting and exit preparation quickly and hand over smoothly to a permanent CFO"},{"ja":"監査法人の役割を代替し、会計監査を不要にするため","en":"To replace the auditor and make the audit unnecessary"},{"ja":"ファンドの担当者が、CFOの業務を直接代行するため","en":"So that the fund's staff can directly perform the CFO's work"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"資金管理や月次報告、Exit準備は投資後すぐに必要になるので、経験のあるインテリムCFOで早く立ち上げ、常勤CFOへ引き継ぐ。会計監査は独立した監査人の役割で、CFOが代わることはできない。","en":"Cash management, monthly reporting and exit preparation are needed right after investment, so an experienced interim CFO starts them quickly and hands over to a permanent CFO. The audit is the independent auditor's role and cannot be taken over by a CFO."}},
{"id":"s14x32","dom":"talent","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"オーナー経営者が会社を売却する際、売却代金の一部を再出資して株主として残る（ロールオーバー）ことの主な狙いはどれか。","en":"When an owner-manager sells a company and reinvests part of the proceeds to stay on as a shareholder (rollover), what is the main aim?"},"choices":[{"ja":"売却代金を全額現金で受け取り、会社や買い手との関係を完全に断ち切るため","en":"To receive all proceeds in cash and cut ties with the company and the buyer completely"},{"ja":"買い手に、売却代金の支払いを無期限に延ばしてもらうため","en":"To have the buyer postpone payment of the price indefinitely"},{"ja":"経営権を維持したまま、取引の価格を一切変えないため","en":"To keep control while changing nothing in the deal price"},{"ja":"売り手の利害を買い手と一致させ、経営の継続と承継を円滑にするため","en":"To align the seller's interests with the buyer and smooth the continuity and succession of management"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"ロールオーバーでは、売り手が一部の株式を持ち続けるため、価値向上への動機づけが買い手と一致する。経営のノウハウと顧客との関係の承継も円滑になる。全額を現金で受け取って関係を断つ形とは異なる。","en":"In a rollover the seller keeps part of the equity, so incentives to raise value align with the buyer, and the transfer of know-how and customer relationships becomes smoother. This differs from taking all proceeds in cash and walking away."}},
{"id":"s14x33","dom":"talent","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"経営陣の年次賞与の指標をEBITDAだけに連動させると生じやすい問題と、その対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"What problem tends to arise when annual executive bonuses are linked to EBITDA alone, and what is the most appropriate response?"},"choices":[{"ja":"運転資本の悪化を招きやすいため、キャッシュ創出の指標を組み合わせる","en":"It tends to worsen working capital, so combine it with a cash generation metric"},{"ja":"EBITDAは短期の指標なので、賞与の指標は非上場でも把握できる株価だけにするのが望ましい","en":"EBITDA is a short-term metric, so bonuses should depend only on share price, which is observable even for unlisted firms"},{"ja":"指標を増やすほど経営陣の負担が増えるので、EBITDAに加えるものは何もない","en":"Adding metrics burdens management more, so nothing should be added to EBITDA"},{"ja":"賞与は固定額にして、業績との連動はすべて外すべきである","en":"Bonuses should be fixed amounts with all links to performance removed"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"EBITDAだけに連動させると、売上の押し込みや在庫の積み増しなど、運転資本を悪化させてでも利益を作る動きを招く。キャッシュ創出（キャッシュ・コンバージョンなど）を組み合わせて、利益の質を担保する。","en":"Linking pay to EBITDA alone invites pushing sales or building inventory to make profit at the expense of working capital. Combine it with cash generation metrics such as cash conversion to safeguard the quality of earnings."}},
{"id":"s14x34","dom":"talent","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"投資後の早い時期に、従業員のエンゲージメント調査を行う主な目的はどれか。","en":"What is the main purpose of running an employee engagement survey soon after investment?"},"choices":[{"ja":"従業員の氏名と所属を一覧にして、人員削減の対象者を決めるため","en":"To list employees by name and unit and decide who will be laid off"},{"ja":"離職リスクや組織の課題を把握して、施策の優先順位を決めるため","en":"To grasp attrition risk and organizational issues and prioritize measures"},{"ja":"調査の回答の結果に応じて、個人の賞与を自動的に決めるため","en":"To automatically set individual bonuses according to survey answers"},{"ja":"経営陣の人事評価を、従業員の投票だけで決めるため","en":"To decide management appraisals by employee vote alone"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"エンゲージメント調査は、意欲や不満、離職しそうな層や組織の課題を数値で把握し、施策の優先順位を決める材料にする。個人の処遇や人員削減の選定に使うと、回答が歪み、調査の信頼を失う。","en":"An engagement survey quantifies motivation, dissatisfaction, groups at risk of leaving and organizational issues to prioritize action. Using it to decide individual treatment or layoffs distorts answers and destroys trust in the survey."}},
{"id":"s14x35","dom":"talent","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"業績の悪化でMIPの普通株やオプションの価値がほぼなくなり（アンダーウォーター）、経営陣の意欲が下がっている。見直しの議論で最も適切な考え方はどれか。","en":"Poor performance has left MIP shares or options almost worthless (underwater), and management morale is falling. Which approach is the most appropriate in the review discussion?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営陣の意欲を保つため、ファンドの判断だけで、他の株主に知らせず条件を自由に引き下げる","en":"To keep management motivated, the fund alone lowers the terms freely without informing other shareholders"},{"ja":"業績が悪い責任は経営陣にあるので、どのような場合も見直しはしない","en":"Management is responsible for poor results, so no review is ever made"},{"ja":"見直しは、すべての従業員のMIPの条件をゼロにすることを意味する","en":"A review means setting the MIP terms of all employees to zero"},{"ja":"追加付与や条件変更は、株主間の公平と貸し手との合意と、取締役会の承認を踏まえて検討する","en":"Consider additional grants or changes in light of fairness among shareholders, agreement with lenders and board approval"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"MIPの価値がなくなるとリテンションの力が失われるので、追加付与や条件の変更が議論される。ただし他の株主との公平、貸し手との合意、取締役会の承認が前提で、ファンドの一存で進めてはならない。","en":"When MIP value disappears, its retention power is lost, so additional grants or changes are discussed. They require fairness among shareholders, agreement with lenders and board approval, and must not be pushed through by the fund alone."}},
{"id":"s14x36","dom":"capital","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本の株式会社が配当リキャップ（借入による追加配当）を行う際の制約として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate constraint when a Japanese stock company carries out a dividend recap (an extra dividend funded by borrowing)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"配当は会社法上の分配可能額の範囲内に限られ、不足するときは資本金等の減少を検討する","en":"Dividends are limited to the distributable amount under the Companies Act, and if it is insufficient, consider reducing capital and similar"},{"ja":"借入さえ実行できれば、剰余金や純資産の額にかかわらず、借入額に相当する配当をいくらでも出せる","en":"As long as the borrowing is executed, dividends equal to the loan can be paid in any amount regardless of surplus or net assets"},{"ja":"配当リキャップは、会社法上、株主総会の決議なしに取締役が自由に行える","en":"Under the Companies Act, directors may carry out a dividend recap freely without a shareholders' resolution"},{"ja":"分配可能額の制約は上場会社だけに適用され、非上場会社には適用されない","en":"The distributable amount limit applies only to listed companies and not to unlisted ones"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"会社法では、剰余金の配当は分配可能額の範囲内に限られ、借入があっても配当原資が増えるわけではない。剰余金が足りないときは、資本金や準備金の減少（債権者保護手続を伴う）などを検討する。","en":"Under the Companies Act, dividends are limited to the distributable amount, and borrowing does not enlarge the source of dividends. If surplus is insufficient, consider reducing capital or reserves (which involves creditor protection procedures)."}},
{"id":"s14x37","dom":"capital","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"LBOで、買収目的の会社（SPC）が対象会社を買収した後、両社を合併する（または税務上のグループ通算制度を使う）主な狙いとして最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"In an LBO, after the acquisition vehicle (SPC) buys the target, what is the main aim of merging the two (or using the group tax consolidation regime)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"借入金のうち、利息の部分を自動的に免除させ、元本だけを返済すれば足りるようにするため","en":"To have the interest portion of the borrowing automatically waived so that repaying principal is enough"},{"ja":"対象会社の株主に、新しい株式を無償で配るため","en":"To distribute new shares to the target's shareholders free of charge"},{"ja":"合併すると、金融機関の同意なしに借入条件を自由に変更できるため","en":"Because after a merger the loan terms can be changed freely without the lenders' consent"},{"ja":"対象会社の利益とSPCの支払利息を相殺し、返済原資を同一の法人に置くため","en":"To offset the target's profit against the SPC's interest expense and place the repayment resources in the same entity"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"SPC単体は収益がなく、支払利息を損金にしても節税効果を使えない。合併や通算制度で対象会社の利益と相殺し、返済原資も同じ法人に置く。損金算入には過大支払利子税制などの制限がある（2026年10月時点）。","en":"The SPC alone has no income, so deducting interest yields no tax benefit. A merger or tax consolidation lets it offset the target's profit and places repayment resources in the same entity. Deductibility is restricted by rules such as the excess interest limitation (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s14x38","dom":"capital","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"純有利子負債300億円、EBITDA60億円（5.0倍）の会社の財務制限条項が、純有利子負債/EBITDAを5.5倍以下としている。純有利子負債が変わらないとき、EBITDAがおよそ何%減ると抵触するか。","en":"A company has net debt of JPY 30 billion and EBITDA of JPY 6 billion (5.0x), and a covenant requires net debt/EBITDA of 5.5x or lower. With net debt unchanged, by about what percent must EBITDA fall to breach it?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約9.1%","en":"About 9.1%"},{"ja":"約10.0%","en":"About 10.0%"},{"ja":"約5.0%","en":"About 5.0%"},{"ja":"約18.2%","en":"About 18.2%"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"抵触するEBITDAは300÷5.5≒54.5億円で、60億円からの減少率は約9.1%。倍率の差0.5を5.0で割った10%は、分母のEBITDAが動くことを無視した誤りである。余裕（ヘッドルーム）を数字で把握しておく。","en":"The breach point for EBITDA is 300 / 5.5, about JPY 5.45bn, a fall of about 9.1% from 6bn. The 10% obtained by dividing the 0.5 gap by 5.0 ignores that the denominator, EBITDA, is what moves. Know the headroom numerically."}},
{"id":"s14x39","dom":"capital","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"LBOのメザニンローン（劣後ローン）の特徴として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which best describes the features of a mezzanine (subordinated) loan in an LBO?"},"choices":[{"ja":"シニアローンより返済順位が高く、金利も低いので、最も安全で割安な調達手段である","en":"It ranks ahead of senior loans and carries a lower rate, so it is the safest and cheapest source of funds"},{"ja":"株式と同じ扱いなので、金利は発生せず、返済の義務もない","en":"It is treated like equity, so no interest accrues and there is no obligation to repay"},{"ja":"シニアローンに劣後する分、金利が高く、エクイティを増やさずに資金を補える","en":"It is subordinated to senior loans, so carries a higher rate, and supplements funding without increasing equity"},{"ja":"担保を必ず最優先で取得でき、破綻時にも全額が回収される","en":"It always takes first-ranking security and is recovered in full on bankruptcy"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"メザニンはシニアに劣後し、破綻時の回収が後回しになる分、金利が高い。エクイティを増やさずに借入余力を補えるが、金利負担が増え、返済順位の低さは貸し手との契約で定まる。","en":"Mezzanine ranks behind senior debt, so recovery in a bankruptcy comes later and the rate is higher. It supplements debt capacity without more equity, but increases interest burden, and its ranking is set by the lenders' agreements."}},
{"id":"s14x40","dom":"capital","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"変動金利のシニアローンを使うLBOで、金利スワップや金利キャップによるヘッジを行う主な目的はどれか。","en":"In an LBO using a floating-rate senior loan, what is the main purpose of hedging with interest rate swaps or caps?"},"choices":[{"ja":"金利が下がった場合に、借入金が自動的に減額されるようにするため","en":"To have the loan automatically reduced when rates fall"},{"ja":"金利上昇による利払いの増加を抑え、返済計画の確実性を高めるため","en":"To limit higher interest payments from rising rates and improve the certainty of the repayment plan"},{"ja":"借入の元本を、将来の金利にかかわらず確実に免除させるため","en":"To have the principal reliably forgiven regardless of future rates"},{"ja":"金利の変動で利益を得ることを主な目的とし、ファンドの収益源にするため","en":"To profit from rate movements as the main purpose and make it a source of fund income"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"変動金利では金利が上がると利払いが増え、カバレッジが悪化する。スワップやキャップで金利を固定または上限を付けると、キャッシュフローの見通しが安定する。ヘッジは損益を狙う取引ではなく、リスクを抑える手段である。","en":"With a floating rate, rising rates increase interest payments and weaken coverage. Swaps or caps fix or cap the rate and steady the cash flow outlook. Hedging is a risk reduction tool, not a trade to seek profit."}},
{"id":"s14x41","dom":"capital","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"EBITDA20億円のアドオン企業を6倍（120億円）で取得した。統合後はプラットフォームと同じ10倍で評価されるとき、倍率差による価値の上乗せはいくらか（シナジーと統合費用は除く）。","en":"An add-on company with EBITDA of JPY 2 billion is acquired at 6x (JPY 12 billion). If it is valued at the platform's 10x after integration, how much value does the multiple gap add (excluding synergies and integration costs)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"40億円","en":"JPY 4 billion"},{"ja":"80億円","en":"JPY 8 billion"},{"ja":"120億円","en":"JPY 12 billion"},{"ja":"200億円","en":"JPY 20 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"統合後の評価額=20億円×10=200億円で、取得額120億円との差は80億円。これがマルチプル・アービトラージである。200億円は評価額、120億円は取得額で、上乗せ分ではない。実際にはシナジーの実現や統合費用で変わる。","en":"Post-integration value = JPY 2bn x 10 = JPY 20bn, and the gap from the purchase price of 12bn is JPY 8bn. This is multiple arbitrage. 20bn is the valuation and 12bn the price, neither is the uplift. In practice, synergy realization and integration costs change the result."}},
{"id":"s14x42","dom":"capital","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"LBO時のファイナンスに、将来のアドオン買収に備えて、必要なときに引き出せる追加の借入枠（アクイジション・ファシリティ、DDTL）を組み込む主な利点はどれか。","en":"What is the main advantage of building into LBO financing an extra facility that can be drawn when needed for future add-on acquisitions (an acquisition facility, DDTL)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"借入枠は、利用しなければ費用が一切かからないため、いくらでも大きく設定できる","en":"The facility costs nothing unless used, so it can be set as large as desired"},{"ja":"借入枠があるとアドオンの実施を義務づけられるため、買収のペースを守れる","en":"Having the facility obliges the sponsor to carry out add-ons, which keeps up the pace of acquisitions"},{"ja":"借入枠の利用に貸し手の審査は不要で、条件は後から自由に変更できる","en":"Drawing needs no lender review and the terms can be changed freely later"},{"ja":"案件ごとに資金を探さず、買収の機会に素早く資金を確保できる","en":"There is no need to seek funds deal by deal, so funds are secured quickly when opportunities arise"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"あらかじめ借入枠を合意しておくと、買収の機会が出たときに素早く資金を確保でき、売り手にも資金の確実性を示せる。引出しには条件があり、未使用の枠にもコミットメントフィーがかかる。","en":"Agreeing a facility in advance lets the sponsor secure funds quickly when an opportunity arises and shows sellers funding certainty. Drawing is subject to conditions, and undrawn amounts carry a commitment fee."}},
{"id":"s14x43","dom":"capital","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"LBOのファイナンスで、リボルビング・クレジット・ファシリティ（RCF）が主に担う役割はどれか。","en":"In LBO financing, what role does a revolving credit facility (RCF) mainly play?"},"choices":[{"ja":"買収代金の大部分を、長期の固定した返済計画に基づく分割返済で調達する","en":"Funding most of the purchase price through installments under a fixed long-term repayment schedule"},{"ja":"経営陣に対する報酬の支払いを、繰り延べるための枠を確保する","en":"Reserving a facility to defer payment of management compensation"},{"ja":"運転資金の季節変動や一時的な資金不足を、借入と返済の繰り返しで賄う","en":"Covering seasonal swings in working capital and temporary cash shortages by repeatedly drawing and repaying"},{"ja":"シニアローンの返済を免除し、元本を恒久的に減らす","en":"Waiving repayment of the senior loan and permanently reducing principal"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"RCFは、枠の範囲で借入と返済を繰り返せる借入枠で、運転資金の季節変動や一時的な資金不足に備える。買収代金の主な調達は長期のタームローンが担い、RCFは日々の流動性の備えである。","en":"An RCF is a facility within which funds can be drawn and repaid repeatedly, used for seasonal working capital swings and temporary shortfalls. Long-term term loans fund the bulk of the price, while the RCF is a day-to-day liquidity backstop."}},
{"id":"s14x44","dom":"exit","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"PEがExit時に、買い手側が表明保証保険（W&I保険）を付けることを歓迎する主な利点として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"What is the main advantage for a PE seller at exit in welcoming a buyer-side warranty and indemnity (W&I) insurance policy?"},"choices":[{"ja":"売り手の補償責任を小さくでき、分配後の返還リスクを抑えられる","en":"The seller's indemnity liability can be kept small, limiting the risk of having to return distributions"},{"ja":"保険があれば、売り手は表明保証違反があっても、全く責任を負わなくてよい","en":"With insurance, the seller bears no responsibility at all even for breaches of warranties"},{"ja":"保険料は常に売り手だけが負担し、買い手には費用がかからない","en":"The premium is always borne by the seller alone and costs the buyer nothing"},{"ja":"保険を付けると、売却価格が自動的に引き上げられる","en":"Taking out insurance automatically raises the sale price"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"W&I保険では、表明保証違反の損失を主に保険がカバーするので、売り手の補償責任の上限を小さくできる。ファンドは投資家への分配後に返還を求められるリスクを抑えられる。故意の不正などは通常、保険や免責の対象外である。","en":"Under W&I insurance the policy mainly covers losses from breaches of warranties, so the seller's indemnity cap can be small. The fund limits the risk of being asked to return money after distributing to investors. Deliberate fraud and the like is normally outside cover or exempt."}},
{"id":"s14x45","dom":"exit","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"投資額100億円の2案件のMOICはどちらも2.0倍である。案件Xは5年後に一括200億円、案件Yは3年後に60億円、5年後に140億円を回収する。IRRが高いのはどれか。","en":"Two investments of JPY 10 billion each both have a MOIC of 2.0x. Deal X returns JPY 20 billion in one sum after five years; Deal Y returns JPY 6 billion after three years and JPY 14 billion after five. Which has the higher IRR?"},"choices":[{"ja":"案件X。回収が一度で済み、途中の不確実性が小さく、手続も簡単なため","en":"Deal X, because it is a single return with less interim uncertainty and simpler procedures"},{"ja":"どちらも同じ。MOICが同じなら、IRRも必ず同じになる","en":"They are equal. If MOIC is the same, IRR is always the same"},{"ja":"案件Y。早い時期に一部を回収でき、資金の拘束期間が短いため","en":"Deal Y, because part is recovered earlier and capital is tied up for a shorter time"},{"ja":"比較できない。IRRは回収の時期に影響されないため","en":"They cannot be compared, because IRR is not affected by the timing of recovery"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"IRRは時間を考慮するので、同じMOICでも早く回収できる案件のほうが高い。案件Xは約14.9%、案件Yは約17%になる。途中のリキャップや配当でIRRを高める手法は、この性質を利用している。","en":"IRR accounts for time, so with the same MOIC the deal that returns cash earlier is higher: about 14.9% for X and about 17% for Y. Dividend recaps and interim distributions raise IRR by exploiting this property."}},
{"id":"s14x46","dom":"exit","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"株主間契約のドラッグ・アロング（drag-along）条項の目的として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"What is the purpose of a drag-along clause in a shareholders' agreement?"},"choices":[{"ja":"少数株主が、多数株主の売却に反対してそれを拒否し、会社の売却全体を止められるようにするため","en":"To let minority shareholders oppose and refuse the majority's sale and stop the entire sale of the company"},{"ja":"多数株主の売却時に、少数株主にも同条件での売却を求め、全株取得を望む買い手に応えるため","en":"To require minority holders to sell on the same terms when the majority sells, meeting buyers who want all the shares"},{"ja":"売却の際に、少数株主だけが先に売却して、利益を確定できるようにするため","en":"To let only minority holders sell first and lock in their profit"},{"ja":"経営陣が会社を辞めたときに、株式を会社が低い価格で買い戻せるようにするため","en":"To let the company buy back shares at a low price when management leaves"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"ドラッグ・アロングは、多数株主が売却する際に少数株主にも同じ条件での売却を請求できる権利である。買い手は通常100%の取得を望むので、売却を円滑にする。少数株主に売却を止める力を与えるものではない。","en":"Drag-along gives the majority the right to require minority holders to sell on the same terms. Buyers usually want 100%, so it smooths the sale. It does not give minority holders the power to stop it."}},
{"id":"s14x47","dom":"exit","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"Exitの相手が、別のPEファンド（セカンダリー・バイアウト）である場合の特徴として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate characteristic when the buyer at exit is another PE fund (a secondary buyout)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"買い手は事業を詳しく知らないが、前のファンドが調べ済みなので、デューデリジェンスは不要である","en":"The buyer does not know the business well, but the prior fund has already examined it, so no due diligence is needed"},{"ja":"買い手がPEファンドだと、価格は売り手が一方的に決められ、交渉は行われない","en":"When the buyer is a PE fund, the seller sets the price unilaterally and no negotiation takes place"},{"ja":"買い手が価値向上の余地を見込まないため、価格は常に低くなる","en":"The buyer sees no room to add value, so the price is always low"},{"ja":"買い手は次の価値向上の余地と借入余力で価格を決めるため、成長の道筋を示す必要がある","en":"The buyer prices on the next value creation potential and debt capacity, so the seller must show the growth path"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"セカンダリーの買い手も、自らのリターン目標に向けて次の価値向上の余地と借入余力を見て価格を決める。売り手は、これまでの成果に加え、今後の成長の道筋を示す必要がある。デューデリジェンスは通常どおり行われる。","en":"A secondary buyer also prices on its own return targets, looking at remaining value creation potential and debt capacity. The seller must show a path for future growth in addition to past results. Due diligence proceeds as normal."}},
{"id":"s14x48","dom":"exit","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ファンドの期限が近い優良な投資先を、同じ運用会社が組成する別のファンド（コンティニュエーション・ファンド）に移すGPリード型のセカンダリー取引で、とくに求められる対応はどれか。","en":"In a GP-led secondary where a strong portfolio company is moved from a fund nearing its term to another fund set up by the same manager (a continuation fund), which step is especially required?"},"choices":[{"ja":"利益相反を踏まえ、独立した価格の検証と既存投資家の選択権を確保する","en":"Given the conflict of interest, secure independent price verification and the existing investors' right to choose"},{"ja":"運用会社の判断だけで価格を決め、既存の投資家には取引が済んだ後に結果だけを知らせる","en":"The manager alone sets the price and informs existing investors of the result only after the deal is done"},{"ja":"取引の価格は常に直近の簿価に固定し、第三者の意見を取らない","en":"Always fix the price at the latest book value and take no third-party opinion"},{"ja":"既存の投資家は全員、売却を強制され、継続して保有する選択肢はない","en":"All existing investors are forced to sell, with no option to continue holding"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"運用会社が売り手と買い手の両側に立つため、利益相反の管理が最大の論点になる。独立した価格の検証や競争的な入札、既存投資家が売却か継続かを選べる機会が求められる。事後通知や簿価での固定では、公正性を示せない。","en":"Because the manager sits on both sides, managing the conflict of interest is the key issue. Independent price verification, competitive bidding and a choice for existing investors between selling and rolling are expected. After-the-fact notice or book-value pricing cannot demonstrate fairness."}},
{"id":"s14x49","dom":"exit","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"PEがExit時に、ロックドボックス方式を好む理由として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"Why does a PE seller often prefer a locked box mechanism at exit?"},"choices":[{"ja":"クロージング後に、買い手が数値の誤りを理由に価格を自由に再交渉できるため","en":"Because after closing the buyer can freely renegotiate the price on grounds of numerical errors"},{"ja":"基準日以降の価値の流出を、売り手に対して無制限に認められるため","en":"Because unlimited leakage of value after the reference date is allowed to the seller"},{"ja":"売却価格が、クロージング後の財務数値によって何度も変動するため","en":"Because the sale price fluctuates repeatedly with post-closing financial figures"},{"ja":"価格が固定されて事後の精算がなく、投資家への分配を早く確定できるため","en":"Because the price is fixed with no post-closing true-up, so distributions to investors can be finalized early"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"ファンドは期限内に投資家へ分配して終えたいので、価格が基準日の数字で固定され、クロージング後の精算や再交渉が生じないロックドボックスが好まれる。基準日以降の価値の流出は、通常は契約で禁止される。","en":"Funds want to distribute to investors and wind up within their term, so they favor a locked box in which the price is fixed on reference-date figures and no true-up or renegotiation follows closing. Leakage after the reference date is normally prohibited by the contract."}},
{"id":"s14x50","dom":"exit","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"M&Aで、売却代金の一部を第三者の口座に一定期間預けるエスクローの目的はどれか。","en":"In M&A, what is the purpose of an escrow in which part of the sale proceeds is held in a third party's account for a set period?"},"choices":[{"ja":"売り手が支払うべき税金の納付を、その期間だけ遅らせて猶予を得るため","en":"To postpone the seller's tax payment for that period and gain a grace period"},{"ja":"表明保証違反などによる補償の支払いを確実にするため","en":"To make sure that indemnity payments for breaches of warranties and the like will be paid"},{"ja":"買い手が支払う価格を自動的に引き下げるため","en":"To automatically lower the price the buyer pays"},{"ja":"従業員への退職金を、売却後に免除するため","en":"To exempt severance pay to employees after the sale"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"エスクローは、売却代金の一部を一定期間預けておき、表明保証違反などの補償が必要になったときに、そこから確実に支払えるようにする仕組みである。買い手の補償の確実性が高まり、売り手は期間後に残りを受け取る。","en":"An escrow holds part of the proceeds for a set period so that indemnity for breaches of warranties and the like can be paid from it with certainty. The buyer's indemnity is more secure, and the seller receives the remainder after the period."}}
);
