  _quiz.push(
{"id":"s15x01","dom":"industry","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"SWOT分析で、機会（O）と脅威（T）に分類される要因の特徴はどれか。","en":"In a SWOT analysis, which description fits the factors classified as opportunities (O) and threats (T)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"自社ではコントロールできない外部環境の要因","en":"Factors in the external environment that the company cannot control"},{"ja":"自社が管理でき短期間で改善できる社内の要因","en":"Internal factors that the company manages and can improve in the short term"},{"ja":"競合他社の内部資源のうち公開されていない要因","en":"Undisclosed internal resources held by competitors"},{"ja":"過去の決算に表れた財務指標の実績値そのもの","en":"The actual financial metrics reported in past results"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"機会と脅威は、市場・規制・技術・競合など自社の外にある要因で、自社の裁量では変えられない。自社が管理できる社内の要因は強みと弱みに分類する。財務指標の実績は強み・弱みを裏付ける材料であり、外部要因の分類基準にはならない。","en":"Opportunities and threats are external factors such as markets, regulation, technology and competitors, which the company cannot change at will. Internal factors it can manage are strengths and weaknesses. Past financial metrics support the internal view and do not define external factors."}},
{"id":"s15x02","dom":"industry","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある業界の市場シェアが、甲社40%、乙社30%、丙社20%、丁社10%である。ハーフィンダール・ハーシュマン指数（HHI）はいくつか。","en":"The market shares in an industry are 40%, 30%, 20% and 10% for four firms. What is the Herfindahl-Hirschman Index (HHI)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1,600","en":"1,600"},{"ja":"2,500","en":"2,500"},{"ja":"10,000","en":"10,000"},{"ja":"3,000","en":"3,000"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"HHIは各社の市場シェア（%）を2乗して合計した値で、40の2乗＋30の2乗＋20の2乗＋10の2乗＝1,600＋900＋400＋100＝3,000となる。独占なら10,000、4社が25%ずつなら2,500であり、このケースは均等な場合より集中度が高い。1,600は最大手だけを2乗した値である。","en":"HHI is the sum of squared market shares in percent: 40^2 + 30^2 + 20^2 + 10^2 = 1,600 + 900 + 400 + 100 = 3,000. A monopoly gives 10,000 and four equal firms at 25% give 2,500, so this market is more concentrated than the equal case. 1,600 squares only the largest firm."}},
{"id":"s15x03","dom":"industry","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"部品メーカーX社は売上の60%を完成車メーカー1社に依存し、毎年の値下げ要求を受けている。ファイブフォース分析で最も直接の原因となる力と、その対応策の組合せとして適切なのはどれか。","en":"Parts maker X depends on one automaker for 60% of its sales and faces price-cut demands every year. Which pairing of the force that is most directly responsible and a suitable response is appropriate under Five Forces analysis?"},"choices":[{"ja":"代替品の脅威が高い状態で、主要顧客向けの専用設備を増設して取引関係をいっそう深める","en":"The threat of substitutes is high; deepen the relationship by adding dedicated equipment for the main customer"},{"ja":"売り手の交渉力が強い状態で、原材料の調達先を減らして取引量を1社に集約し、購買力を高める","en":"Supplier power is strong; raise purchasing power by cutting the number of raw-material sources and concentrating volume on one"},{"ja":"買い手の交渉力が強い状態で、顧客の分散と代替のきかない技術の確立によって交渉力を取り戻す","en":"Buyer power is strong; regain bargaining power by diversifying customers and building technology that cannot be substituted"},{"ja":"業界内の競争が激しい状態で、既存の全顧客への販売価格を一律に引き下げて競合に対抗する","en":"Rivalry is intense; match competitors by cutting prices uniformly for every existing customer"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"売上の6割を1社に依存すると、買い手が集中して購入量が大きく、切替えの脅しも使えるため、買い手の交渉力が強まる。対応は顧客の分散と、他社が代替できない技術の確立である。専用設備の増設は依存をさらに深め、一律の値下げは利益を削る。","en":"Depending on one buyer for 60% of sales means a concentrated, high-volume buyer who can credibly threaten to switch, so buyer power is strong. The response is to diversify customers and build technology others cannot substitute. Adding dedicated equipment deepens dependence, and uniform price cuts erode profit."}},
{"id":"s15x04","dom":"industry","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"電力小売の全面自由化（2016年4月）により、新規事業者が家庭向けの小売にも参入できるようになった。ファイブフォースで見て、既存の大手電力会社にとって最も直接に変化した要因はどれか。","en":"Full liberalization of retail electricity in April 2016 let new operators enter household retail. Under Five Forces, which factor changed most directly for the incumbent utilities?"},"choices":[{"ja":"売り手の交渉力（燃料を供給する会社の集中度の上昇）","en":"Supplier power (higher concentration of fuel suppliers)"},{"ja":"新規参入の脅威（法的な参入障壁の低下）","en":"Threat of new entrants (lower legal entry barriers)"},{"ja":"代替品の脅威（家庭用の太陽光発電による自家発電の普及）","en":"Threat of substitutes (spread of household solar self-generation)"},{"ja":"業界内の競争（既存の大手電力会社同士の合併による寡占化）","en":"Industry rivalry (oligopoly through mergers among incumbent utilities)"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"新規事業者が小売に参入できるようになったのは、法的な参入規制が撤廃された結果であり、ファイブフォースでは新規参入の脅威が高まったと整理できる。燃料供給の集中度や自家発電、大手同士の合併は、この制度変更が直接変えた要因ではない。","en":"New operators could enter retail because legal entry restrictions were removed, so the threat of new entrants rose in Five Forces terms. Fuel-supplier concentration, self-generation and mergers among incumbents are not what the regulatory change directly altered."}},
{"id":"s15x05","dom":"industry","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"自社の業界に対する代替品の脅威を評価するとき、最も重視すべき見方はどれか。","en":"When assessing the threat of substitutes to your industry, which view should receive the most weight?"},"choices":[{"ja":"代替品が顧客の同じ課題を、より良い価格性能比と低いスイッチングコストで解決できるか","en":"Whether the substitute solves the same customer problem with better price-performance and lower switching costs"},{"ja":"代替品を製造している企業の数と、それらの企業の売上高の合計がどれだけ大きいかという規模","en":"How many firms make the substitute and how large their combined sales are, as a measure of scale"},{"ja":"代替品が自社製品と同じ名称と同じ形状で、同じ流通経路で販売されているかどうか","en":"Whether the substitute is sold under the same name, in the same form and through the same channels as your product"},{"ja":"代替品の市場で、これまでに既存の同業他社が何社撤退したかという過去の実績の数","en":"How many incumbent rivals have withdrawn from the substitute market in the past"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"代替品の脅威は、形状の類似ではなく、顧客が同じニーズを満たすために乗り換える合理性で決まる。価格性能比が自社より優れ、乗り換えの手間や費用が小さいほど脅威は高い。供給企業の数や売上規模は、乗り換えの起きやすさを直接示さない。","en":"The threat of substitutes depends on whether customers have good reason to switch to meet the same need, not on similar form. The better the price-performance and the lower the switching cost, the greater the threat. The number of suppliers or their sales does not directly show how likely switching is."}},
{"id":"s15x06","dom":"industry","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"買収候補のX社は営業利益率が業界平均の2倍の20%である。ファイブフォースで見ると、買い手の交渉力は上昇傾向にあり、技術の進歩で新規参入も増えている。投資委員会に出す事業計画の立て方として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Target X has an operating margin of 20%, twice the industry average. Under Five Forces, buyer power is rising and technology is attracting more entrants. How should the business plan for the investment committee be built?"},"choices":[{"ja":"過去の20%が今後も続くことを前提に営業利益率を据え置いた計画とし、業界構造の変化はリスクとして割引率にも反映しない","en":"Hold the operating margin at 20% on the assumption the past continues, and do not reflect industry structure changes in the discount rate as risk"},{"ja":"高利益率が構造的な障壁によるものか一時的な要因によるものかを検証し、計画では利益率が業界平均へ近づく可能性を織り込む","en":"Test whether the high margin rests on structural barriers or temporary factors, and build in the possibility that margins converge toward the industry average"},{"ja":"業界平均の2倍は優良企業の証なので、買収価格にさらに高いプレミアムを上乗せして、競合他社の入札を排除する","en":"Since twice the average proves a superior firm, add a higher premium to the price to shut out competing bidders"},{"ja":"ファイブフォースは業界全体の分析なので個別企業の投資判断には使わず、過去の財務諸表の数値だけで企業価値を評価する","en":"Five Forces is an industry-wide tool and is not used for individual investment decisions, so value the firm using past financial statements only"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"超過利益は、参入障壁や顧客との関係など構造的な優位に支えられているときだけ持続する。買い手の力が強まり参入が増えれば、利益率は平均へ回帰しやすいため、計画に織り込むのが妥当である。利益率の据え置きや高いプレミアムの上乗せは、この回帰リスクを無視している。","en":"Excess profit persists only when it rests on structural advantages such as entry barriers or customer ties. With stronger buyers and more entrants, margins tend to revert toward the average, so the plan should allow for that. Holding the margin flat or adding a high premium ignores the reversion risk."}},
{"id":"s15x07","dom":"industry","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ファイブフォース分析の限界として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate limitation of Five Forces analysis?"},"choices":[{"ja":"競合他社の分析に特化しているため、買い手や供給業者などの取引先は分析の対象に含まれていない","en":"It focuses solely on competitor analysis, so trading partners such as buyers and suppliers are not part of the analysis"},{"ja":"業界の収益性を定性的にしか示せないため、売上高や利益率などの数値データを分析に一切利用できない","en":"It can show industry profitability only qualitatively, so numerical data such as sales or margins cannot be used at all"},{"ja":"業界の境界を固定して静的に構造を見るため、技術や規制による境界の変化や補完財の影響を捉えにくい","en":"It takes industry boundaries as fixed and views structure statically, so it struggles to capture shifting boundaries from technology or regulation and the effect of complements"},{"ja":"参入障壁の高さを評価できないため、新規参入が起きる確率を推定することがまったくできない","en":"It cannot evaluate the height of entry barriers, so it cannot estimate at all how likely new entry is"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"5Fは業界を所与の枠として構造を診断するため、デジタル化や規制緩和で業界の境界が動く場面や、補完財が需要を左右する場面を捉えにくい。買い手・供給業者は分析の対象であり、数値データも使える。参入障壁も評価の中核である。","en":"Five Forces diagnoses structure within a given industry frame, so it is weak where digitization or deregulation moves boundaries or where complements drive demand. Buyers and suppliers are part of the analysis, numerical data can be used, and entry barriers are central to it."}},
{"id":"s15x08","dom":"industry","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"シナリオ・プランニングで、将来像を描く軸として最初に選ぶべき要因はどれか。","en":"In scenario planning, which factor should be chosen first as an axis for describing futures?"},"choices":[{"ja":"自社への影響が小さく、かつ今後の動向が最も不確実な要因","en":"A factor with a small impact on the company whose future course is the most uncertain"},{"ja":"自社が自由に決められる社内の方針や組織体制に関する要因","en":"A factor in internal policy or organization that the company can decide freely"},{"ja":"自社への影響が大きく、かつ今後の動向が最も不確実な要因","en":"A factor with a large impact on the company whose future course is the most uncertain"},{"ja":"自社への影響が大きく、かつ今後の動向がほぼ確実に予測できる要因","en":"A factor with a large impact on the company whose future course can be predicted almost with certainty"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"シナリオの軸には、影響が大きく不確実性も大きい要因（クリティカルな不確実性）を選び、軸の組合せで複数の将来像を描く。影響が大きくても予測可能な要因は全シナリオの前提に置き、影響の小さい要因は軸にしない。","en":"Axes should be factors with both large impact and large uncertainty (critical uncertainties), and combinations of the axes yield several futures. Predictable factors, even with large impact, become assumptions common to all scenarios, and low-impact factors are not used as axes."}},
{"id":"s15x09","dom":"positioning","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"STP分析の正しい進め方の順序はどれか。","en":"Which is the correct order of steps in STP analysis?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ポジショニング → セグメンテーション → ターゲティング","en":"Positioning -> Segmentation -> Targeting"},{"ja":"セグメンテーション → ターゲティング → ポジショニング","en":"Segmentation -> Targeting -> Positioning"},{"ja":"ターゲティング → ポジショニング → セグメンテーション","en":"Targeting -> Positioning -> Segmentation"},{"ja":"ポジショニング → ターゲティング → セグメンテーション","en":"Positioning -> Targeting -> Segmentation"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"STPは、市場を細分化し（セグメンテーション）、狙う層を選び（ターゲティング）、その層に対する自社の独自の位置づけを決める（ポジショニング）順に進める。ターゲットを決める前に位置づけを決めると、誰にどんな価値を訴えるかが定まらない。","en":"STP first divides the market (segmentation), then selects the group to pursue (targeting), then decides the firm's distinctive position for that group (positioning). Deciding positioning before the target leaves unclear whom the value proposition addresses."}},
{"id":"s15x10","dom":"positioning","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"経験曲線効果により、累積生産量が2倍になるごとに単位コストが20%低下する製品がある。累積生産量が100万個の時点で単位コストが1,000円のとき、累積生産量が400万個に達した時点の単位コストはいくらか。","en":"A product follows an experience curve in which unit cost falls 20% each time cumulative output doubles. Unit cost is 1,000 yen at 1 million units cumulative. What is unit cost at 4 million units?"},"choices":[{"ja":"800円","en":"800 yen"},{"ja":"600円","en":"600 yen"},{"ja":"400円","en":"400 yen"},{"ja":"640円","en":"640 yen"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"400万個は100万個の4倍で、2回倍増する。1回目で1,000×0.8＝800円、2回目で800×0.8＝640円となる。20%を2回足して40%下がると考える600円は誤りで、低下は複利で効く。800円は倍増を1回しか見ていない。","en":"4 million units is four times 1 million, so output doubles twice. The first doubling gives 1,000 x 0.8 = 800 yen and the second gives 800 x 0.8 = 640 yen. 600 yen wrongly adds two 20% cuts to 40%, but the decline compounds. 800 yen counts only one doubling."}},
{"id":"s15x11","dom":"positioning","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ある製品の価格は1,000円、単位原価は800円、年間販売量は10万個である。差別化投資により単位原価が880円に上がり、価格を1,100円に引き上げられるが、販売量は9万個に減る見込みである。他の費用を無視すると、年間の利益は現状と比べてどうなるか。","en":"A product sells at 1,000 yen with a unit cost of 800 yen and annual volume of 100,000 units. Differentiation investment raises unit cost to 880 yen and lets the price rise to 1,100 yen, but volume is expected to fall to 90,000 units. Ignoring other costs, how does annual profit change?"},"choices":[{"ja":"200万円増加する","en":"It rises by 2 million yen"},{"ja":"20万円減少する","en":"It falls by 200,000 yen"},{"ja":"変わらない","en":"It does not change"},{"ja":"100万円減少する","en":"It falls by 1 million yen"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"現状の利益は(1,000−800)×10万＝2,000万円。差別化後は(1,100−880)×9万＝1,980万円で、20万円減る。単位あたりの利益が20円増えても、販売量の減少がそれを上回る。売上高の減少額100万円で比べるのは、原価の変化を無視した誤りである。","en":"Current profit is (1,000 - 800) x 100,000 = 20 million yen. After differentiation it is (1,100 - 880) x 90,000 = 19.8 million yen, a fall of 200,000 yen. The 20 yen gain per unit is outweighed by lost volume. Comparing the 1 million yen fall in sales ignores the change in cost."}},
{"id":"s15x12","dom":"positioning","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ブルー・オーシャン戦略のERRCグリッドで、『取り除く（Eliminate）』に入れるべき競争要因はどれか。","en":"In the ERRC grid of Blue Ocean Strategy, which competitive factor belongs under Eliminate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"業界がこれまで提供してこなかった、顧客にとって新しい価値を生み出すと期待される要因","en":"A factor the industry has never offered that is expected to create new value for customers"},{"ja":"業界で当たり前とされてきたが、顧客にとっての価値が低く、費用だけがかかっている要因","en":"A factor the industry has taken for granted that adds little customer value yet costs money"},{"ja":"業界標準よりも低い水準にしても、顧客の満足度への影響が小さい要因","en":"A factor that can be set below the industry standard with little effect on customer satisfaction"},{"ja":"顧客が特に重視しており、業界標準を大きく上回る水準まで引き上げて強化すべき要因","en":"A factor customers particularly value that should be raised well above the industry standard"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"ERRCは、除去・削減・増加・創造の4つで価値曲線を描き直す枠組みである。除去は、業界が当然視してきたものの顧客価値が低くコスト負担が大きい要因を対象にする。顧客が重視する要因の強化は増加、新しい価値の追加は創造、標準を下回る水準への引下げは削減に当たる。","en":"ERRC redraws the value curve with four actions: eliminate, reduce, raise and create. Eliminate targets factors the industry takes for granted that add little customer value and carry high cost. Strengthening what customers prize is raise, adding new value is create, and going below the standard is reduce."}},
{"id":"s15x13","dom":"positioning","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ポーターは、業務効率（オペレーショナル・エフェクティブネス）の改善だけでは持続的な競争優位にならないと指摘した。その理由として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Porter argued that improving operational effectiveness alone does not yield sustainable competitive advantage. Which is the most appropriate reason?"},"choices":[{"ja":"業務効率の改善は短期的にしか費用を下げられず、長期的にはかえって単位コストが上昇していく性質があり、費用が増え続けるから","en":"Efficiency gains lower costs only in the short run and by nature keep raising unit cost in the long run, so costs keep growing"},{"ja":"業務効率は顧客満足度に影響しないため、改善しても売上高にも利益率にもまったく反映されないから","en":"Operational efficiency does not affect customer satisfaction, so improving it never shows up in sales or margins"},{"ja":"業務効率の追求は規模の経済を損なうため、市場シェアが拡大するほど平均コストが高くなってしまうから","en":"Pursuing efficiency undermines economies of scale, so average cost rises as market share grows"},{"ja":"ベストプラクティスは競合にも模倣されやすく、各社が同じ方向へ収斂して差別化が失われ、利益が圧迫されるから","en":"Best practices are easily copied by rivals, so firms converge in the same direction, differentiation is lost and profits are squeezed"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"同じ活動をより上手に行う業務効率は、ベンチマーキングなどで競合も追随でき、各社の手法が似通って収斂する。その結果、利益は生産性の限界を競う消耗戦で削られる。持続的優位には、異なる活動の選択か、活動の独自の組合せが要る。","en":"Doing the same activities better can be matched through benchmarking, so rivals' methods converge. Profit is then eroded in a contest over the productivity frontier. Lasting advantage requires choosing different activities or combining them in a distinctive way."}},
{"id":"s15x14","dom":"positioning","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"特定のニッチ市場に経営資源を集中する戦略を採る企業に特有のリスクとして、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate risk specific to a firm that concentrates its resources on a niche market?"},"choices":[{"ja":"狙ったセグメントの需要が縮小するか、大手が細分化して参入し、集中による優位が崩れること","en":"The targeted segment's demand shrinks, or large firms enter with segment-specific offerings, and the advantage from focus collapses"},{"ja":"対象とする顧客が多すぎて個別ニーズへの対応が間に合わず、サービスの品質が下がってしまうこと","en":"There are too many target customers to serve individual needs in time, so service quality drops"},{"ja":"経営資源を分散しすぎるため、どのセグメントでも中途半端な地位になり、規模の経済が働かないこと","en":"Resources are spread too thin, leaving a half-hearted position in every segment where economies of scale do not work"},{"ja":"市場の範囲が広すぎるため、業界全体の価格競争に巻き込まれ、価格プレミアムを維持できなくなること","en":"The market scope is so wide that the firm is drawn into industry-wide price competition and cannot hold a price premium"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"集中戦略は狭い市場で深く優位を築く分、そのセグメントが縮む、または大手が専用製品で攻めてくると依存が裏目に出る。資源の分散や顧客の多さ、広い市場の価格競争は、集中ではなく広範囲に展開する戦略で生じやすい問題である。","en":"A focus strategy builds deep advantage in a narrow market, so dependence backfires if the segment shrinks or large firms attack with dedicated products. Spread-thin resources, too many customers and wide-market price wars are problems of broad strategies, not focus."}},
{"id":"s15x15","dom":"positioning","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ある製品の価格は1,000円、単位変動費は400円、年間固定費は3億円である。競合に対抗して価格を10%下げて900円にする場合、損益分岐点の販売数量は現状に比べて何%増えるか（変動費と固定費は変わらないものとする）。","en":"A product is priced at 1,000 yen with a unit variable cost of 400 yen and annual fixed costs of 300 million yen. If the price is cut 10% to 900 yen to counter a rival, by what percentage does the break-even volume rise from today (variable and fixed costs unchanged)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50%","en":"50%"},{"ja":"25%","en":"25%"},{"ja":"20%","en":"20%"},{"ja":"10%","en":"10%"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"現状の損益分岐点は3億円÷(1,000−400)円＝50万個。値下げ後は3億円÷(900−400)円＝60万個で、20%増える。価格を10%下げても、単位あたりの限界利益は600円から500円へ約17%減るため、必要な販売数量は価格の下げ幅より大きく増える。","en":"Current break-even is 300 million yen / (1,000 - 400) yen = 500,000 units. After the cut it is 300 million / (900 - 400) = 600,000 units, up 20%. A 10% price cut reduces the unit contribution from 600 to 500 yen, about 17%, so required volume rises by more than the price cut."}},
{"id":"s15x16","dom":"resource","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある資源が、価値があり（V）、希少で（R）、模倣が困難（I）である一方、それを活用するための組織体制（O）が整っていない。VRIOの考え方で、この資源の評価として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"A resource is valuable (V), rare (R) and costly to imitate (I), but the organization (O) needed to exploit it is not in place. Under VRIO, which is the most appropriate evaluation of this resource?"},"choices":[{"ja":"価値と希少性だけを満たす資源と同じく、一時的な競争優位にとどまる","en":"As with a resource meeting only value and rarity, it yields merely a temporary advantage"},{"ja":"V・R・Iを満たすため、組織の状況にかかわらず持続的な競争優位がすでに実現している","en":"Because it meets V, R and I, a sustained competitive advantage is already realized regardless of the organization"},{"ja":"競争優位の潜在力はあるが、組織が整うまでは十分に活用されない未活用の競争優位である","en":"It has potential for advantage but is an unexploited advantage until the organization is ready"},{"ja":"組織を欠くので、価値も希少性も模倣困難性も認められず、経営資源とはいえない","en":"Without the organization, value, rarity and inimitability are not recognized and it is not a resource"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"V・R・Iを満たす資源は優位の源泉になりうるが、活かす組織（O）がなければ収益に結びつかない。そのため未活用の競争優位と評価し、組織設計や評価制度を整えて活用を促す。組織の有無にかかわらず優位が実現済みとみなすのは誤りである。","en":"A resource meeting V, R and I can be a source of advantage, but without the organization (O) to exploit it, it does not translate into returns. It is therefore an unexploited advantage, and organization design and incentives should be built. Treating the advantage as already realized ignores this."}},
{"id":"s15x17","dom":"resource","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"VRIOで、価値はあるが希少性がない資源がもたらす競争上の結果はどれか。","en":"In VRIO, what competitive outcome does a resource that is valuable but not rare produce?"},"choices":[{"ja":"競合と同等の水準にとどまる競争均衡","en":"Competitive parity, staying at the same level as rivals"},{"ja":"競合に対する競争劣位に陥ってしまう","en":"The firm falls into a competitive disadvantage against rivals"},{"ja":"競合に対する一時的な競争優位が生まれる","en":"A temporary competitive advantage over rivals arises"},{"ja":"競合に対する持続的な競争優位が生まれる","en":"A sustained competitive advantage over rivals arises"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"価値があっても多くの競合が持っている資源は、持つこと自体が優位にならず、生き残りのための必須条件にとどまる。希少で初めて一時的な優位が生まれ、模倣困難で持続的な優位になる。価値がなければ競争劣位となる。","en":"A valuable resource that many rivals also hold gives no edge by itself and is merely a condition for survival. Rarity creates a temporary advantage and inimitability makes it sustained. A resource without value leads to competitive disadvantage."}},
{"id":"s15x18","dom":"resource","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ソフトウェア企業の買収で、対象会社の価値の大半が少数の創業エンジニアの暗黙知にある。買収後の統合（PMI）で最優先すべき施策はどれか。","en":"In acquiring a software company, most of the target's value lies in the tacit knowledge of a few founding engineers. Which post-merger integration (PMI) measure should have top priority?"},"choices":[{"ja":"重複する開発拠点を直ちに閉鎖して統合し、買収によるコスト削減額を早期に実現する","en":"Immediately close and merge overlapping development sites to realize the acquisition's cost savings early"},{"ja":"買収完了後すぐに本社の人事制度へ全員を移行させ、報酬体系を買い手の水準へ一本化して不公平をなくす","en":"Move everyone to the parent's HR system right after closing and unify pay to the buyer's levels to remove unfairness"},{"ja":"キーパーソンの残留を、報酬の繰延べや業績連動の対価（アーンアウト）などの仕組みで確保する","en":"Secure the key people's retention through mechanisms such as deferred pay or performance-linked consideration (earn-out)"},{"ja":"対象会社の開発手順を早期に買い手の標準へ統一し、属人的な暗黙知を速やかに排除する","en":"Quickly unify the target's development process to the buyer's standard and promptly eliminate person-dependent tacit knowledge"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"価値が人に宿る買収では、キーパーソンの流出が価値の毀損に直結する。繰延報酬、残留ボーナス、アーンアウトなどで残留を確保するのが先決である。開発手順の統一や拠点閉鎖、人事制度の一本化を急ぐと、暗黙知の担い手が離れて買収の目的を損なう。","en":"When value resides in people, losing key people directly destroys value, so securing retention through deferred pay, retention bonuses or an earn-out comes first. Rushing to unify processes, close sites or standardize HR can drive away the holders of tacit knowledge and defeat the deal's purpose."}},
{"id":"s15x19","dom":"resource","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"プラハラードとハメルが示したコア・コンピタンスの条件として、含まれないものはどれか。","en":"Which of the following is NOT among the conditions for a core competence set out by Prahalad and Hamel?"},"choices":[{"ja":"会計上の資産として貸借対照表に計上できること","en":"It can be recorded as an asset on the balance sheet under accounting rules"},{"ja":"特定の製品に限られず、多様な製品や市場へ展開できる拡張性があること","en":"It is not limited to one product and can extend to diverse products and markets"},{"ja":"最終製品が顧客に認識される価値へ大きく貢献すること","en":"It contributes substantially to the value customers perceive in the end product"},{"ja":"競合他社が容易には模倣できない、独自性の高い能力であること","en":"It is a distinctive capability that competitors cannot easily imitate"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"コア・コンピタンスの条件は、顧客価値への貢献、競合との差別性（模倣困難）、多様な市場への展開可能性である。ノウハウや技術の組合せのような無形の能力が中心で、貸借対照表に資産として計上できるかどうかは条件に含まれない。","en":"The conditions are contribution to customer value, differentiation from competitors (hard to imitate) and extendability to diverse markets. Core competences are mainly intangible capabilities such as know-how and technology combinations, and whether they can be booked as a balance-sheet asset is not a condition."}},
{"id":"s15x20","dom":"resource","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"ポーターのバリューチェーンで、主活動ではなく支援活動に分類されるものはどれか。","en":"In Porter's value chain, which activity is classified as a support activity rather than a primary activity?"},"choices":[{"ja":"販売・マーケティング（広告や営業に関する活動）","en":"Marketing and sales (activities for advertising and selling)"},{"ja":"技術開発（研究開発や工程改善に関する活動）","en":"Technology development (activities for R&D and process improvement)"},{"ja":"製造オペレーション（原材料の加工や組立に関する活動）","en":"Operations (activities for processing materials and assembly)"},{"ja":"出荷物流（完成品の保管や配送に関する活動）","en":"Outbound logistics (activities for storing and delivering finished goods)"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"主活動は購買物流、製造、出荷物流、販売・マーケティング、サービスの5つである。支援活動は調達、技術開発、人事・労務管理、全般管理で、主活動を横断して支える。出荷物流・製造・販売・マーケティングは、いずれも製品の流れに直接関わる主活動である。","en":"The primary activities are inbound logistics, operations, outbound logistics, marketing and sales, and service. Support activities are procurement, technology development, human resource management and firm infrastructure, which cut across the primary ones. Outbound logistics, operations and marketing and sales are primary activities tied to the product flow."}},
{"id":"s15x21","dom":"resource","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"設計をコア資源とするメーカーが、製造を外部へ全面委託して設計に集中する計画を立てた。ただし、同社の設計改善は製造現場で得た不具合や歩留まりの知見に大きく依存している。最も警戒すべきリスクはどれか。","en":"A manufacturer whose core resource is design plans to outsource all production and focus on design. Its design improvements, however, depend heavily on defect and yield knowledge gained on the shop floor. Which risk deserves the most caution?"},"choices":[{"ja":"製造現場との相互作用を失い、設計の改善に必要なノウハウが蓄積されず、設計力そのものが空洞化すること","en":"Losing interaction with the shop floor, so the know-how needed to improve designs stops accumulating and design capability itself is hollowed out"},{"ja":"製造を委託すると製品の品質基準を自社で決められなくなり、品質基準の設定権限が完全に失われてしまうこと","en":"Outsourcing means the firm can no longer set its own quality standards, and the authority to set them is lost completely"},{"ja":"委託により固定費が増えて損益分岐点が上がり、需要が落ち込んだときの利益の変動が大きくなること","en":"Outsourcing increases fixed costs and raises the break-even point, making profit swing more when demand falls"},{"ja":"委託先に支払う加工費が、自社で製造する場合の変動費を常に上回り、粗利率が必ず低下してしまうこと","en":"The processing fee paid to the contractor always exceeds the variable cost of in-house production, so gross margin necessarily declines"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"設計と製造の知見が相互に影響し合う場合、製造を手放すと学習の機会が失われ、コア資源である設計力が劣化する。委託は通常、固定費を変動費に置き換えるので、損益分岐点が上がるとは限らない。品質基準は契約で定められ、加工費が常に上回るとも限らない。","en":"When design and production knowledge feed each other, giving up production removes learning opportunities and erodes the core design capability. Outsourcing normally converts fixed costs into variable ones, so break-even need not rise. Quality standards are set by contract, and processing fees do not always exceed in-house costs."}},
{"id":"s15x22","dom":"resource","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ティースのダイナミック・ケイパビリティは、感知（sensing）・捕捉（seizing）・変容（transforming）の3つから成る。このうち『捕捉』に当たる行動はどれか。","en":"Teece's dynamic capabilities consist of sensing, seizing and transforming. Which action corresponds to seizing?"},"choices":[{"ja":"顧客や技術の変化を継続的に観察し、脅威や機会の兆候を早期に見つけて組織内の関係者へ速やかに共有する","en":"Continuously observing changes in customers and technology, spotting early signs of threats and opportunities and promptly sharing them with relevant people in the organization"},{"ja":"把握した機会に対して投資を決断し、必要な資源を動員して新しい事業やビジネスモデルを立ち上げる","en":"Deciding to invest in an identified opportunity and mobilizing the needed resources to launch a new business or business model"},{"ja":"競合他社の業績と戦略を定期的に分析し、自社のポジションを指標の数値で評価する","en":"Regularly analyzing rivals' results and strategies and evaluating the firm's position with numerical indicators"},{"ja":"既存の組織構造や資産の組合せを継続的に見直し、事業の再編や資源の再配置を実行する","en":"Continuously reviewing the organization and the mix of assets, and carrying out business restructuring and resource reallocation"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"感知は変化の兆候を見つけること、捕捉は見つけた機会に投資を決め資源を動員して形にすること、変容は組織や資産を組み替えて維持・刷新することを指す。観察や情報共有は感知、再編や再配置は変容に当たる。","en":"Sensing is spotting signs of change, seizing is deciding to invest in an identified opportunity and mobilizing resources to realize it, and transforming is recombining the organization and assets to sustain and renew the firm. Observation and information sharing are sensing, and restructuring and reallocation are transforming."}},
{"id":"s15x23","dom":"growth","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"既存顧客に対して、既存の製品に新しい保守サービスを追加して販売する戦略は、アンゾフの成長マトリクスのどれに当たるか。","en":"Selling a new maintenance service in addition to an existing product to existing customers falls under which cell of Ansoff's growth matrix?"},"choices":[{"ja":"多角化戦略","en":"Diversification strategy"},{"ja":"市場開拓戦略","en":"Market development strategy"},{"ja":"市場浸透戦略","en":"Market penetration strategy"},{"ja":"新製品開発","en":"New product development strategy"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"アンゾフのマトリクスは、既存市場×既存製品が市場浸透、既存市場×新製品が新製品開発、新市場×既存製品が市場開拓、新市場×新製品が多角化である。既存顧客へ新しいサービスを加えるのは、既存市場に新製品を投入する新製品開発である。","en":"In Ansoff's matrix, existing market and existing product is market penetration, existing market and new product is new product development, new market and existing product is market development, and new market and new product is diversification. Adding a new service for existing customers is new product development."}},
{"id":"s15x24","dom":"growth","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"あるサブスクリプション事業の月額料金は5,000円、粗利率は60%、月次の解約率は5%（平均継続期間は20か月）、顧客獲得コスト（CAC）は1人あたり3万円である。粗利ベースの顧客生涯価値（LTV）とLTV/CACの組合せとして正しいのはどれか。","en":"A subscription business charges 5,000 yen a month with a 60% gross margin, 5% monthly churn (average lifetime 20 months) and a customer acquisition cost (CAC) of 30,000 yen per customer. Which pair of gross-margin-based customer lifetime value (LTV) and LTV/CAC is correct?"},"choices":[{"ja":"LTVは6万円、LTV/CACは2.0倍","en":"LTV is 60,000 yen and LTV/CAC is 2.0x"},{"ja":"LTVは10万円、LTV/CACは3.3倍","en":"LTV is 100,000 yen and LTV/CAC is 3.3x"},{"ja":"LTVは12万円、LTV/CACは4.0倍","en":"LTV is 120,000 yen and LTV/CAC is 4.0x"},{"ja":"LTVは3万円、LTV/CACは1.0倍","en":"LTV is 30,000 yen and LTV/CAC is 1.0x"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"粗利ベースのLTVは、月額5,000円×粗利率60%＝3,000円を解約率5%で割った6万円（3,000円×平均20か月）である。CAC3万円に対するLTV/CACは2.0倍となる。売上ベースで10万円とする計算は、粗利を無視した誤りである。","en":"Gross-margin LTV is 5,000 yen x 60% = 3,000 yen a month divided by the 5% churn rate, or 60,000 yen (3,000 yen x 20 months). Against a CAC of 30,000 yen, LTV/CAC is 2.0x. The 100,000 yen figure is revenue-based and ignores gross margin."}},
{"id":"s15x25","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"国内メーカーのY社は、海外の新市場で現地の流通網を3年以内に使えるようにしたい。自社で構築すると5年かかり、現地大手の買収は規模が大きすぎて難しい。両社の強みは補完的で、現地大手も日本製品の取扱い拡大に前向きである。最も整合的な選択はどれか。","en":"Domestic manufacturer Y wants access to local distribution in a new overseas market within three years. Building its own would take five years, and acquiring the local leader is too large. The two firms' strengths are complementary and the local leader is keen to expand Japanese products. Which choice is most consistent?"},"choices":[{"ja":"買収の規模を問わず、借入を最大限に使って現地大手を完全子会社にして一気に流通網を得る","en":"Make the local leader a wholly owned subsidiary using maximum borrowing regardless of deal size to gain the network at once"},{"ja":"現地大手との合弁事業や販売提携によって、流通網へ早期にアクセスする","en":"Gain early access to the distribution network through a joint venture or sales alliance with the local leader"},{"ja":"自社単独で5年かけて現地の流通網を構築し、完成するまで当該市場への参入を見送る","en":"Build the distribution network alone over five years and defer entering the market until it is finished"},{"ja":"現地の流通網は使わず、日本からの輸出のみで当面の売上を確保して様子を見る","en":"Do not use local distribution and secure near-term sales through exports from Japan alone while watching how things develop"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"時間の制約があり、自社構築は遅く、買収は規模が過大という条件では、補完関係にある相手との合弁や販売提携が、資本負担を抑えつつ早期に流通網へ到達できる選択となる。単独構築では期限に間に合わず、無理な借入での買収は財務リスクが大きい。","en":"With a time limit, a slow build-out and an oversized acquisition, a joint venture or alliance with a complementary partner reaches distribution early while limiting capital. Building alone misses the deadline, and a debt-fueled acquisition carries heavy financial risk."}},
{"id":"s15x26","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"経営企画が『3つのホライズン』で事業を整理するとき、H3（ホライズン3）に当たるものはどれか。","en":"When corporate planning organizes businesses with the Three Horizons model, which corresponds to Horizon 3 (H3)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"現在の収益の大半を生み、効率化と市場での防衛によって収益性の最大化を図る既存の中核事業","en":"The existing core business that generates most current revenue and aims to maximize profitability through efficiency and defense of its market"},{"ja":"市場の縮小が進み、投資を抑えて撤退の時期を探っている衰退事業","en":"A declining business in a shrinking market where investment is held back and the timing of exit is being explored"},{"ja":"既に立ち上がっており、今後数年で規模の拡大が見込まれる成長事業","en":"A growth business that has already launched and is expected to scale up over the next few years"},{"ja":"現時点では収益にほとんど貢献しないが、将来の成長の選択肢として育てる新規事業の芽","en":"Seeds of new businesses that contribute little revenue now but are nurtured as options for future growth"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"3つのホライズンは、H1が現在の中核事業、H2が数年内に拡大する成長事業、H3が将来の選択肢となる新規事業の種である。H3は収益化に時間がかかるため、H1と同じ指標で短期の成果を求めず、選択肢としての価値を評価する。","en":"In the Three Horizons, H1 is the current core business, H2 is growth businesses that scale within a few years, and H3 is seeds of new businesses that serve as future options. H3 takes time to monetize, so it is judged on option value rather than the short-term metrics used for H1."}},
{"id":"s15x27","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"新サービスの市場規模を整理したところ、TAMは1,000億円、自社の提供範囲で到達できるSAMは300億円であった。3年後に現実的に獲得できるシェアをSAMの10%と見るとき、SOM（獲得可能市場）はいくらか。","en":"Sizing a new service gives a TAM of 100 billion yen and a SAM, reachable with the firm's offering, of 30 billion yen. If realistic share after three years is 10% of SAM, what is the SOM (serviceable obtainable market)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"3億円","en":"300 million yen"},{"ja":"300億円","en":"30 billion yen"},{"ja":"30億円","en":"3 billion yen"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"10 billion yen"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"SOMは、SAMのうち自社が現実に獲得できる売上規模で、300億円×10%＝30億円となる。TAMの10%である100億円や、SAM全体の300億円は、獲得を前提にした過大な見積りである。","en":"SOM is the revenue the firm can realistically win within the SAM: 30 billion yen x 10% = 3 billion yen. 10 billion yen (10% of TAM) and the full 30 billion yen SAM are overstated estimates that assume capture."}},
{"id":"s15x28","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"海外進出先の選定にCAGEフレームワーク（ゲマワット）を使う。このうちA（Administrative）が表すものはどれか。","en":"Ghemawat's CAGE framework is used to choose an overseas target. What does the A (Administrative) dimension represent?"},"choices":[{"ja":"法制度、政治体制、旧宗主国との関係、貿易協定などの制度的・政治的な違い","en":"Institutional and political differences such as legal systems, political regimes, colonial ties and trade agreements"},{"ja":"所得水準、天然資源、労働力の質、資本市場、情報の入手しやすさなどの経済的な違い","en":"Economic differences such as income levels, natural resources, labor quality, capital markets and availability of information"},{"ja":"言語、宗教、価値観、社会規範などの文化的な違い","en":"Cultural differences such as language, religion, values and social norms"},{"ja":"国土の距離、時差、気候、輸送インフラなどの地理的な違い","en":"Geographic differences such as physical distance, time zones, climate and transport infrastructure"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"CAGEは、国と国との距離を文化（Cultural）、制度（Administrative）、地理（Geographic）、経済（Economic）の4つで測る。制度的な距離は、法規制、政治、貿易協定、植民地時代の関係などの違いを指す。言語や価値観は文化、時差や気候は地理、所得水準は経済に属する。","en":"CAGE measures distance between countries along four dimensions: Cultural, Administrative, Geographic and Economic. Administrative distance covers differences in laws, politics, trade agreements and colonial ties. Language and values are cultural, time zones and climate are geographic, and income levels are economic."}},
{"id":"s15x29","dom":"growth","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"新製品の年間売上高は10億円で、粗利率は40%である。このうち4億円は既存製品の売上からの置換え（カニバリゼーション）で、既存製品の粗利率は30%である。他の費用を無視すると、新製品の投入による年間の粗利の純増額はいくらか。","en":"A new product has annual sales of 1 billion yen at a 40% gross margin. Of that, 400 million yen is cannibalization of an existing product with a 30% gross margin. Ignoring other costs, what is the net annual increase in gross profit from launching the new product?"},"choices":[{"ja":"2.4億円","en":"240 million yen"},{"ja":"4.0億円","en":"400 million yen"},{"ja":"2.8億円","en":"280 million yen"},{"ja":"1.2億円","en":"120 million yen"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"新製品の粗利は10億円×40%＝4億円。置換えで失う既存製品の粗利は4億円×30%＝1.2億円で、純増は4−1.2＝2.8億円である。4億円は置換えを無視した値で、2.4億円は純増売上6億円に新製品の粗利率だけを掛けた値であり、失う粗利を見落としている。","en":"The new product's gross profit is 1 billion yen x 40% = 400 million yen. The lost gross profit on cannibalized sales is 400 million x 30% = 120 million, so the net gain is 400 - 120 = 280 million yen. 400 million ignores cannibalization, and 240 million applies the new margin to net new sales of 600 million, overlooking the profit lost."}},
{"id":"s15x30","dom":"corporate","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"BCGのプロダクト・ポートフォリオ・マネジメント（PPM）で『花形（スター）』に当たる事業の特徴はどれか。","en":"In BCG's product portfolio management (PPM) matrix, which is a characteristic of a business classified as a star?"},"choices":[{"ja":"市場成長率が高く、相対市場シェアが低い事業で、投資の成否が見通しにくい","en":"High market growth and low relative market share, where the outcome of investment is hard to foresee"},{"ja":"市場成長率が低く、相対市場シェアが高い事業で、投資を抑えても資金を生み出す","en":"Low market growth and high relative market share, generating cash even with restrained investment"},{"ja":"市場成長率が高く、相対市場シェアも高い事業で、地位の維持に多くの投資資金を要する","en":"High market growth and high relative market share, requiring heavy investment to keep its position"},{"ja":"市場成長率が低く、相対市場シェアも低い事業で、資金の流入も少ないため撤退を検討する","en":"Low market growth and low relative market share, with little cash inflow, so exit is considered"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"花形は、市場成長率と相対市場シェアがともに高い事業である。成長市場での地位を守るため多くの投資資金が要り、現金の創出と投資が拮抗しやすい。市場成長率が低下してシェアが維持されれば、金のなる木へ移る。他の区分の特徴を述べた記述は当てはまらない。","en":"A star has both high market growth and high relative share. It needs heavy investment to defend its position in a growing market, so cash generation and investment tend to offset each other. If growth slows and share holds, it becomes a cash cow. The other descriptions fit different quadrants."}},
{"id":"s15x31","dom":"corporate","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある事業の市場シェアは12%、市場最大の競合のシェアは30%、市場成長率は3%である。PPMの区分（成長率の高低の境を10%、相対シェアの境を1.0とする）と標準的な方針の組合せとして適切なのはどれか。","en":"A business has a 12% market share, the largest rival has 30% and market growth is 3%. Using PPM with a growth threshold of 10% and a relative share threshold of 1.0, which pairing of classification and standard policy is appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"相対市場シェア0.4の問題児で、積極的に追加の投資をしてスターへの育成を図る","en":"A question mark with relative share of 0.4; invest actively to grow it into a star"},{"ja":"相対市場シェア0.4の負け犬で、改善の見込みが乏しければ撤退や売却を検討する","en":"A dog with relative share of 0.4; if improvement prospects are poor, consider exit or sale"},{"ja":"相対市場シェア2.5の金のなる木で、成長投資を抑えて得た資金を他事業へ回す","en":"A cash cow with relative share of 2.5; restrain growth investment and redirect cash to other businesses"},{"ja":"相対市場シェア0.4の花形で、現在の地位を守るために継続的な投資を行う","en":"A star with relative share of 0.4; keep investing to protect its present position"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"相対市場シェアは自社シェア÷最大競合シェアで、12÷30＝0.4となる。シェアが1.0未満かつ成長率が低い事業は負け犬に区分され、資金の流入が乏しいため、立て直しの見込みがなければ撤退や売却を検討する。2.5は分子と分母を逆にした誤りである。","en":"Relative market share is own share divided by the largest rival's share: 12 / 30 = 0.4. A business with share below 1.0 and low growth is a dog; with scant cash inflow, exit or sale is considered unless a turnaround is plausible. 2.5 inverts numerator and denominator."}},
{"id":"s15x32","dom":"corporate","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"全社の資本コスト（WACC）が7%の企業で、事業別のROICが事業X 12%、事業Y 5%、事業Z 8%であった。他の事情が同じとき、資本効率の観点から最優先で改善または売却を検討すべき事業はどれか。","en":"A company with a group WACC of 7% has business ROICs of 12% for X, 5% for Y and 8% for Z. All else equal, which business should be considered first for improvement or sale from a capital efficiency standpoint?"},"choices":[{"ja":"事業X・Y・Zのすべてを、一律に同じ比率で縮小する","en":"Shrink businesses X, Y and Z uniformly by the same proportion"},{"ja":"事業Y（ROICがWACCを下回り、価値を毀損している）","en":"Business Y (ROIC is below WACC, so it destroys value)"},{"ja":"事業Z（ROICはWACCを上回っているが、事業Xよりは低いため）","en":"Business Z (its ROIC exceeds WACC but is lower than business X)"},{"ja":"事業X（ROICが最も高く、成長のための投資負担が重いため）","en":"Business X (it has the highest ROIC, so its growth investment burden is heavy)"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"ROICが資本コストを下回る事業は、投下した資本に対して要求リターンを稼げず、企業価値を毀損する。事業Yは5%で7%を下回るため、改善か売却を優先して検討する。事業Zは8%で資本コストを上回り、事業Xはさらに高い。一律縮小は価値創造事業まで削る。","en":"A business whose ROIC is below the cost of capital fails to earn the required return and destroys value. Y at 5% is below 7%, so improvement or sale comes first. Z at 8% exceeds the cost of capital and X is higher still. Uniform shrinkage would cut value-creating businesses too."}},
{"id":"s15x33","dom":"corporate","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"A社のB事業は、自社で保有し続けた場合の価値（DCF）が400億円と見積られる。ある事業会社が、自社の販路と組み合わせることでより多くの収益を見込み、450億円で買収したいと申し出た。税や取引費用を無視した場合、ベストオーナーの考え方に最も沿った判断はどれか。","en":"Company A values its business B at 40 billion yen on a hold-and-run (DCF) basis. A trading company expects higher earnings by combining B with its sales channels and offers 45 billion yen. Ignoring taxes and transaction costs, which decision best fits the best-owner principle?"},"choices":[{"ja":"事業の価値は誰が保有しても同じなので、売却価額と保有価値の差は考慮せずに事業規模の拡大を優先する","en":"Value is the same whoever owns the business, so ignore the gap between price and holding value and prioritize scale"},{"ja":"過去の投資額が回収済みか否かを確認し、未回収であれば売却額にかかわらず保有を続ける","en":"Check whether past investment has been recovered and, if not, keep the business regardless of the sale price"},{"ja":"売却価額が保有価値を上回っても、本業の規模縮小を避けるために売却を見送る","en":"Even though the price exceeds the holding value, decline to sell to avoid shrinking the core business scale"},{"ja":"買い手の方が事業の価値を高く引き出せるので、売却して50億円分の価値を実現する","en":"The buyer can extract more value from the business, so sell and realize 5 billion yen of value"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"ベストオーナーの考え方では、事業の価値は所有者によって変わり、最も高く引き出せる者が持つのが望ましい。保有価値400億円に対し450億円の提示があるなら、売却で50億円分の価値を株主に実現できる。投資の未回収分は埋没費用であり、判断に使わない。","en":"Under the best-owner principle, a business is worth different amounts to different owners and should be held by whoever can extract the most. With a holding value of 40 billion yen and an offer of 45 billion yen, a sale realizes 5 billion yen for shareholders. Unrecovered past investment is a sunk cost and is not used."}},
{"id":"s15x34","dom":"corporate","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"買収候補の時価総額は800億円で、買収価格は1,000億円（プレミアム200億円）である。買収により実現するコストシナジーの現在価値は、確度の高いものだけで150億円と見積られた。シナジーが見積どおりに実現した場合、買収者の株主にとっての価値の増減はいくらか。","en":"The target's market capitalization is 80 billion yen and the acquisition price is 100 billion yen (a premium of 20 billion). The present value of high-confidence cost synergies is estimated at 15 billion yen. If synergies materialize as estimated, what is the change in value for the acquirer's shareholders?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50億円の価値創造","en":"5 billion yen of value created"},{"ja":"50億円の価値毀損","en":"5 billion yen of value destroyed"},{"ja":"150億円の価値創造","en":"15 billion yen of value created"},{"ja":"200億円の価値毀損","en":"20 billion yen of value destroyed"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"買い手の価値増減は、シナジーの現在価値からプレミアムを引いた額で、150−200＝−50億円となる。シナジー全額が買い手の取り分になるわけではなく、プレミアムとして売り手に支払う分が差し引かれる。プレミアムはシナジーの現在価値を超えて払うべきでない。","en":"The change for the buyer is the present value of synergies minus the premium: 15 - 20 = -5 billion yen. Synergies do not all accrue to the buyer, since the premium paid to the seller is deducted. A buyer should not pay a premium above the present value of synergies."}},
{"id":"s15x35","dom":"corporate","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"取引コスト理論の観点で、特定の取引相手にしか価値を持たない専用設備への投資（高い資産特殊性）を伴う基幹部品の調達について、最も適切な推論はどれか。","en":"From the standpoint of transaction cost theory, which is the most appropriate inference for sourcing a key component that requires investment in equipment valuable only to one trading partner (high asset specificity)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"専用設備は他社に転用できないので、都度の市場取引で最安値の供給元を選ぶ方が、取引コストが小さくなって有利になる","en":"Dedicated equipment cannot be redeployed, so choosing the cheapest supplier in spot market transactions keeps transaction costs lower and is more advantageous"},{"ja":"専用設備への投資額は回収できない埋没費用なので調達方法の選択に影響せず、価格だけで決めるべきである","en":"The dedicated investment is an unrecoverable sunk cost that does not affect the sourcing choice, so decide on price alone"},{"ja":"取引後に相手が条件を迫るホールドアップのリスクが大きいため、長期契約や垂直統合による内部化が有利になる","en":"The risk of hold-up, where the partner presses for better terms after the investment, is large, so long-term contracts or internalization through vertical integration become advantageous"},{"ja":"資産特殊性が高いほど取引相手の候補が増えるため、価格競争が働いて調達コストが下がっていく","en":"The higher the asset specificity, the more potential partners there are, so price competition drives procurement costs down"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"専用設備に投資した後は他に売れず、相手が価格を吊り上げても応じざるを得ないホールドアップが起きやすい。そのため長期契約、相互持合い、垂直統合で関係を固定し、リスクを減らすのが有利になる。都度取引は、この脆弱性を放置する。","en":"After investing in dedicated equipment that cannot be sold elsewhere, a firm is prone to hold-up and must accept a partner's price increases. Long-term contracts, cross-holdings or vertical integration that lock in the relationship reduce the risk. Spot transactions leave this vulnerability unaddressed."}},
{"id":"s15x36","dom":"corporate","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"複数事業を持つ企業を、事業別の評価額を合計して評価する（SOTP）。事業XはEBITDA100億円に同業の評価倍率8倍、事業YはEBITDA50億円に同業の評価倍率12倍を適用する。本社コストと税を無視し、純有利子負債が500億円のとき、株式価値はいくらか。","en":"A multi-business company is valued by summing business values (sum of the parts). Business X uses EBITDA of 10 billion yen at a peer multiple of 8x, and business Y uses EBITDA of 5 billion yen at 12x. Ignoring head-office costs and taxes, with net interest-bearing debt of 50 billion yen, what is the equity value?"},"choices":[{"ja":"700億円","en":"70 billion yen"},{"ja":"1,900億円","en":"190 billion yen"},{"ja":"1,400億円","en":"140 billion yen"},{"ja":"900億円","en":"90 billion yen"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"事業別の企業価値は、X＝100億円×8＝800億円、Y＝50億円×12＝600億円で、合計1,400億円である。ここから純有利子負債500億円を引くと、株式価値は900億円となる。1,400億円は企業価値であり、負債を差し引いていない。1,900億円は負債を足す符号の誤りである。","en":"Enterprise values are X = 10 billion x 8 = 80 billion yen and Y = 5 billion x 12 = 60 billion yen, a total of 140 billion yen. Subtracting net debt of 50 billion yields an equity value of 90 billion yen. 140 billion is enterprise value with debt not deducted, and 190 billion adds debt by mistake."}},
{"id":"s15x37","dom":"execution","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"マッキンゼーの7Sモデルで、比較的変えやすいハードのSに分類されるものはどれか。","en":"In McKinsey's 7S model, which element is classified as a hard S that is relatively easy to change?"},"choices":[{"ja":"戦略（Strategy）","en":"Strategy"},{"ja":"共通の価値観（Shared Values）","en":"Shared Values"},{"ja":"スタイル（Style）","en":"Style"},{"ja":"スキル（Skills）","en":"Skills"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"7Sのうち、戦略・組織構造・システムは文書や制度として表現でき、変えやすいハードのSである。共通の価値観・スキル・スタイル・人材は形にしにくく、変化に時間のかかるソフトのSで、変革では特に調整が難しい。","en":"Of the 7S, strategy, structure and systems can be expressed in documents and rules and are the easier-to-change hard S's. Shared values, skills, style and staff are hard to codify and slow to change, so they are the soft S's that are hardest to align in a transformation."}},
{"id":"s15x38","dom":"execution","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"営業部門を売上高のみで評価したところ、過度な値引きで受注が増え、売上は伸びたが全社の粗利が悪化した。この問題の本質と対策として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"After evaluating the sales department on revenue alone, excessive discounting raised orders and sales but worsened company-wide gross profit. Which diagnosis and remedy is the most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"評価指標が戦略目標である収益性と結びついていないことが原因で、粗利や顧客別の収益性を評価に加える","en":"The cause is a metric not linked to the strategic goal of profitability; add gross profit and customer-level profitability to the evaluation"},{"ja":"売上高は最も客観的な指標なので評価はそのままにして、値引き額の把握は各営業担当者の自己申告に委ねる","en":"Revenue is the most objective metric, so leave the evaluation as it is and leave tracking of discounts to each salesperson's self-report"},{"ja":"値引きの権限が現場にあることだけが原因なので、評価指標は変えず値引きを全面的に禁止する","en":"The only cause is that discount authority sits with the field, so leave the metric unchanged and ban discounting entirely"},{"ja":"営業担当者の努力不足が原因なので、売上目標を引き上げて達成度の基準を厳しくする","en":"The cause is insufficient effort by salespeople, so raise the sales target and tighten the achievement standard"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"人は評価される指標に合わせて行動するため、売上だけを評価すると、利益を犠牲にした値引きが合理的な行動になる。戦略目標の収益性につながる粗利や顧客別収益性を評価に加え、指標を戦略と整合させるのが根本対策である。目標の引上げは、問題を悪化させる。","en":"People act to the metric they are judged by, so evaluating on revenue alone makes profit-sacrificing discounts rational. The fundamental fix is to add gross profit or customer profitability, linked to the strategic goal, and align the metric with strategy. Raising the target would worsen the problem."}},
{"id":"s15x39","dom":"execution","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある事業は売上高100億円、税引後営業利益10億円、投下資本50億円である。在庫を10億円削減して投下資本が40億円になったとき、売上と利益が変わらなければROICは何%に改善するか。","en":"A business has sales of 10 billion yen, after-tax operating profit of 1 billion yen and invested capital of 5 billion yen. If inventory is cut by 1 billion yen, reducing invested capital to 4 billion yen, to what level does ROIC improve when sales and profit are unchanged?"},"choices":[{"ja":"20%","en":"20%"},{"ja":"25%","en":"25%"},{"ja":"22%","en":"22%"},{"ja":"30%","en":"30%"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"改善前のROICは10億円÷50億円＝20%。在庫削減で投下資本が40億円になると、10億円÷40億円＝25%に改善する。利益率10%は変わらず、投下資本回転率が2.0回から2.5回に上がったことが改善の要因である。","en":"ROIC before is 1 billion / 5 billion = 20%. With inventory cut, invested capital becomes 4 billion yen and ROIC improves to 1 billion / 4 billion = 25%. The 10% margin is unchanged, and the gain comes from invested capital turnover rising from 2.0 to 2.5 times."}},
{"id":"s15x40","dom":"execution","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"市場環境の変化が速い事業で、年次予算の硬直性を和らげる管理手法として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"For a business in a fast-changing market, which management method best eases the rigidity of the annual budget?"},"choices":[{"ja":"四半期ごとに先の12〜18か月の見通しを更新する、ローリング・フォーキャストを併用する","en":"Use a rolling forecast alongside the budget, updating the outlook for the next 12 to 18 months each quarter"},{"ja":"予算は固定したまま環境変化への対応をすべて現場の裁量に任せ、本社は期末に結果だけを確認する","en":"Keep the budget fixed, leave all responses to change to the field's discretion, and have headquarters check only the results at year-end"},{"ja":"予算の達成率を厳しく評価するために期中の予算修正を禁じ、未達の責任を部門長に明確に負わせる","en":"Prohibit mid-year budget revisions to evaluate attainment strictly, and place clear responsibility for shortfalls on division heads"},{"ja":"期初に一度だけ編成した年次予算を期末まで一切修正せず、差異の分析は翌年度の予算編成に回す","en":"Never revise the annual budget set once at the start of the year, and push variance analysis to next year's budgeting"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"環境変化が速いと、年初の予算は早く陳腐化する。四半期ごとに先の12〜18か月を更新するローリング・フォーキャストなら、実態に合わせて資源配分を見直せる。期中の修正を禁じる運用は、硬直性を強め、戦略と実行のずれを広げる。","en":"In a fast-changing market the year-start budget soon goes stale. A rolling forecast updated quarterly for the next 12 to 18 months lets resource allocation follow reality. Banning mid-year revisions adds rigidity and widens the gap between strategy and execution."}},
{"id":"s15x41","dom":"execution","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"買収の目的が、対象会社の独自の開発力と意思決定の速さを維持して新分野で成長することにある。ハスペスラグとジェミソンの統合アプローチ（吸収型・保全型など）の考え方に照らして、最も適切な進め方はどれか。","en":"The purpose of an acquisition is to keep the target's distinctive development capability and speed of decision-making and grow in a new field. In light of Haspeslagh and Jemison's integration approaches (absorption, preservation and others), which is the most appropriate way to proceed?"},"choices":[{"ja":"放任型：統合の取組みは行わず、能力の移転も想定せず、財務数値の連結以外にはほとんど関与しない","en":"Hands-off: make no integration effort, plan no capability transfer, and do little beyond consolidating the financials"},{"ja":"本社直轄型：買い手の経営陣を主要ポストへ送り込み、意思決定を本社へ集中させて統制を強める","en":"Headquarters control: place the buyer's executives in key posts and centralize decisions at headquarters to tighten control"},{"ja":"吸収型：対象会社を速やかに買い手の組織・制度・手続へ吸収し、重複する機能を整理する","en":"Absorption: quickly fold the target into the buyer's organization, systems and procedures and consolidate duplicated functions"},{"ja":"保全型：対象会社の自律性を保ち、戦略上必要な接点だけを選んで統合し、能力の移転を慎重に進める","en":"Preservation: keep the target autonomous, integrate only the interfaces needed strategically, and transfer capabilities carefully"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"目的が対象会社の独自能力と意思決定の速さの維持にある場合は、自律性を保つ保全型が適する。統合は戦略上必要な接点に絞り、能力の移転を慎重に進める。吸収型や本社直轄は、強みの源泉である自律性を壊す。放任では、買収の狙いである新分野の成長に結びつかない。","en":"When the aim is to keep the target's distinctive capability and decision speed, preservation, which maintains autonomy, fits. Integration is limited to strategically necessary interfaces and capability transfer proceeds carefully. Absorption and headquarters control destroy the autonomy that is the source of strength, and a hands-off stance does not deliver the new-field growth the deal targets."}},
{"id":"s15x42","dom":"execution","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"新工場の建設に既に120億円を投じたが、市場環境の悪化で収益が想定を下回る。完成させるには追加で30億円が必要で、完成後に稼働させた場合の将来キャッシュフローの現在価値は25億円と見積られる。完成させないときの回収額は0円とすると、経済合理性に沿った判断はどれか。","en":"A new plant has already absorbed 12 billion yen, but weaker markets leave returns below plan. Completing it needs another 3 billion yen, and the present value of future cash flows once operating is estimated at 2.5 billion yen. If abandoning recovers nothing, which decision is economically rational?"},"choices":[{"ja":"市場環境が回復するまで投資額を変えずに工事を保留し、判断を無期限に先送りする","en":"Suspend construction with the investment unchanged until the market recovers and postpone the decision indefinitely"},{"ja":"追加投資が現在価値を5億円上回っても、既存投資の回収が優先なので、完成後に稼働させる","en":"Even though the extra investment exceeds present value by 500 million yen, recovering the existing investment comes first, so complete and run it"},{"ja":"既に120億円を投じているので、投資を無駄にしないために30億円を追加して完成させる","en":"Complete it with another 3 billion yen so that the 12 billion yen already invested is not wasted"},{"ja":"追加投資30億円が将来の現在価値25億円を上回るので、完成させずに中止する","en":"Stop without completing, because the additional 3 billion yen exceeds the 2.5 billion yen present value of future cash flows"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"既に投じた120億円は、完成させても中止しても戻らない埋没費用であり、判断には使わない。追加の30億円に対し得られる現在価値が25億円なら、完成させると5億円の価値を失う。中止が合理的である。投資済み額の回収を理由に続けると、損失を拡大させる。","en":"The 12 billion yen already spent is a sunk cost that is lost whether the plant is completed or not, so it is ignored. If an extra 3 billion yen yields a present value of 2.5 billion, completing it loses 500 million yen of value, so stopping is rational. Continuing to recover past spending enlarges the loss."}},
{"id":"s15x43","dom":"execution","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ルメルトが『良い戦略』の核（カーネル）とした3つの要素はどれか。","en":"Which three elements did Rumelt name as the kernel of a good strategy?"},"choices":[{"ja":"診断、基本方針、一貫した行動","en":"Diagnosis, guiding policy and coherent action"},{"ja":"市場分析、競合分析、自社分析の3つの現状把握","en":"The three situation assessments of market analysis, competitor analysis and self-analysis"},{"ja":"目標設定、予算配分、業績評価の3つの管理プロセス","en":"The three management processes of goal setting, budget allocation and performance evaluation"},{"ja":"ビジョン、ミッション、バリューとして掲げる3つの理念","en":"The three statements of vision, mission and values"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"ルメルトは、良い戦略の核を、状況の本質をつかむ診断、診断への対処の方向を示す基本方針、基本方針を具体化する一貫した行動の3つとした。目標や予算の羅列、理念の掲示は、診断も行動の一貫性も欠く悪い戦略の典型として退けた。","en":"Rumelt put at the core of good strategy a diagnosis that grasps the nature of the situation, a guiding policy for dealing with it, and coherent actions that carry out the policy. He rejected lists of goals and budgets or posted ideals as typical bad strategy, lacking diagnosis and coherent action."}},
{"id":"s15x44","dom":"dynamics","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"寡占市場で同じ数社が長期にわたり価格競争を繰り返す状況で、暗黙の協調（高い価格の維持）が成り立ちやすくなる条件として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"In an oligopoly where the same few firms repeat price competition over a long period, which condition most favors tacit coordination (holding prices high)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"各社が今期の利益だけを重視し、競合の価格が把握しにくく、逸脱への報復の手段もないこと","en":"Firms care only about this period's profit, rivals' prices are hard to observe, and there is no means of retaliating against deviation"},{"ja":"各社の費用構造と製品の差が大きく、需要も大きく変動するため、協調の基準が定まりにくいこと","en":"Cost structures and products differ widely and demand fluctuates greatly, so a benchmark for coordination is hard to settle"},{"ja":"将来の利益を重く見て、逸脱を素早く見つけて報復でき、協調の利益が逸脱の短期利益を上回ること","en":"Firms weigh future profits heavily, can quickly detect and retaliate against deviation, and the gains from coordination exceed the short-term gain from deviating"},{"ja":"新規参入が容易で参加企業が入れ替わりやすく、取引関係が1回限りに近い性質を強く持っていること","en":"Entry is easy, participants turn over often, and the relationships are close to one-off in nature"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"繰り返しゲームでは、逸脱による今期の得より、報復で将来の協調利益を失う損の方が大きければ、協調が維持される。将来を重視し、逸脱を素早く検知でき、報復が信頼できることが条件になる。目先の利益重視、1回限りに近い取引、費用や需要の不安定は、いずれも協調を崩す方向に働く。","en":"In a repeated game, coordination holds if the loss of future coordination gains through retaliation outweighs this period's gain from deviating. The conditions are valuing the future, detecting deviation quickly and credible retaliation. Short-termism, near one-off dealings and unstable costs or demand all undermine coordination."}},
{"id":"s15x45","dom":"dynamics","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"既存企業が需要を上回る生産能力を事前に整備しておくことが、新規参入の阻止に有効になりうる理由として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate reason why an incumbent building production capacity beyond demand in advance can be effective in deterring new entry?"},"choices":[{"ja":"過剰な設備はいつでも売却して資金化できるので、参入があれば直ちに事業を縮小して、競争を避けられるから","en":"Excess equipment can be sold for cash at any time, so if entry occurs the incumbent can shrink at once and avoid competition"},{"ja":"設備の過剰は規模の経済を弱めるので、参入者との費用の差が縮まり、価格で競争できなくなるから","en":"Excess equipment weakens economies of scale, so the cost gap with entrants narrows and the incumbent can no longer compete on price"},{"ja":"遊休設備は費用がかからないので価格を高く維持でき、参入者がその高い価格を見て参入を誘われるから","en":"Idle equipment costs nothing, so prices can be kept high, and entrants are drawn in by the high price"},{"ja":"参入後に即座に増産して価格を下げられるため、報復の脅しに信憑性があり、参入者の見込み利益を下げるから","en":"It can expand output and cut prices immediately after entry, so the threat of retaliation is credible and lowers the entrant's expected profit"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"過剰能力は既に費用を払った埋没投資であり、参入後に増産して価格を下げる追加費用が小さい。そのため報復の脅しが信憑性を持ち、参入者の見込み利益が下がって参入が思いとどまられる。能力の過剰が価格を高止まりさせたり、縮小を容易にしたりするわけではない。","en":"Excess capacity is a sunk investment already paid for, so the extra cost of expanding output and cutting prices after entry is small. The threat of retaliation is therefore credible, entrants' expected profits fall and entry is discouraged. Excess capacity neither keeps prices high nor makes shrinking easy."}},
{"id":"s15x46","dom":"dynamics","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ネットワークの価値が接続可能な組合せの数（ユーザー数の2乗にほぼ比例）で決まると仮定する。ユーザー数が10倍になったとき、ネットワークの価値はおよそ何倍になるか。","en":"Assume network value is determined by the number of possible connections, roughly proportional to the square of the number of users. When users grow tenfold, by about how many times does network value rise?"},"choices":[{"ja":"20倍","en":"20 times"},{"ja":"100倍","en":"100 times"},{"ja":"1,000倍","en":"1,000 times"},{"ja":"10倍","en":"10 times"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"価値がユーザー数の2乗に比例するなら、ユーザー数が10倍で価値は10の2乗＝100倍になる。接続の組合せは n(n−1)/2 で、nが大きいほど2乗に近づく。10倍は価値がユーザー数に比例する場合、1,000倍は3乗に比例する場合の値である。","en":"If value is proportional to the square of users, a tenfold increase in users raises value by 10^2 = 100 times. The number of connections is n(n-1)/2, which approaches the square as n grows. 10 times applies if value is proportional to users, and 1,000 times if proportional to the cube."}},
{"id":"s15x47","dom":"dynamics","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"新しいフリマアプリが、買い手と売り手の双方が少ない立上げ期に直面する『鶏と卵』問題への対策として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate way for a new flea-market app to tackle the chicken-and-egg problem at launch, when both buyers and sellers are few?"},"choices":[{"ja":"サービスの機能を絞り込み、広告費を投じずに口コミだけで双方の利用者が自然に増えていくのを待つ","en":"Narrow the service features and wait for both groups to grow naturally through word of mouth with no advertising spend"},{"ja":"利用者数が十分に増えるまで、運営会社が全ての出品物の品質を審査して掲載の可否を決める","en":"Until users grow enough, have the operator review the quality of every listing and decide whether it is posted"},{"ja":"買い手と売り手の双方から同額の手数料を徴収して、立上げ初期から収益性を確保する","en":"Charge both buyers and sellers the same fee to secure profitability from the earliest stage"},{"ja":"一方の側（例えば売り手）に手数料の無料化や出品支援を集中して先に集め、もう一方の側を呼び込む","en":"Concentrate on one side, for example sellers, with fee waivers and listing support to gather them first and then draw in the other side"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"マルチサイド・プラットフォームでは、片側が少ないともう片側にとっての価値も低く、双方が増えない。一方に補助や無料化を集中して先に呼び込み、その存在を理由にもう一方を引き込むのが定石である。初期に双方へ課金したり、審査で絞ったりすると、成長が止まる。","en":"On a multi-sided platform, too few on one side lowers value for the other, so neither grows. The standard move is to subsidize or waive fees for one side first and use that presence to draw in the other. Charging both sides early or restricting through screening stalls growth."}},
{"id":"s15x48","dom":"dynamics","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"クリステンセンの『新市場型破壊』の特徴として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate characteristic of Christensen's new-market disruption?"},"choices":[{"ja":"既存市場の最上位の顧客に、高性能で高価な製品を提供して、既存企業の利益を奪う","en":"Offering high-performance, expensive products to the top customers of an existing market and taking incumbents' profits"},{"ja":"既存市場の低価格帯の顧客に、既存企業より安い製品を提供して、下位市場から侵食する","en":"Offering cheaper products than incumbents to low-end customers of an existing market and eroding it from below"},{"ja":"既存製品を使えなかった無消費の層に、単純で安価な製品を提供して新しい市場を作る","en":"Offering simple, inexpensive products to non-consumers who could not use existing products and creating a new market"},{"ja":"既存の大手企業の顧客を、営業人員の増員と値下げによって短期間で奪い取る","en":"Taking large incumbents' customers in a short time through more salespeople and price cuts"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"新市場型破壊は、従来の製品が高価・複雑で使えなかった無消費の層に、単純で手頃な製品を届けて新しい市場を作る。既存の下位市場を低価格で侵食するのはローエンド型破壊である。高性能路線での上位顧客の獲得は、持続的イノベーションに当たる。","en":"New-market disruption brings simple, affordable products to non-consumers who found earlier products too costly or complex and creates a new market. Eroding an existing market from below with low prices is low-end disruption, and winning top customers with higher performance is sustaining innovation."}},
{"id":"s15x49","dom":"dynamics","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"利用者が複数のプラットフォームを同時に使うマルチホーミングが一般的な市場では、勝者総取りが起きにくい。その理由として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"In markets where multi-homing, using several platforms at once, is common, winner-take-all outcomes are less likely. Which is the most appropriate reason?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ネットワーク効果は複数のプラットフォームを併用する利用者にだけ働き、新規に参加する利用者にとっては価値が生まれないから","en":"Network effects work only for users who use several platforms at once and create no value for newly joining users"},{"ja":"併用の利用者が増えるほど全プラットフォームの質が自動的に同水準へ収斂し、価格競争が止まるから","en":"As more users multi-home, the quality of all platforms automatically converges to the same level and price competition stops"},{"ja":"利用者の併用は各プラットフォームの収益を高めるため、すべての運営会社が高い利益率を保てるから","en":"Users' multi-homing raises each platform's revenue, so every operator can maintain a high profit margin"},{"ja":"利用者が併用できるので、ひとつのプラットフォームが利用者を囲い込めず、規模が大きくても他社が存続できるから","en":"Users can use several platforms, so no single platform can lock them in, and other platforms survive even if one is larger"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"勝者総取りは、利用者が1つに集中するほど価値が高まり、他へ乗り換える動機が生まれる状況で起きる。併用が容易でスイッチングコストが低いと、大手のプラットフォームでも囲い込めず、小規模な競合が特定の利用者や機能で共存できる。","en":"Winner-take-all arises when value rises as users concentrate on one platform and give others up. With easy multi-homing and low switching costs, even a large platform cannot lock users in, and smaller rivals can coexist by serving particular users or functions."}},
{"id":"s15x50","dom":"dynamics","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"経験曲線効果が強い製品で、市場の成長期に当初コストを下回る価格でも販売して累積生産量を積み上げる戦略が正当化される条件として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"For a product with a strong experience curve, which condition best justifies selling below initial cost during market growth to build cumulative volume?"},"choices":[{"ja":"需要の価格弾力性が低く、値下げをしても販売量がほとんど増えず、累積生産量もなかなか伸びていかないという状況にあること","en":"Price elasticity of demand is low, so cutting the price barely raises volume and cumulative output hardly grows"},{"ja":"固定費がほとんどなく、生産量が増えても単位コストが下がらない費用構造になっていること","en":"There are almost no fixed costs and the cost structure keeps unit cost from falling as output increases"},{"ja":"製品の差別化が進んでいて、顧客が価格に敏感でなく、高い価格でも十分に売れる状態にあること","en":"The product is well differentiated, customers are not price sensitive, and it sells well even at a high price"},{"ja":"将来のコスト低下が十分に大きく、先行して得たコスト優位を競合が短期間で追いつけない形で固定できること","en":"Future cost reductions are large enough, and the cost advantage gained first can be locked in so that rivals cannot catch up quickly"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"当初コスト割れの価格が正当化されるのは、累積生産量の増加でコストが大きく下がり、その優位を競合が追随できない形で確保できる場合である。需要が価格に反応せず量が増えない、差別化で高価格が通る、単位コストが下がらない構造では、先行して損失を出す意味がない。","en":"Below-cost pricing is justified when rising cumulative output cuts costs sharply and the advantage can be secured so rivals cannot follow. If demand does not respond to price, differentiation supports high prices, or unit cost does not fall, there is no point in taking early losses."}}
);
