  _quiz.push(
{"id":"s16x01","dom":"corptax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"資本金10億円の内国法人（中小法人等に該当しない）の当期の繰越欠損金控除前の所得は8,000万円で、青色申告の繰越欠損金（10年内に生じたもの）が2億円ある。当期に控除できる繰越欠損金の額はいくらか。","en":"A Japanese corporation with 1 billion yen of capital (not a small or medium-sized corporation) has pre-deduction income of 80 million yen for the year and 200 million yen of blue-return net operating losses incurred within 10 years. How much of the losses can be deducted this year?"},"choices":[{"ja":"6,000万円","en":"60 million yen"},{"ja":"8,000万円","en":"80 million yen"},{"ja":"4,000万円","en":"40 million yen"},{"ja":"2億円","en":"200 million yen"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"資本金1億円超の大法人では、繰越欠損金の控除限度は控除前所得の50%で、8,000万円×50%＝4,000万円である。所得の全額まで控除できるのは中小法人等だけで、残る欠損金は翌期以降に繰り越す（2026年10月時点）。","en":"For large corporations with capital above 100 million yen, the loss deduction cap is 50% of pre-deduction income: 80 million yen x 50% = 40 million yen. Only small and medium-sized corporations can offset up to the full income, and the remaining losses carry forward (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x02","dom":"corptax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"内国法人が、発行済株式の3%を保有する上場会社から配当1億円を受け取った。負債利子の控除を無視すると、法人税の所得計算で益金に算入される額はいくらか。","en":"A Japanese corporation holding 3% of a listed company's issued shares receives a dividend of 100 million yen. Ignoring the deduction for interest on debt, how much enters taxable gross income for corporate tax?"},"choices":[{"ja":"5,000万円","en":"50 million yen"},{"ja":"1億円","en":"100 million yen"},{"ja":"0円","en":"0 yen"},{"ja":"8,000万円","en":"80 million yen"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"保有割合5%以下の株式は非支配目的株式等で、受取配当の益金不算入割合は20%である。1億円×(1−20%)＝8,000万円が益金に算入される。0円は完全子法人株式など全額不算入の区分、5,000万円は保有割合5%超から3分の1以下の区分の割合である（2026年10月時点）。","en":"Shares held at 5% or less are non-controlling-purpose shares, for which 20% of dividends received is excluded from gross income. 100 million yen x (1 - 20%) = 80 million yen is included. 0 yen applies to fully excluded categories such as wholly owned subsidiary shares, and 50 million yen is the result for holdings above 5% and up to one third (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x03","dom":"corptax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"親会社が、完全支配関係にある国内の100%子会社に、事業上の理由なく現金1,000万円を無償で供与した。法人税の取扱いとして正しいのはどれか。","en":"A parent company gave 10 million yen in cash for no business reason to its 100% domestic subsidiary, with which it has a full control relationship. Which statement on corporate tax treatment is correct?"},"choices":[{"ja":"親会社は寄附金の損金算入限度額までは損金に算入でき、子会社は受贈益の全額が益金に算入される","en":"The parent may deduct up to the donation deduction limit, and the subsidiary includes the whole gift in gross income"},{"ja":"親会社は全額が損金不算入、子会社は全額が益金不算入となる","en":"The parent's amount is wholly non-deductible and the subsidiary's receipt is wholly excluded from gross income"},{"ja":"親会社は全額を損金に算入でき、子会社は受贈益の全額が益金に算入される","en":"The parent may deduct the whole amount, and the subsidiary includes the whole gift in gross income"},{"ja":"親会社も子会社も、時価との差額に当たる部分だけを損金または益金として認識する","en":"Both recognize as a deduction or income only the portion equal to the difference from fair value"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"完全支配関係にある法人間の寄附は、支払側で全額が損金不算入、受取側で全額が益金不算入になる。課税関係がグループ内で中立となり、利益の付替えによる税負担の調整を防ぐ。限度額まで損金算入できる一般の寄附金や、受贈益課税とは異なる扱いである。","en":"Donations between corporations with a full control relationship are wholly non-deductible for the payer and wholly excluded from income for the recipient. The tax result is neutral within the group, which prevents tax adjustment by shifting profit. This differs from ordinary donations deductible up to a limit and from taxation of gains on gifts."}},
{"id":"s16x04","dom":"corptax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"期末に貸倒引当金の繰入限度超過額が1,000万円あった（税務上は損金不算入で、将来の貸倒れ時に損金算入となる）。法定実効税率を30%とし、回収可能性に問題がないとき、税効果会計で計上するのはどれか。","en":"At year-end the allowance for doubtful accounts exceeded the tax-deductible limit by 10 million yen (non-deductible now, deductible when the loss actually occurs). With a statutory effective tax rate of 30% and no recoverability problem, what is recorded under tax effect accounting?"},"choices":[{"ja":"一時差異に当たらないため何も計上しない","en":"Nothing, because it is not a temporary difference"},{"ja":"繰延税金資産1,000万円を計上する","en":"A deferred tax asset of 10 million yen"},{"ja":"繰延税金資産300万円を計上する","en":"A deferred tax asset of 3 million yen"},{"ja":"繰延税金負債300万円を計上する","en":"A deferred tax liability of 3 million yen"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"貸倒引当金の繰入限度超過額は、会計上は費用だが税務上は損金不算入で、将来の損金算入時に税負担を減らす将来減算一時差異である。1,000万円×30%＝300万円が繰延税金資産となる。1,000万円を資産計上するのは、税率を掛けていない誤りである。","en":"The excess allowance is an expense in the books but non-deductible for tax now, and it reduces future tax when deducted, so it is a deductible temporary difference. 10 million yen x 30% = 3 million yen is recorded as a deferred tax asset. Recording 10 million yen forgets to apply the tax rate."}},
{"id":"s16x05","dom":"corptax","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"3月決算（4月〜翌3月）の会社が、取締役の月額報酬を10月に増額改定した。定時株主総会の決議は6月で、業績悪化などの臨時改定事由はない。この増額分の法人税上の扱いとして適切なのはどれか。","en":"A company with a March fiscal year-end (April to March) raised a director's monthly pay in October. The ordinary general meeting resolution was in June, and there is no special revision event such as a poor result. How is the increase treated for corporate tax?"},"choices":[{"ja":"株主総会で決議された報酬なので、改定の時期にかかわらず、増額分も含めて全額が損金に算入される","en":"Since pay was resolved at the general meeting, the full amount including the increase is deductible regardless of timing"},{"ja":"増額分の2分の1に限り損金に算入され、残りの2分の1は翌期の損金へ繰り越される","en":"Only half of the increase is deductible and the other half is carried over to the next year as a deduction"},{"ja":"期首から3か月を超えた改定は定期同額給与に当たらず、増額分は損金不算入となる","en":"A revision made more than three months after the start of the year does not qualify as fixed periodic pay, so the increase is non-deductible"},{"ja":"増額改定の届出書を改定日から1か月以内に税務署へ提出すれば、増額分も損金に算入される","en":"If a notification of the raise is filed with the tax office within one month of the revision date, the increase is also deductible"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"定期同額給与は、期首から3か月以内の通常改定、臨時改定事由、業績悪化改定事由による改定でなければ、期中に増額すると定期同額と認められない。10月の増額は該当せず、増額分は損金不算入になる。届出で救済される事前確定届出給与は別の枠組みである。","en":"Fixed periodic pay loses that status if raised mid-year, unless the change is an ordinary revision within three months of the year start or arises from a special revision event or a worsening of results. The October increase fits none, so the increase is non-deductible. Pay fixed in advance by notification is a separate framework."}},
{"id":"s16x06","dom":"corptax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"適格請求書発行事業者でない免税事業者から課税仕入れを行った場合、2026年10月1日から2029年9月30日までに行う仕入れに適用される、仕入税額控除の経過措置の控除割合はどれか。","en":"When taxable purchases are made from an exempt business that is not a qualified invoice issuer, what is the deduction ratio under the transitional input tax credit rule for purchases made from October 1, 2026 to September 30, 2029?"},"choices":[{"ja":"80%","en":"80%"},{"ja":"20%","en":"20%"},{"ja":"50%","en":"50%"},{"ja":"100%","en":"100%"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"インボイス制度の経過措置では、免税事業者などからの課税仕入れについて、2023年10月から2026年9月までは仕入税額相当額の80%、2026年10月から2029年9月までは50%を控除でき、その後は控除できない（2026年10月時点）。80%は前の期間の割合である。","en":"Under the invoice system's transitional rule, input tax on purchases from exempt businesses is 80% deductible from October 2023 to September 2026 and 50% from October 2026 to September 2029, and not deductible after that (as of October 2026). 80% is the ratio of the previous period."}},
{"id":"s16x07","dom":"corptax","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"法人税の確定申告書の提出期限は、原則としていつか（延長の特例を受けない場合）。","en":"By when must a corporate tax final return be filed in principle, without an extension special rule?"},"choices":[{"ja":"事業年度終了の日の翌日から6か月以内","en":"Within six months from the day after the end of the fiscal year"},{"ja":"事業年度終了の日の翌日から1か月以内","en":"Within one month from the day after the end of the fiscal year"},{"ja":"事業年度終了の日の翌日から2か月以内","en":"Within two months from the day after the end of the fiscal year"},{"ja":"事業年度終了の日の翌日から3か月以内","en":"Within three months from the day after the end of the fiscal year"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"法人税の確定申告書は、事業年度終了の日の翌日から2か月以内に提出し、納付もこの期限までに行う。申請により1か月延長する特例があるが、延長しても納付期限は延びず、延長期間には利子税がかかる。","en":"A corporate tax final return is due within two months from the day after the fiscal year ends, and payment is due by the same date. An extension of one month is available on application, but the payment deadline is not extended and interest tax applies for the extended period."}},
{"id":"s16x08","dom":"corptax","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"B社（繰越欠損金あり）をA社が適格合併で吸収する。A社とB社は、合併の7年前から親会社を同じくする完全支配関係にある。合併後のA社へのB社の繰越欠損金の引継ぎとして適切なのはどれか。","en":"Company A absorbs Company B, which has net operating losses, in a qualified merger. A and B have been under the same parent in a full control relationship for seven years before the merger. Which describes the carry-over of B's losses to A?"},"choices":[{"ja":"引き継げるのは合併前5年以内に生じた欠損金に限られ、5年を超える分は切り捨てられる","en":"Only losses arising within five years before the merger carry over, and those older than five years are cut off"},{"ja":"適格合併でも欠損金の引継ぎは認められず、B社の欠損金は合併の時点で消滅する","en":"Even in a qualified merger, losses may not be carried over and B's losses expire at the merger"},{"ja":"引継ぎにはみなし共同事業要件の充足が常に必要で、支配関係の継続期間がどれだけ長くても結論は変わらない","en":"Carry-over always requires the deemed joint business requirements, and the length of the control relationship does not affect the result"},{"ja":"支配関係が5年を超えて継続しているので、みなし共同事業要件を満たさなくても、欠損金を引き継げる","en":"Because the control relationship has lasted more than five years, the losses carry over even without meeting the deemed joint business requirements"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"適格合併では被合併法人の繰越欠損金を引き継げる。ただし、支配関係が合併の前5年以内に生じた場合は、みなし共同事業要件などを満たさないと一部が制限される。本件は支配関係が5年超であり、この制限を受けず、引継ぎが可能である（2026年10月時点）。","en":"A qualified merger lets the absorbed company's losses carry over. If the control relationship arose within five years before the merger, however, part is restricted unless requirements such as the deemed joint business test are met. Here the relationship exceeds five years, so the restriction does not apply and carry-over is possible (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x09","dom":"intltax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"内国法人が、持株比率25%以上を6か月以上保有する外国子会社から配当1億円を受け取った。外国子会社配当益金不算入制度により、益金に算入される額はいくらか（外国での源泉税は考慮しない）。","en":"A Japanese corporation receives a dividend of 100 million yen from a foreign subsidiary in which it has held at least 25% for at least six months. Under the foreign subsidiary dividend exclusion, how much enters gross income (ignoring foreign withholding tax)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1億円","en":"100 million yen"},{"ja":"0円","en":"0 yen"},{"ja":"500万円","en":"5 million yen"},{"ja":"5,000万円","en":"50 million yen"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"外国子会社配当益金不算入制度では、配当の95%が益金不算入となり、残る5%が益金に算入される（子会社株式の管理費用に相当する部分とされる）。1億円×5%＝500万円である。全額不算入の0円は国内の完全子法人株式の扱いで、外国子会社配当には当てはまらない（2026年10月時点）。","en":"Under the foreign subsidiary dividend exclusion, 95% of the dividend is excluded and the remaining 5% enters gross income (treated as covering the cost of managing the shares). 100 million yen x 5% = 5 million yen. Zero applies to domestic wholly owned subsidiary shares and not to foreign subsidiary dividends (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x10","dom":"intltax","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本に事務所を持たない米国企業の社員が、日本に出張を繰り返して顧客と価格・数量の条件を実質的に交渉し、契約の内容を確定させている（契約書の署名は米国で行う）。日本の法人税上の評価として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Employees of a US company with no office in Japan travel to Japan repeatedly, substantively negotiate price and quantity with customers and settle the contract terms (signing takes place in the US). Which is the most appropriate assessment for Japanese corporate tax?"},"choices":[{"ja":"契約書の署名が米国で行われる以上、日本でどれだけ条件を交渉しても契約とは無関係であり、恒久的施設は認定されない","en":"Since signing happens in the US, however much is negotiated in Japan it is unrelated to the contract and no permanent establishment is found"},{"ja":"契約の締結に重要な役割を果たす代理人が日本にいるとして、恒久的施設（代理人PE）が認定される可能性が高い","en":"Because an agent playing a key role in concluding contracts is present in Japan, a permanent establishment (agent PE) is likely to be found"},{"ja":"日本に支店などの固定的な事務所がない限り、事業活動の内容にかかわらず恒久的施設にはならない","en":"Unless there is a fixed place such as a branch in Japan, no permanent establishment arises whatever the business activity"},{"ja":"恒久的施設の認定は、日本での滞在日数が年間183日を超えるかどうかのみで機械的に決まる","en":"Permanent establishment status is determined mechanically only by whether stays in Japan exceed 183 days a year"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"BEPS行動7を受けた国内法の改正後は、契約の締結に重要な役割を果たす者も代理人PEの判定に含める。署名の場所に関係なく、日本で条件交渉を実質的に行い契約を確定させているなら、PE認定のリスクが高い。固定的事務所の有無や滞在日数だけでは決まらない。","en":"Since domestic law was amended following BEPS Action 7, persons who play a key role in concluding contracts are included in the agent PE test. Wherever the signing takes place, substantive negotiation in Japan that settles the contract carries a high risk of PE status. It does not hinge only on a fixed office or days of stay."}},
{"id":"s16x11","dom":"intltax","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本の親会社が、海外の製造子会社に自社の設計・仕様・原材料調達の指示のもとで製品を受託製造させ、全量を買い取っている。製造子会社は独自の無形資産を持たず、機能とリスクが限定的で、同一仕様の第三者取引はない。この取引の独立企業間価格を検証する手法として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"A Japanese parent has an overseas manufacturing subsidiary make products under contract to its design, specifications and materials sourcing instructions, and buys the entire output. The subsidiary has no unique intangibles, performs limited functions and bears limited risks, and no third-party transaction on the same specification exists. Which method is most appropriate for testing the arm's-length price?"},"choices":[{"ja":"親会社の総売上高営業利益率を、比較対象となる独立企業と比べる取引単位営業利益法（TNMM）","en":"The TNMM applied to the parent, comparing its operating margin on total sales with comparable independent companies"},{"ja":"親会社と子会社の合算利益を、双方が保有する資産額に比例して配分する残余利益分割法","en":"The residual profit split method, allocating the combined profit in proportion to the assets each party holds"},{"ja":"子会社から親会社への販売価格を、第三者が同じ製品を販売した価格と比べる独立価格比準法（CUP法）","en":"The comparable uncontrolled price (CUP) method, comparing the sales price from subsidiary to parent with the price third parties charge for the same product"},{"ja":"製造子会社を検証対象とし、総原価営業利益率を独立企業と比べる取引単位営業利益法（TNMM）","en":"The transactional net margin method (TNMM), testing the subsidiary and comparing its operating margin on total cost with comparable independent companies"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"機能とリスクが限定的な受託製造子会社は、単純な機能を担う側として検証対象に選び、総原価営業利益率を比較対象企業と比べるTNMMで検証するのが一般的である。同一仕様の第三者取引がなく、CUP法は使いにくい。双方が独自の無形資産を持つときに使う利益分割法も適さない。","en":"A contract manufacturing subsidiary with limited functions and risks is usually chosen as the tested party, and TNMM comparing its operating margin on total cost with comparable companies is the standard test. With no third-party transaction on the same specification, CUP is hard to use. Profit split, used when both sides own unique intangibles, does not fit either."}},
{"id":"s16x12","dom":"intltax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"日本の内国法人が、国外関連者Zとの間で前期に、棚卸資産の取引（受払合計）40億円と、ロイヤルティなどの無形資産取引（受払合計）4億円を行った。移転価格税制の同時文書化（ローカルファイル）に関する取扱いとして適切なのはどれか。","en":"A Japanese corporation transacted with foreign related party Z in the previous year, with inventory transactions of 4 billion yen in total and intangible transactions such as royalties of 400 million yen in total. Which is the appropriate treatment under the contemporaneous documentation (local file) rules of transfer pricing?"},"choices":[{"ja":"作成義務はなく、税務調査で求められたときに、60日以内に独立企業間価格を算定する資料を作成すればよい","en":"There is no duty to prepare it, and it suffices to create materials computing the arm's-length price within 60 days when requested in a tax audit"},{"ja":"ローカルファイルの作成義務は資本金100億円以上の法人に限られ、この法人は対象外である","en":"The local file duty applies only to corporations with capital of 10 billion yen or more, and this corporation is outside it"},{"ja":"棚卸資産の取引が50億円未満のため、無形資産取引の額にかかわらずローカルファイルの作成義務はない","en":"Because inventory transactions are under 5 billion yen, there is no duty to prepare a local file regardless of the intangible transaction amount"},{"ja":"無形資産取引が3億円以上のため、ローカルファイルを確定申告書の提出期限までに作成・保存する義務がある","en":"Because intangible transactions are 300 million yen or more, the company must prepare and retain a local file by the filing deadline of the final return"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"ローカルファイルは、国外関連者との前期の取引が、受払合計で50億円以上、または無形資産取引が3億円以上のとき、確定申告書の提出期限までに作成・保存する義務を負う。本件は無形資産取引が4億円で基準を超える。棚卸資産が40億円でも、無形資産の基準で判定される（2026年10月時点）。","en":"A local file must be prepared and retained by the final return filing deadline when the previous year's transactions with a foreign related party total 5 billion yen or more, or intangible transactions are 300 million yen or more. Here intangibles are 400 million yen, above the threshold, and the 4 billion yen of inventory does not change that (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x13","dom":"intltax","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"日本法人が米国法人へソフトウェアの使用料を支払う際に、租税条約の軽減税率（または免税）を適用するために必要な手続はどれか。","en":"When a Japanese company pays software royalties to a US company, which procedure is needed to apply the reduced rate (or exemption) under the tax treaty?"},"choices":[{"ja":"届出は不要で、支払者が租税条約の存在を認識していれば、自動的に軽減税率が適用される","en":"No filing is needed and the reduced rate applies automatically if the payer knows of the treaty"},{"ja":"受領者が米国の税務当局に納税証明書を発行してもらい、その写しを日本の税務署へ翌年に提出する","en":"The recipient has the US tax authority issue a tax payment certificate and submits a copy to the Japanese tax office the following year"},{"ja":"受領者が『租税条約に関する届出書』を、最初の支払の前日までに支払者経由で税務署へ提出する","en":"The recipient files the treaty application form with the tax office through the payer by the day before the first payment"},{"ja":"支払者が国税庁の事前承認を得たうえで、租税条約を適用する旨を支払後の確定申告書へ記載する","en":"The payer obtains advance approval from the National Tax Agency and then states in the post-payment final return that the treaty applies"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"租税条約の軽減・免除を受けるには、使用料などの受領者が、最初に支払を受ける日の前日までに『租税条約に関する源泉徴収税額の軽減・免除届出書』を、支払者を経由して税務署に提出する。届出がなければ、国内法の税率で源泉徴収される。","en":"To obtain treaty reduction or exemption, the recipient of royalties files the treaty application form through the payer with the tax office by the day before it first receives payment. Without the filing, tax is withheld at the domestic law rate."}},
{"id":"s16x14","dom":"intltax","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"税源浸食と利益移転（BEPS）プロジェクトを主導した国際機関はどれか。","en":"Which international organization led the Base Erosion and Profit Shifting (BEPS) project?"},"choices":[{"ja":"世界貿易機関（WTO）とその紛争解決機関","en":"The World Trade Organization (WTO) and its dispute settlement body"},{"ja":"国際決済銀行（BIS）のバーゼル委員会","en":"The Basel Committee of the Bank for International Settlements (BIS)"},{"ja":"経済協力開発機構（OECD）","en":"The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD)"},{"ja":"国際通貨基金（IMF）と世界銀行グループ","en":"The International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the World Bank Group"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"BEPSプロジェクトは、多国籍企業による租税回避への国際的な対応として、G20の要請を受けOECDが主導した。2015年に15項目の行動計画の最終報告書が公表され、移転価格文書化や恒久的施設の人為的回避の防止などが各国の制度に反映された。IMFやWTOは主導機関ではない。","en":"The BEPS project was led by the OECD at the request of the G20 as an international response to tax avoidance by multinationals. Final reports on the 15 action items were published in 2015, and measures such as transfer pricing documentation and prevention of artificial avoidance of permanent establishment status entered national rules. The IMF and WTO did not lead it."}},
{"id":"s16x15","dom":"intltax","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"多国籍企業グループの軽課税国にある子会社について、国別のGloBE所得が100億円、実効税率が9%、最低税率が15%である。実質ベースの所得除外などを考慮しないとき、所得合算ルール（IIR）などにより課される上乗せ税額はいくらか。","en":"For a subsidiary in a low-tax country of a multinational group, the jurisdictional GloBE income is 10 billion yen, the effective tax rate is 9% and the minimum rate is 15%. Disregarding the substance-based income exclusion and similar items, what top-up tax is imposed through rules such as the income inclusion rule (IIR)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"15億円","en":"1.5 billion yen"},{"ja":"24億円","en":"2.4 billion yen"},{"ja":"9億円","en":"900 million yen"},{"ja":"6億円","en":"600 million yen"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"上乗せ税率は、最低税率15%から実効税率9%を引いた6%で、これを国別のGloBE所得100億円に掛けて6億円となる。9億円は子会社がすでに現地で負担した税額、15億円は最低税率で課税した場合の総額で、すでに納めた税額を差し引いていない。最低税率は15%（2026年10月時点）。","en":"The top-up tax rate is the 15% minimum rate less the 9% effective rate, or 6%, applied to jurisdictional GloBE income of 10 billion yen to give 600 million yen. 900 million yen is tax the subsidiary has already borne locally, and 1.5 billion yen is the total at the minimum rate without deducting tax already paid. The minimum rate is 15% (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x16","dom":"contract","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"株式譲渡契約（SPA）の補償条項に、損害額500万円のバスケット（基準額）を定めた。買主が被った表明保証違反による損害が800万円のとき、デダクタブル型（控除型）とティッピング型（初日型）で売主に請求できる額の組合せとして正しいのはどれか。","en":"A share purchase agreement (SPA) indemnity clause sets a basket of 5 million yen. If the buyer's loss from a breach of representations and warranties is 8 million yen, which pair correctly gives the amounts claimable from the seller under a deductible basket and a tipping basket?"},"choices":[{"ja":"デダクタブル型は800万円、ティッピング型は300万円","en":"Deductible 8 million yen, tipping 3 million yen"},{"ja":"デダクタブル型は300万円、ティッピング型は800万円","en":"Deductible 3 million yen, tipping 8 million yen"},{"ja":"デダクタブル型は500万円、ティッピング型は800万円","en":"Deductible 5 million yen, tipping 8 million yen"},{"ja":"デダクタブル型もティッピング型も300万円","en":"Both deductible and tipping 3 million yen"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"デダクタブル型は損害が基準額を超えた部分だけを補償するため、800−500＝300万円となる。ティッピング型は損害が基準額を超えると、最初の1円から全額を補償するため、800万円となる。基準額以下の少額の請求を排除する点は共通で、超えたときの範囲が異なる。","en":"A deductible basket covers only the part of the loss above the threshold, so 8 - 5 = 3 million yen. A tipping basket covers the whole loss from the first yen once the threshold is exceeded, so 8 million yen. Both screen out small claims below the threshold and differ in the scope once it is exceeded."}},
{"id":"s16x17","dom":"contract","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"M&Aで買主が表明保証保険（R&W保険）を利用する主な利点として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"What is the most appropriate main advantage for a buyer using representations and warranties insurance (R&W insurance) in M&A?"},"choices":[{"ja":"売主の資力や補償の上限に頼らず、表明保証違反による損害を保険で填補でき、売主の補償負担を抑えて交渉を進めやすい","en":"Losses from breaches can be covered by insurance without relying on the seller's means or indemnity cap, which eases negotiation by limiting the seller's indemnity burden"},{"ja":"保険料は売主が負担する定めが法律で義務づけられており、買主の費用負担がゼロになる","en":"The law requires the seller to bear the premium, so the buyer's cost is zero"},{"ja":"デューデリジェンスで判明した問題や、買主が契約前から知っていた違反も含め、すべての損害が例外なく保険の対象になる","en":"All losses are insured without exception, including problems found in due diligence and breaches the buyer knew of before signing"},{"ja":"表明保証の内容を契約書から削除でき、売主は一切の責任を負わなくなるため、買主は事実の確認を省略できる","en":"The representations and warranties can be removed from the contract and the seller bears no liability at all, so the buyer can skip verifying the facts"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"R&W保険は、表明保証違反の損害を保険会社が填補するため、売主の信用力や補償上限への依存が減り、売主は補償負担を抑えられる。既知の問題や、DDで判明した事項は通常免責となる。保険料の負担者は契約で決まり、法律で売主負担とされているわけではない。","en":"R&W insurance has the insurer cover losses from breaches, reducing reliance on the seller's creditworthiness and indemnity cap and limiting the seller's burden. Known issues and matters found in due diligence are usually excluded. Who pays the premium is set by contract, not by law."}},
{"id":"s16x18","dom":"contract","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"M&Aの基本合意書（LOI）で、一般に法的拘束力を持たせる条項として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which clause in an M&A letter of intent (LOI) is most appropriately given legally binding force as a general rule?"},"choices":[{"ja":"基本合意書に記載した譲渡価格で、必ず株式を売却しなければならない義務","en":"An obligation to sell the shares without fail at the price stated in the LOI"},{"ja":"一定期間、他の買主候補との交渉を行わない独占交渉義務","en":"An exclusivity obligation not to negotiate with other potential buyers for a set period"},{"ja":"デューデリジェンスの結果にかかわらず、最終契約を締結しなければならない義務","en":"An obligation to conclude the definitive agreement regardless of the due diligence results"},{"ja":"買収後も対象会社の従業員の雇用条件を変更してはならないという義務","en":"An obligation not to change the target's employees' terms of employment after the acquisition"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"基本合意書で拘束力を持たせるのは、独占交渉、秘密保持、費用負担、準拠法・管轄などの手続的な条項が一般的である。譲渡価格や最終契約の締結は、デューデリジェンスの結果を踏まえて決まるため、拘束力を持たせないのが通常である。","en":"Procedural clauses such as exclusivity, confidentiality, cost allocation and governing law and jurisdiction are generally made binding in an LOI. The transfer price and entry into the definitive agreement depend on due diligence results, so they are normally not binding."}},
{"id":"s16x19","dom":"contract","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"A社は、B社の特定事業（多数の取引先との継続的契約を含む）を買い取る。事業譲渡の方式で進める場合に、会社分割や合併と比べて特に手間がかかる点として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Company A will buy a specific business of Company B, which includes continuing contracts with many counterparties. If done as a business transfer, which point is most notably burdensome compared with a corporate split or merger?"},"choices":[{"ja":"契約上の地位の移転に取引先ごとの個別の承諾が必要で、承諾が得られない契約は承継されない","en":"Moving each contractual position requires the individual consent of each counterparty, and a contract without consent does not transfer"},{"ja":"債権者保護手続として、すべての債権者への個別の催告と官報公告が法律上必ず必要になる","en":"The law always requires individual notice to all creditors and a public notice in the official gazette as creditor protection procedures"},{"ja":"株主総会の特別決議が買主と売主の双方で必ず必要となり、省略できる場合が一切ない","en":"A special resolution of shareholders is always required at both buyer and seller, with no case in which it can be omitted"},{"ja":"譲渡する事業の資産や負債の範囲を当事者が自由には選べず、すべてを一括して承継しなければならない","en":"The parties cannot freely choose which assets and liabilities of the business to transfer and must take everything over as a whole"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"事業譲渡は特定承継であり、契約上の地位の移転には取引先の承諾、債務の引受けには債権者の同意が個別に要る。承諾が得られない契約は承継されない。承継範囲を選べるのは事業譲渡の利点で、債権者異議手続は合併や会社分割で必要になる手続である。","en":"A business transfer is a succession of individual items: moving a contractual position needs the counterparty's consent and assuming a debt needs the creditor's consent. Contracts without consent do not transfer. Being able to choose what to transfer is an advantage of this route, and creditor objection procedures belong to mergers and corporate splits."}},
{"id":"s16x20","dom":"contract","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"システム開発契約で、ベンダーの損害賠償責任の上限を『受領した対価の総額』と定める条項について、利用者側が交渉で求めるべき修正として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"For a system development contract clause capping the vendor's liability at the total fees received, which amendment is most appropriate for the user to seek in negotiation?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ベンダーの故意・重大な過失による損害や、情報漏えいによる損害は、上限の対象外とする例外を設ける","en":"Add exceptions removing damage from the vendor's intent or gross negligence and damage from information leaks from the cap"},{"ja":"ベンダーの責任を契約書に明記した軽微な不具合に限定し、重大な不具合は賠償の対象外にする","en":"Limit the vendor's liability to minor defects specified in the contract and exclude serious defects from compensation"},{"ja":"責任の上限額を撤廃し、損害の種類や原因を問わず、実際に生じたすべての損害を無制限に賠償させるべきである","en":"Abolish the cap and make the vendor pay without limit for all damage actually incurred, whatever its type or cause, as the proper approach"},{"ja":"利用者が負う責任にも同額の上限を設け、利用者側の責任はすべて上限の対象とする","en":"Set a cap of the same amount on the user's own liability and subject all of the user's liability to the cap"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"責任上限条項は予見しにくい巨額の賠償を避ける合理性があるが、故意・重大な過失や情報漏えいなど、重い損害まで上限で切ると、利用者の実損を回収できない。これらを上限の例外とする交渉が実務で一般的である。上限の全面撤廃は、受け入れられにくい。","en":"A liability cap is reasonable to avoid unforeseeable huge claims, but if it also cuts off serious harm such as intent, gross negligence or information leaks, the user cannot recover real losses. Negotiating these as exceptions to the cap is common practice. Abolishing the cap entirely is hard to get accepted."}},
{"id":"s16x21","dom":"contract","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"2020年4月施行の民法改正で、売買の目的物が契約の内容に適合しない場合の売主の責任を表す用語として採用されたのはどれか。","en":"Which term was adopted in the Civil Code amendment effective April 2020 for a seller's liability when the goods sold do not conform to the contract?"},"choices":[{"ja":"使用者責任（従業員の不法行為に対する責任）","en":"Employer's vicarious liability (for an employee's tort)"},{"ja":"製造物責任（製造業者に課される無過失責任）","en":"Product liability (strict liability imposed on manufacturers)"},{"ja":"契約不適合責任（債務不履行責任の一種）","en":"Liability for non-conformity to the contract (a form of liability for default)"},{"ja":"瑕疵担保責任（隠れた瑕疵を要件とする法定責任）","en":"Warranty liability for latent defects (a statutory liability requiring a hidden defect)"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"改正民法は、売主の責任を、契約の内容に適合しない目的物を引き渡した債務不履行責任として整理し、契約不適合責任と呼ぶ。買主は追完請求、代金減額請求、損害賠償請求、解除ができる。改正前の瑕疵担保責任は法定責任とされ、隠れた瑕疵を要件としていた。","en":"The amended Civil Code treats the seller's liability as liability for default in delivering goods that do not conform to the contract and calls it liability for non-conformity. The buyer may demand cure, demand a price reduction, claim damages or cancel. The earlier warranty against latent defects was a statutory liability that required a hidden defect."}},
{"id":"s16x22","dom":"contract","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"請負契約で、請負人の工場が火災で全焼し、納品が不可能になったことが確定した。注文者が契約を解除する手続として、民法上最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Under a contract for work, the contractor's factory burned down and delivery has become definitively impossible. Which procedure for the client to terminate the contract is most appropriate under the Civil Code?"},"choices":[{"ja":"履行が不能でも、相当の期間を定めて履行を催告し、期間内に履行がなかったときに限り解除できる","en":"Even if performance is impossible, the client can terminate only after demanding performance within a reasonable period and no performance occurs"},{"ja":"請負人に帰責事由がある場合に限り解除でき、不可抗力による履行不能では解除できない","en":"The client can terminate only if the contractor is at fault, and cannot terminate for impossibility caused by force majeure"},{"ja":"解除には裁判所の判決が必要で、判決が確定するまで注文者は代金の支払を停止できない","en":"Termination requires a court judgment, and the client cannot suspend payment until the judgment becomes final"},{"ja":"履行が不能なので、相当の期間を定めた催告をせずに、直ちに契約を解除できる","en":"Because performance is impossible, the client can terminate immediately without a demand setting a reasonable period"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"債務の全部の履行が不能であれば、催告なしで直ちに解除できる。2020年施行の改正民法では、解除に債務者の帰責事由は要らず、不可抗力による不能でも解除できる。催告が必要なのは、履行が可能な遅滞の場合である。解除に裁判所の判決は不要で、意思表示で足りる。","en":"If performance of the whole obligation is impossible, the client can terminate at once without a demand. Under the Civil Code amended in 2020, termination does not require fault of the obligor, so even impossibility from force majeure allows it. A demand is needed for delay where performance is still possible. No court judgment is required; a declaration of intent suffices."}},
{"id":"s16x23","dom":"corplaw","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"株式会社の株主総会における特別決議の成立要件として、会社法の原則どおりのものはどれか。","en":"Which sets out the requirements for a special resolution at a general meeting of shareholders of a stock company, as provided by the Companies Act in principle?"},"choices":[{"ja":"定足数は議決権の過半数（定款で完全に排除可）、決議は出席株主の議決権の過半数の賛成で足りる","en":"Quorum of a majority of the voting rights (fully excludable by the articles), and approval by a majority of the voting rights of those present suffices"},{"ja":"定足数は設けず、決議は議決権を行使できる株主の半数以上であって、その議決権の3分の2以上の賛成が必要","en":"No quorum is set, and approval by at least half of the shareholders entitled to vote holding two thirds or more of their voting rights"},{"ja":"定足数は議決権の過半数（定款で3分の1以上に変更可）、決議は出席株主の議決権の3分の2以上の賛成","en":"Quorum of a majority of the voting rights (changeable by the articles to one third or more), and approval by two thirds or more of the voting rights of those present"},{"ja":"定足数は総株主の過半数、決議は総株主の半数以上であって、総株主の議決権の4分の3以上の賛成","en":"Quorum of a majority of all shareholders, and approval by at least half of all shareholders holding three quarters or more of all voting rights"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"特別決議は、議決権を行使できる株主の議決権の過半数（定款で3分の1以上まで引下げ可）を有する株主の出席を定足数とし、出席株主の議決権の3分の2以上の賛成を要する。過半数の賛成で足りるのは普通決議、半数以上かつ4分の3以上の賛成は一部の非公開会社の特別事項に限られる。","en":"A special resolution requires a quorum of shareholders holding a majority of the voting rights of those entitled to vote (reducible by the articles to one third) and approval by two thirds or more of the voting rights present. A majority suffices for an ordinary resolution, and the half-and-three-quarters test is limited to certain special matters of non-public companies."}},
{"id":"s16x24","dom":"corplaw","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"A社（純資産1,000億円）がB社を吸収合併し、B社株主に交付する対価の帳簿価額の合計は150億円である。A社側の手続として、会社法の原則どおりのものはどれか。","en":"Company A (net assets of 100 billion yen) absorbs Company B in a merger, and the total book value of consideration delivered to B's shareholders is 15 billion yen. Which describes Company A's procedure as provided by the Companies Act in principle?"},"choices":[{"ja":"対価が純資産の10%以下の場合に限り、存続会社の株主総会の承認決議を省略できる","en":"The surviving company's shareholder approval resolution can be omitted only when consideration is 10% or less of net assets"},{"ja":"対価が存続会社の純資産の20%以下の簡易合併にあたり、A社の株主総会の承認決議を原則省略できる","en":"This is a simplified merger, with consideration at 20% or less of the surviving company's net assets, so A's shareholder approval resolution can in principle be omitted"},{"ja":"合併対価の額にかかわらず、存続会社であるA社の株主総会の特別決議が必ず必要となり、省略は認められない","en":"Regardless of the amount of consideration, a special resolution of the shareholders of A as surviving company is always required and omission is not permitted"},{"ja":"簡易合併では、存続会社の株主総会と取締役会の双方の承認決議をともに省略できる","en":"In a simplified merger, both the shareholders' meeting and the board approval resolutions of the surviving company can be omitted"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"吸収合併の対価の帳簿価額が存続会社の純資産の20%（5分の1）以下なら簡易合併となり、存続会社の株主総会決議を原則省略できる。本件は150億円÷1,000億円＝15%で該当する。ただし一定数の反対通知があれば決議が必要で、10%という基準はない。取締役会の承認は省略できない。","en":"If the book value of consideration is 20% (one fifth) or less of the surviving company's net assets, the merger is simplified and the surviving company's shareholder resolution can in principle be omitted. Here 15 billion / 100 billion = 15% qualifies. A resolution is still required if enough objections are notified, there is no 10% test, and board approval cannot be omitted."}},
{"id":"s16x25","dom":"corplaw","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"TOBの結果、買付者が対象会社の議決権の92%を取得した。残りの少数株主に現金を交付して退出させる手続のうち、対象会社の株主総会の決議を経ずに行えるものはどれか。","en":"After a tender offer the bidder holds 92% of the target's voting rights. Which procedure for cashing out the remaining minority shareholders can be carried out without a resolution of the target's general meeting?"},"choices":[{"ja":"全部取得条項付種類株式の取得（定款を変更して株式の内容を改めたうえで行う）","en":"Acquisition of all-cash-out class shares (carried out after amending the articles to change the terms of the shares)"},{"ja":"株式併合による端数株式の処理（併合の割合を定めて少数株主の持株を端数にする）","en":"Handling of fractional shares through a share consolidation (setting a ratio that reduces minority holdings to fractions)"},{"ja":"事業の全部の譲受け（対象会社の事業を現金で買い取り、対象会社を清算する）","en":"Acquisition of the whole business (buying the target's business for cash and liquidating the target)"},{"ja":"特別支配株主による株式等売渡請求（対象会社の取締役会の承認を得て行う）","en":"A demand for sale of shares by a special controlling shareholder (made with the approval of the target's board)"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"議決権の90%以上を持つ特別支配株主は、対象会社の取締役会の承認を得て、他の株主全員に株式の売渡しを請求できる。この手続は株主総会の決議を要しない。全部取得条項付種類株式の取得と株式併合は、株主総会の特別決議が必要である。","en":"A special controlling shareholder holding 90% or more of the voting rights can, with the approval of the target's board, demand that all other shareholders sell their shares. This procedure needs no general meeting resolution. Acquiring all-cash-out class shares and a share consolidation both require a special resolution of the general meeting."}},
{"id":"s16x26","dom":"corplaw","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"取締役Xが所有する土地を、取締役会設置会社である自社が買い取る。会社法上必要な手続として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"A board-managed company will buy land owned by its director X. Which is the most appropriate procedure required under the Companies Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取締役会で土地に関する重要な事実を開示して承認を受け、取引後に遅滞なく重要な事実を報告する","en":"Disclose the material facts about the land to the board and obtain approval, then report the material facts to the board without delay after the transaction"},{"ja":"取引価格が時価であれば承認は不要で、取引の事実を決算時に監査役へ報告すれば足りる","en":"If the price is fair market value, no approval is needed and it suffices to report the transaction to the auditor at the closing of the accounts"},{"ja":"代表取締役が単独で承認すれば足り、他の取締役の同意も取締役会の決議も必要ない","en":"Approval by the representative director alone is sufficient, with no consent of other directors and no board resolution needed"},{"ja":"株主総会の特別決議で承認を受ければ足り、取締役会の承認も取引後の報告もいずれも必要ないものとされる","en":"Approval by a special resolution of shareholders suffices, and neither board approval nor a post-transaction report is needed"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"取締役が自己のために会社と直接取引をする利益相反取引は、取締役会設置会社では、取締役会で重要な事実を開示して承認を受け、取引後に遅滞なく重要な事実を報告する。取引価格が時価でも承認は省略できない。代表取締役の単独判断や総会の特別決議では足りない。","en":"A conflict-of-interest transaction in which a director deals directly with the company for the director's own account requires, at a board-managed company, disclosure of material facts to the board, approval, and a report of the material facts without delay after the transaction. Fair-value pricing does not excuse approval, and a representative director's sole decision or a special shareholder resolution is not enough."}},
{"id":"s16x27","dom":"corplaw","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"最終事業年度の末日の貸借対照表で、その他資本剰余金が20億円、その他利益剰余金が80億円、自己株式の帳簿価額が10億円であった。のれんや繰延資産の調整、期末後の変動、臨時決算は考えないとき、分配可能額はいくらか。","en":"On the balance sheet at the end of the last fiscal year, other capital surplus was 2 billion yen, other retained earnings 8 billion yen and treasury shares at book value 1 billion yen. Ignoring goodwill and deferred asset adjustments, post-year-end changes and interim accounts, what is the distributable amount?"},"choices":[{"ja":"90億円","en":"9 billion yen"},{"ja":"80億円","en":"8 billion yen"},{"ja":"110億円","en":"11 billion yen"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"10 billion yen"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"分配可能額は、剰余金（その他資本剰余金＋その他利益剰余金＝100億円）から自己株式の帳簿価額10億円を差し引いて、90億円となる。100億円は自己株式を控除していない金額、110億円は自己株式を足す符号の誤りである。資本金と準備金は剰余金に含まれない。","en":"The distributable amount is surplus (other capital surplus plus other retained earnings = 10 billion yen) less the book value of treasury shares of 1 billion yen, or 9 billion yen. 10 billion does not deduct treasury shares, and 11 billion adds them by mistake. Stated capital and reserves are not part of surplus."}},
{"id":"s16x28","dom":"corplaw","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"株式の譲渡制限がない公開会社が、会社法上必ず設置しなければならない機関はどれか。","en":"Which organ must a public company, whose shares have no transfer restrictions, establish under the Companies Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取締役会","en":"A board of directors"},{"ja":"指名委員会等","en":"Nomination, audit and compensation committees"},{"ja":"監査役会","en":"A board of company auditors"},{"ja":"会計監査人","en":"An accounting auditor"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"公開会社は、取締役会の設置が義務づけられている。監査役会や会計監査人は、大会社など一定の会社だけが必須で、監査役会に代えて監査等委員会や指名委員会等を選ぶこともできる。社外取締役の設置義務も、有価証券報告書提出会社である監査役会設置の大会社に限られる。","en":"A public company must have a board of directors. A board of company auditors and an accounting auditor are required only for certain companies such as large companies, and an audit and supervisory committee or committees can be chosen instead of the auditor board. The outside director requirement is also limited to large companies with an auditor board that file securities reports."}},
{"id":"s16x29","dom":"corplaw","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"上場会社の株主が、議決権の2%を1年前から保有している。この株主が単独で行使できる権利として、会社法上正しいのはどれか（取締役会設置会社）。","en":"A shareholder of a listed company has held 2% of the voting rights for one year. Which right can this shareholder exercise alone under the Companies Act (board-managed company)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"株主総会の議題・議案を提出する株主提案権","en":"The shareholder proposal right to submit agenda items and proposals for the general meeting"},{"ja":"取締役に対して株主総会の招集を求める請求","en":"A demand that the directors convene a general meeting of shareholders"},{"ja":"株主総会で否決された取締役の解任を求める訴えの提起","en":"Filing an action seeking removal of a director after the general meeting voted down the removal"},{"ja":"会社の会計帳簿とその資料の閲覧・謄写を求める請求","en":"A request to inspect and copy the company's accounting books and related materials"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"取締役会設置会社の株主提案権は、総株主の議決権の1%以上または300個以上を、6か月前から保有する株主が行使できる。2%はこれを満たす。会計帳簿の閲覧請求、総会の招集請求、取締役の解任の訴えは、いずれも議決権の3%以上が必要で、2%では足りない（2026年10月時点）。","en":"At a board-managed company, the shareholder proposal right can be exercised by a shareholder holding 1% or more of all voting rights, or 300 or more votes, for six months. 2% satisfies this. Requests to inspect accounting books, to convene a meeting and an action to remove a director each need 3% or more of voting rights, which 2% does not meet (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x30","dom":"compliance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"財務報告に係る内部統制（J-SOX）の評価で、業務プロセスを評価する重要な事業拠点を選定するときの一般的な目安はどれか。","en":"In evaluating internal control over financial reporting (J-SOX), what is the general guideline for selecting significant business locations whose business processes are evaluated?"},"choices":[{"ja":"連結ベースの売上高等の金額が高い拠点から合算し、全体のおおむね3分の2に達するまでの拠点","en":"Locations, taken in descending order of sales and similar amounts on a consolidated basis, until they reach roughly two thirds of the total"},{"ja":"連結子会社のうち、親会社が議決権の過半数を保有しているすべての拠点","en":"All locations of consolidated subsidiaries in which the parent holds a majority of the voting rights"},{"ja":"連結ベースの利益を稼ぎ出している拠点のうち、利益額が最も大きい上位3拠点のみ","en":"Only the top three locations by profit among those earning consolidated profit"},{"ja":"連結ベースの売上高等の金額が高い拠点から順に合算し、全体の95%に達するまでのすべての拠点","en":"Locations, taken in descending order of sales and similar amounts on a consolidated basis, until they reach 95% of the total"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"実施基準では、売上高等の金額が高い拠点から合算して連結ベースの売上高等のおおむね3分の2に達するまでの拠点を、重要な事業拠点の目安とする。その他の拠点は、重要性の高い業務プロセスがあれば追加して評価する。95%や過半数保有の全拠点は目安ではない。","en":"The implementation standards use locations taken in descending order of sales and similar amounts until they reach roughly two thirds of the consolidated total as a guide to significant business locations. Other locations are added if they have highly significant processes. 95% or all majority-owned locations are not the guide."}},
{"id":"s16x31","dom":"compliance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"内部監査部門（3線の第3線）の独立性を確保するために最も重要なのはどれか。","en":"What is most important for securing the independence of the internal audit function (the third line of the three lines model)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"内部監査担当者の人事評価を、監査対象部門の管理職が行い、現場との信頼関係を重視すること","en":"Having managers of the audited departments evaluate the internal auditors' performance, emphasizing trust with the field"},{"ja":"取締役会や監査役（会）へ直接報告する経路を持ち、監査対象部門や経営陣の指揮命令を受けないこと","en":"Having a reporting line directly to the board and the auditors, and not taking direction from the audited business units or executive management"},{"ja":"監査対象の事業部門の責任者が内部監査部門長を兼務し、現場の実態を最もよく把握した体制にすること","en":"Having the head of an audited business unit also serve as head of internal audit, so the setup understands operations best"},{"ja":"内部監査の年間計画と監査結果を、監査対象の事業部門の責任者があらかじめ承認する運用にすること","en":"Having the head of the audited business unit approve in advance the annual audit plan and the audit results"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"第3線の内部監査は、第1線の事業部門や第2線の管理部門から独立して、保証と助言を提供する。独立性の鍵は、取締役会や監査役（会）への機能的な報告ラインと、対象部門から指揮や評価を受けない体制である。対象部門による承認や評価は独立性を損なう。","en":"Internal audit as the third line provides assurance and advice independently of the first-line business units and the second-line control functions. The key is a functional reporting line to the board and auditors and freedom from direction or evaluation by audited units. Approval or evaluation by audited units undermines independence."}},
{"id":"s16x32","dom":"compliance","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"公益通報者保護法（2022年6月施行の改正）で、内部通報に対応する体制の整備が義務づけられる事業者はどれか。","en":"Under the Whistleblower Protection Act (amendment effective June 2022), which businesses are obliged to put in place a system for handling internal reports?"},"choices":[{"ja":"常時使用する労働者の数が100人を超える事業者","en":"Businesses that regularly employ more than 100 workers"},{"ja":"常時使用する労働者の数が300人を超える事業者","en":"Businesses that regularly employ more than 300 workers"},{"ja":"常時使用する労働者の数が50人を超える事業者","en":"Businesses that regularly employ more than 50 workers"},{"ja":"金融商品取引所に株式を上場している事業者のみ","en":"Only businesses whose shares are listed on a financial instruments exchange"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"改正公益通報者保護法は、常時使用する労働者が300人を超える事業者に、通報の窓口設置や調査、是正措置などの体制整備を義務づけ、300人以下の事業者は努力義務とした。上場会社に限る規定ではなく、資本金の額も要件ではない（2026年10月時点）。","en":"The amended Whistleblower Protection Act obliges businesses regularly employing more than 300 workers to establish a system including a reporting contact, investigation and corrective measures, while those with 300 or fewer have a duty to make efforts. It is not limited to listed companies and capital is not a criterion (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x33","dom":"compliance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"不正のトライアングルの3要素のうち、職務分掌や承認手続などの内部統制の整備が、最も直接に低減するのはどれか。","en":"Of the three elements of the fraud triangle, which does the establishment of internal controls such as segregation of duties and approval procedures reduce most directly?"},"choices":[{"ja":"機会","en":"Opportunity"},{"ja":"不正が発覚した後の処分の重さ","en":"The severity of punishment after fraud is discovered"},{"ja":"姿勢・正当化","en":"Attitude or rationalization"},{"ja":"動機・プレッシャー","en":"Motive or pressure"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"不正のトライアングルは、動機・プレッシャー、機会、姿勢・正当化の3つで、内部統制は不正を実行できる機会を減らす働きをする。職務分掌や承認、アクセス制限で、1人で不正を実行し隠せる状況をなくす。動機や正当化には、目標設定や企業文化の面からの対応が必要になる。","en":"The fraud triangle has three elements: motive or pressure, opportunity, and attitude or rationalization. Internal controls reduce the opportunity to commit fraud, using segregation of duties, approvals and access limits to remove situations where one person can commit and hide it. Motive and rationalization call for responses through goal setting and corporate culture."}},
{"id":"s16x34","dom":"compliance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"上場会社で、経営陣の関与が疑われる会計不正が発覚した。調査の信頼性を確保する体制として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"At a listed company, an accounting fraud has come to light in which management involvement is suspected. Which structure best secures the credibility of the investigation?"},"choices":[{"ja":"疑いのある経営陣自身が調査を指揮し、調査の結果は取引所への報告以外の開示を行わない","en":"Have the suspected management lead the investigation itself and make no disclosure of the results other than a report to the exchange"},{"ja":"経理部門の部長を委員長とする社内調査委員会を設け、経営陣の関与は調査の対象から除く","en":"Set up an internal investigation committee chaired by the head of the accounting department and exclude management's involvement from the scope"},{"ja":"顧問弁護士と監査法人から非公式に意見を聴き、調査の報告書は作成せず口頭の報告だけにとどめておく","en":"Informally hear opinions from the company's retained lawyer and the audit firm, and limit reporting to oral communication with no written report"},{"ja":"経営陣から独立した弁護士や会計士で構成する第三者委員会を設け、調査結果と再発防止策を開示する","en":"Set up a third-party committee of lawyers and CPAs independent of management, and disclose in principle the investigation findings and recurrence prevention measures"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"経営陣の関与が疑われる場合、社内や顧問弁護士による調査では独立性に疑問が残る。経営陣から独立した専門家による第三者委員会（日弁連ガイドラインが示す形）が調査し、結果と再発防止策を開示することが、投資家の信頼回復に必要である。","en":"When management involvement is suspected, an internal investigation or one by the retained lawyer leaves doubts about independence. A third-party committee of experts independent of management (the form shown in the Japan Federation of Bar Associations guidelines) should investigate and disclose findings and recurrence prevention measures to restore investor trust."}},
{"id":"s16x35","dom":"compliance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本企業の従業員が、海外で外国の公務員に営業上の便宜を得る目的で金銭を渡した。不正競争防止法上の取扱いとして、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"An employee of a Japanese company paid money abroad to a foreign public official to obtain a business advantage. Which is the most appropriate treatment under the Unfair Competition Prevention Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"現地の慣習として行われているものであれば、金額や目的にかかわらず犯罪にならない","en":"If it is done as a local custom, it is not a crime regardless of the amount or purpose"},{"ja":"従業員個人が処罰されうるほか、両罰規定により法人も罰金（上限10億円）の対象となりうる","en":"The employee may be punished personally, and under the dual liability provision the company too may face a fine (up to 1 billion yen)"},{"ja":"行為地が日本国外なので、日本の法律は適用されず、法人にも罰則は科されない","en":"Because the act took place outside Japan, Japanese law does not apply and no penalty is imposed on the company either"},{"ja":"処罰の対象は従業員個人に限られ、法人は従業員の個人的な行為として一切責任を負うことはない","en":"Only the individual employee is punishable, and the company bears no responsibility for the employee's personal act"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"不正競争防止法は、外国公務員への不正の利益供与を禁じ、日本国民による国外での行為も処罰対象とする。個人に加え、両罰規定により法人にも最大10億円の罰金が科されうる（2026年10月時点）。現地の慣習は抗弁にならず、海外での行為だから適用されないわけでもない。","en":"The Unfair Competition Prevention Act prohibits improper benefits to foreign public officials and also punishes acts abroad by Japanese nationals. Besides the individual, the dual liability provision can impose a fine of up to 1 billion yen on the company (as of October 2026). Local custom is no defense, and acting abroad does not take the act outside the law."}},
{"id":"s16x36","dom":"compliance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"個人データの漏えいが発生し、不正の目的をもって行われたおそれがある場合に、個人情報保護法で求められる個人情報保護委員会への報告の組合せとして正しいのはどれか。","en":"When personal data is leaked and the leak may have been carried out with a wrongful purpose, which pairing of reports to the Personal Information Protection Commission is correct under the Act on the Protection of Personal Information?"},"choices":[{"ja":"速報は24時間以内、確報は7日以内に行う","en":"A preliminary report within 24 hours and a final report within 7 days"},{"ja":"速報は不要で、確報のみを30日以内に行えばよい","en":"No preliminary report is needed, and only a final report within 30 days suffices"},{"ja":"速報は知った時から30日以内、確報は60日以内に行い、不正の目的の有無は問わない","en":"A preliminary report within 30 days of becoming aware and a final report within 60 days, whether or not there was a wrongful purpose"},{"ja":"速報は知った時から速やかに（概ね3〜5日以内）、確報は60日以内に行う","en":"A preliminary report promptly after becoming aware (about 3 to 5 days), and a final report within 60 days"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"報告対象事態を知ったら、速やかに（概ね3〜5日以内）速報を行い、確報は原則30日以内、不正の目的をもって行われたおそれがある事態では60日以内に行う。速報を省いて確報だけにはできない。24時間や7日といった期限は法令に定められていない（2026年10月時点）。","en":"On learning of a reportable incident, a preliminary report is made promptly (about 3 to 5 days) and a final report within 30 days in principle, or 60 days where a wrongful purpose is possible. The preliminary report cannot be skipped, and deadlines of 24 hours or 7 days are not set by law (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x37","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"2021年改訂のコーポレートガバナンス・コードが、東証プライム市場の上場会社に求める独立社外取締役の選任の水準はどれか。","en":"What level of independent outside directors does the Corporate Governance Code, as revised in 2021, ask of companies listed on the Tokyo Stock Exchange Prime Market?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取締役の少なくとも3分の1以上（必要と考える場合は過半数）を独立社外取締役とする","en":"At least one third of the directors (a majority if considered necessary) are independent outside directors"},{"ja":"取締役の過半数を独立社外取締役とすることが、すべてのプライム上場会社に義務づけられる","en":"A majority of the directors must be independent outside directors, mandatory for every Prime company"},{"ja":"独立社外取締役は2名以上であれば足り、取締役の総数に対する割合の定めはない","en":"Two or more independent outside directors suffices, with no ratio to the total number of directors"},{"ja":"取締役の4分の1以上（必要と考える場合は3分の1）を独立社外取締役とする","en":"At least one quarter of the directors (one third if considered necessary) are independent outside directors"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"2021年改訂のコードは、プライム市場の上場会社に、独立社外取締役を少なくとも3分の1以上選任するよう求め（必要と考える場合は過半数）、他の市場では2名以上としている。過半数は必要と考える場合の水準で、4分の1は基準にない。","en":"The Code as revised in 2021 asks Prime Market companies to appoint independent outside directors making up at least one third of the board (a majority if considered necessary), and two or more for other markets. A majority is the level where considered necessary, and one quarter is not a benchmark."}},
{"id":"s16x38","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"コーポレートガバナンス・コードが、政策保有株式を保有する上場会社に求めている対応として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate response the Corporate Governance Code asks of listed companies that hold strategic cross-shareholdings?"},"choices":[{"ja":"議決権は保有先の経営陣の提案に必ず賛成する方針で行使し、反対した場合に限ってその理由を株主に向けて開示する","en":"Always exercise voting rights in favor of the investee management's proposals, and disclose reasons to shareholders only when voting against"},{"ja":"保有比率の上限を法令で10%と定め、超過分は直ちに売却して、売却の実績のみを開示する","en":"Set a legal ceiling of 10% on holdings, sell the excess immediately, and disclose only the sales results"},{"ja":"取引関係の維持が目的であれば検証や開示を省略でき、議決権の行使に関する方針も不要とする","en":"If the purpose is to maintain business relationships, verification and disclosure can be skipped, and no policy on exercising voting rights is needed"},{"ja":"毎年、取締役会で個別銘柄ごとに保有目的や便益・リスクが資本コストに見合うかを検証し、内容を開示する","en":"Verify each year at the board, stock by stock, whether the purpose, benefits and risks of holding meet the cost of capital, and disclose the content"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"コードは、政策保有株式について、保有に関する方針の開示に加え、毎年、取締役会で個別銘柄の保有目的や便益・リスクが資本コストに見合うかを具体的に精査して保有の適否を検証し、その内容の開示を求める。議決権行使は、保有先の企業価値の向上に資するかを基準に判断する。","en":"For strategic cross-shareholdings, the Code asks companies to disclose their policy, and each year to examine at the board, stock by stock, whether the purpose, benefits and risks meet the cost of capital, verify whether to hold, and disclose that content. Voting is judged on whether it contributes to the investee's corporate value."}},
{"id":"s16x39","dom":"governance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"上場会社の経営陣が参加するMBOで、少数株主の利益を守る公正性担保措置として、経済産業省『公正なM&Aの在り方に関する指針』（2019年）が有効とするものとして最も適切な組合せはどれか。","en":"In an MBO of a listed company in which management participates, which combination is most appropriate as fairness-assuring measures protecting minority shareholders, as endorsed by the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry's 2019 Fair M&A Guidelines?"},"choices":[{"ja":"買付価格を過去の市場株価の平均に固定し、プレミアムの水準については一切検討せず、取締役会の議論も省略すること","en":"Fixing the offer price at the average of past market prices and giving no consideration to the level of premium and skipping board discussion"},{"ja":"独立した特別委員会の設置、独立した第三者算定機関の算定書の取得、マジョリティ・オブ・マイノリティ条件の設定","en":"An independent special committee, a valuation report from an independent third-party valuer, and a majority-of-minority condition"},{"ja":"経営陣が選んだ社内取締役のみによる取締役会決議、買付者が依頼した算定機関の算定書の取得、買付価格の事後的な開示","en":"A board resolution by only the inside directors chosen by management, a valuation report from a valuer engaged by the bidder, and after-the-fact disclosure of the offer price"},{"ja":"TOBの買付期間を法定の最短期間に設定し、買付価格の算定根拠は一切開示せず、対抗提案の機会も設けないこと","en":"Setting the tender offer period at the statutory minimum and disclosing no basis for the price and allowing no opportunity for competing offers"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"指針は、特別委員会の設置、独立した第三者算定機関の算定書、マジョリティ・オブ・マイノリティ条件、他の買収者による対抗提案の機会の確保（マーケットチェック）などを、公正性担保措置として挙げる。経営陣に依存した判断や、価格決定過程の秘匿は、利益相反の弊害を高める。","en":"The guidelines list fairness-assuring measures such as a special committee, a valuation report from an independent third-party valuer, a majority-of-minority condition and securing opportunities for competing bids by other acquirers (market check). Decisions dependent on management and a concealed pricing process increase the harm of conflicts of interest."}},
{"id":"s16x40","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"経済産業省『企業買収における行動指針』（2023年）が示す、買収提案を受けた取締役会の基本姿勢として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"Which is the most appropriate basic stance for a board that receives a takeover proposal, as set out in the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry's 2023 Takeover Guidelines?"},"choices":[{"ja":"提案価格が現在の株価を上回れば、買収後の経営方針や従業員への影響にかかわらず受け入れるべきである","en":"If the proposed price exceeds the current share price, accept it regardless of post-acquisition management policy or impact on employees"},{"ja":"同意のない買収提案は敵対的と位置づけ、提案の内容を検討せずにすべて拒絶するのが原則である","en":"Treat unsolicited proposals as hostile and in principle reject all of them without considering their content"},{"ja":"企業価値と株主共同の利益の観点から、真摯な買収提案には誠実に検討し、正当な理由なく検討を拒まない","en":"From the standpoint of corporate value and shareholders' common interests, consider bona fide proposals in good faith and not refuse consideration without legitimate reason"},{"ja":"取締役会は経営陣の地位の維持を最優先して、買収防衛策を平時から導入しておくべきである","en":"The board should give top priority to preserving management's positions and adopt takeover defenses in ordinary times"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"指針は、真摯な買収提案に対し、取締役会が企業価値と株主共同の利益の観点から誠実に検討し、正当な理由なく議論や交渉を拒まないよう求める。同意の有無で一律に拒絶したり、経営陣の保身を目的に防衛策を使ったり、株価プレミアムだけで受け入れたりするのは適切でない。","en":"The guidelines ask the board to consider bona fide proposals in good faith from the standpoint of corporate value and shareholders' common interests and not to refuse discussion or negotiation without legitimate reason. Rejecting all proposals lacking consent, using defenses to protect management, or accepting merely for the share price premium is inappropriate."}},
{"id":"s16x41","dom":"governance","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"アクティビスト株主が、大幅な増配と自社株買いを要求した。取締役会は、成長投資の機会が豊富で、資本コストを上回るリターンが見込めると判断している。対応として最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"An activist shareholder demands a large dividend increase and share buybacks. The board judges that growth investment opportunities are plentiful and expects returns above the cost of capital. Which response is the most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営の独立性を守るため対話の要請はすべて断り、株主総会で提案を否決できるよう議決権の確保に全力で注力していく","en":"To protect management's independence, decline every request for dialogue and devote full effort to securing the votes needed to defeat the proposal at the general meeting"},{"ja":"資本配分の方針を、資本コストとリターンの見通しに基づき具体的に説明し、株主との対話で提案を実質的に検討する","en":"Explain the capital allocation policy concretely on the basis of the cost of capital and expected returns, and substantively consider the proposal in dialogue with shareholders"},{"ja":"株価が下がらないよう、要求どおりに最大限の増配と自社株買いを実施して、成長投資は凍結する","en":"Carry out the maximum dividend increase and buyback as demanded to prevent a share price fall, and freeze growth investment"},{"ja":"成長投資の計画は見直さず、要求の一部を受け入れて足元の配当だけを増やすことで、対立を避ける","en":"Avoid confrontation by accepting part of the demand and raising only the near-term dividend without revising the growth investment plan"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"資本コストを上回る投資機会があるなら、内部留保による投資は株主価値を高める。取締役会は、資本配分の考え方とリターンの見通しを根拠付きで説明し、対話を通じて提案を検討するのが適切である。対話の拒否や対立回避のための場当たり的な増配は、説明責任を果たさない。","en":"If investments earning above the cost of capital are available, retaining earnings to invest raises shareholder value. The board should explain its capital allocation thinking and return outlook with supporting grounds and consider the proposal through dialogue. Refusing dialogue or making an ad hoc dividend increase to avoid conflict does not meet the duty to explain."}},
{"id":"s16x42","dom":"governance","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"中期経営計画の期間中のROICや株主総利回り（TSR）の達成度に応じて、期末に交付される株式の数が変わる株式報酬はどれか。","en":"Which share-based compensation changes the number of shares delivered at the end of the period according to attainment of ROIC or total shareholder return (TSR) over the medium-term plan period?"},"choices":[{"ja":"固定の月額報酬（毎月一定の金銭を支給する報酬）","en":"Fixed monthly compensation (cash paid in a set amount each month)"},{"ja":"譲渡制限付株式（勤務の継続のみを条件に譲渡制限が解除される型）","en":"Restricted stock (a type whose transfer restrictions lift on continued service alone)"},{"ja":"パフォーマンス・シェア（業績連動型株式報酬）","en":"Performance shares (performance-linked share compensation)"},{"ja":"ストックオプション（あらかじめ定めた権利行使価格で株式を取得できる権利）","en":"Stock options (rights to acquire shares at a predetermined exercise price)"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"パフォーマンス・シェアは、ROICやTSRなどの業績目標の達成度に応じて、交付する株式数が変わる。勤務の継続のみを条件とする譲渡制限付株式は、業績にかかわらず株数が固定である。ストックオプションは行使価格での取得権で、固定の月額報酬は業績との連動がない。","en":"Performance shares vary the number of shares delivered according to attainment of performance targets such as ROIC or TSR. Restricted stock conditioned only on continued service has a fixed share count regardless of results. Stock options are rights to buy at an exercise price, and fixed monthly pay has no link to performance."}},
{"id":"s16x43","dom":"governance","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"監査等委員会設置会社の監査等委員会の構成として、会社法の定めに合うものはどれか。","en":"Which composition of the audit and supervisory committee of a company with an audit and supervisory committee conforms to the Companies Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"2人以上の取締役で組織し、その過半数が社外取締役である","en":"Two or more directors, a majority of whom are outside directors"},{"ja":"3人以上の取締役で組織し、その過半数が社外取締役である","en":"Three or more directors, a majority of whom are outside directors"},{"ja":"3人以上の取締役で組織し、その全員が社外取締役である","en":"Three or more directors, all of whom are outside directors"},{"ja":"3人以上の監査役で組織し、その半数以上が社外監査役である","en":"Three or more company auditors, at least half of whom are outside auditors"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"監査等委員会は、3人以上の取締役で組織し、その過半数を社外取締役としなければならない。監査等委員はいずれも取締役である点が監査役会との違いで、半数以上が社外監査役となるのは監査役会である。全員が社外取締役である必要はない。","en":"The audit and supervisory committee must consist of three or more directors, a majority of whom are outside directors. Its members are all directors, unlike an auditor board, where at least half must be outside auditors. They need not all be outside directors."}},
{"id":"s16x44","dom":"disclosure","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"非上場会社が、多数の者に対し、発行価額の総額8,000万円の株式を新たに募集する。金融商品取引法上の開示手続として正しいのはどれか。","en":"An unlisted company will newly offer shares with a total issue value of 80 million yen to many persons. Which disclosure procedure is correct under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"総額が1億円未満であっても、多数の者に対する募集にあたるため有価証券届出書の提出が必要になる","en":"A securities registration statement is required even though the total is under 100 million yen, because the offering is to many persons"},{"ja":"総額が1億円未満のため、有価証券届出書も有価証券通知書もいずれも提出する必要がなくなる","en":"Neither a securities registration statement nor a securities notification is required, because the total is under 100 million yen"},{"ja":"総額が5億円未満であれば、有価証券届出書は不要となり、有価証券通知書のみ提出が必要になる","en":"If the total is under 500 million yen, a registration statement is not required and only a securities notification is needed"},{"ja":"総額が1億円未満で有価証券届出書は不要だが、1,000万円超のため有価証券通知書が必要になる","en":"A securities registration statement is not required because the total is under 100 million yen, but a securities notification must be filed because it exceeds 10 million yen"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"有価証券の募集は、発行価額の総額が1億円以上のとき有価証券届出書を提出する。1億円未満なら届出は不要だが、1,000万円を超える場合は内閣総理大臣への有価証券通知書の提出が必要である。5億円という基準はなく、総額が小さくても通知書が要ることがある（2026年10月時点）。","en":"A securities registration statement is filed when the total issue value is 100 million yen or more. Below that, registration is not required, but a securities notification to the Prime Minister is needed if the total exceeds 10 million yen. There is no 500 million yen threshold, and a notification can be required even for a small total (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x45","dom":"disclosure","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"投資家が上場会社の株券等の保有割合を4.9%から6.2%へ買い増した。当初は報告義務がなかったとき、金融商品取引法上の大量保有報告書の提出期限として正しいのはどれか。","en":"An investor increased its holding in a listed company's shares from 4.9% to 6.2%, having had no reporting duty at first. Which is the correct deadline for filing a large shareholding report under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"保有割合が5%を超えた日から5営業日以内","en":"Within five business days from the day the holding exceeded 5%"},{"ja":"その事業年度の終了後3か月以内","en":"Within three months after the end of that fiscal year"},{"ja":"保有割合が5%を超えた日から10営業日以内","en":"Within ten business days from the day the holding exceeded 5%"},{"ja":"保有割合が5%を超えた日の属する月の翌月末まで","en":"By the end of the month following the month in which the holding exceeded 5%"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"上場株券等の保有割合が5%を超えたら、その日から5営業日以内に大量保有報告書を提出する。その後、保有割合が1%以上増減したときも5営業日以内に変更報告書を提出する。10営業日、月末、事業年度末といった期限は定められていない（2026年10月時点）。","en":"Once the holding in listed shares exceeds 5%, a large shareholding report is filed within five business days from that day. A change report is also due within five business days when the holding later rises or falls by 1% or more. Deadlines of ten business days, month-end or fiscal year-end are not provided (as of October 2026)."}},
{"id":"s16x46","dom":"disclosure","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"インサイダー取引規制で、上場会社の重要事実が『公表』されたものとして、取引が解禁される典型的な方法はどれか。","en":"Under the insider trading rules, which is a typical way for a listed company's material fact to count as 'made public' so that trading becomes permissible?"},"choices":[{"ja":"自社のウェブサイトのトップページに、プレスリリースとして掲載されること","en":"Its being posted as a press release on the company's own website"},{"ja":"特定の報道機関1社に、取材への対応として内容を詳しく伝えること","en":"Its being conveyed to a single news organization in response to an interview"},{"ja":"取引所の適時開示情報伝達システム（TDnet）で開示されること","en":"Its content being disclosed on the exchange's timely disclosure system (TDnet)"},{"ja":"社内のすべての役員と従業員に、重要事実がメールで周知されること","en":"The material fact being made known to all officers and employees within the company"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"重要事実が『公表』されたとされるのは、取引所の適時開示（TDnet）で開示されたとき、または2以上の報道機関に公開してから12時間が経過したときなどである。自社サイトへの掲載、報道機関1社への説明、社内周知だけでは公表にならず、取引を続けるとインサイダー取引に当たりうる。","en":"A material fact is regarded as made public when disclosed through the exchange's timely disclosure (TDnet), or when 12 hours have passed since it was made available to two or more news organizations. Posting on the company's website, telling one news outlet or internal circulation alone is not publication, and trading may still be insider trading."}},
{"id":"s16x47","dom":"disclosure","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"IR担当者が、守秘義務を負う約束のないアナリストとの個別面談で、未公表の次期業績の見通しを誤って伝えてしまった。フェア・ディスクロージャー・ルールの下で求められる対応として、最も適切なのはどれか。","en":"An investor relations officer mistakenly disclosed an unpublished earnings outlook in a one-on-one meeting with an analyst who has made no commitment to confidentiality. Which is the most appropriate response under the fair disclosure rule?"},"choices":[{"ja":"同じ内容を、次回の決算説明会で全投資家に説明するときまで待てば足りる","en":"It is enough to wait until the same content is explained to all investors at the next results briefing"},{"ja":"意図しない伝達だったため、規制の対象外であり、特に対応をとる必要は一切ない","en":"As the communication was unintentional, it is outside the regulation and no particular action is needed"},{"ja":"伝達した相手の氏名と内容を、翌営業日に金融庁へ個別に報告すれば足りる","en":"It is enough to report the recipient's name and the content to the Financial Services Agency individually on the next business day"},{"ja":"意図せず伝達した場合は、速やかに同じ情報を公表して、情報の格差を解消する","en":"Where the communication was unintentional, promptly make the same information public to remove the information gap"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"FDルールは、取引関係者に重要情報を伝達するときは同時に公表することを求め、意図しない伝達の場合は速やかに公表することを求める。報告書の提出や次回の決算説明会まで待つ対応では、一部の者だけが情報を先に得る格差が続くため、規制の趣旨に反する。","en":"The fair disclosure rule requires material information communicated to a relevant person to be made public at the same time, and promptly where the communication was unintentional. Filing a report or waiting for the next results briefing leaves some parties with the information first, contrary to the rule's purpose."}},
{"id":"s16x48","dom":"disclosure","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"有価証券報告書の虚偽記載が公表され、株価が下落した。公表日前1年以内に株式を取得して保有を続けていた投資家が、金融商品取引法21条の2に基づき発行会社へ損害賠償を請求する場合の特徴として、正しいのはどれか。","en":"A false statement in a securities report was made public and the share price fell. For an investor who acquired shares within one year before the announcement and kept holding them, which is a correct feature of a damages claim against the issuer under Article 21-2 of the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act?"},"choices":[{"ja":"株価の下落額がすべて損害と認められ、市場全体の下落や他の要因による株価の変動も一切控除されない","en":"The whole fall in the share price is recognized as damage, and market-wide declines or other factors are not deducted"},{"ja":"公表日前1か月の平均市場価格と公表日後1か月の平均市場価格との差額を、損害額とできる規定がある","en":"A provision lets the amount of damage be taken as the average market price in the month before the announcement less the average market price in the month after it"},{"ja":"責任を負うのは役員個人に限られ、発行会社自身は金融商品取引法上の損害賠償責任を一切負わない","en":"Only the individual officers are liable, and the issuer itself bears no liability for damages under the Act"},{"ja":"請求できるのは募集の際に新株を取得した投資家に限られ、市場で取得した投資家は一切請求できない","en":"Only investors who acquired new shares in the offering can claim, and those who bought on the market cannot"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"金商法21条の2は、虚偽記載の公表日前1年以内に取得して保有を続ける者について、公表日前後各1か月間の平均市場価格の差額を損害額とすることを認める。流通市場で取得した投資家も請求でき、責任を負う主体は発行会社である。他の要因による下落が立証されれば、賠償額は減額される。","en":"Article 21-2 allows an investor who acquired shares within one year before the announcement of a false statement and kept holding them to take as damage the difference between average market prices in the month before and the month after. Market purchasers can claim, and the issuer is the liable party. Proof that other factors caused part of the fall reduces the award."}},
{"id":"s16x49","dom":"disclosure","diff":1,"q":{"ja":"3月決算の上場会社が、有価証券報告書を提出しなければならない期限はいつか。","en":"By when must a listed company with a March fiscal year-end file its securities report?"},"choices":[{"ja":"事業年度終了後3か月以内（6月末まで）","en":"Within three months after the end of the fiscal year (by the end of June)"},{"ja":"事業年度終了後6か月以内（9月末まで）","en":"Within six months after the end of the fiscal year (by the end of September)"},{"ja":"事業年度終了後2か月以内（5月末まで）","en":"Within two months after the end of the fiscal year (by the end of May)"},{"ja":"事業年度終了後45日以内（5月中旬まで）","en":"Within 45 days after the end of the fiscal year (by mid-May)"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"有価証券報告書は、事業年度終了後3か月以内に提出する。3月決算なら6月末が期限で、定時株主総会の時期に合わせて提出される。45日以内は決算短信の開示の目安であり、有価証券報告書の期限ではない。","en":"A securities report is filed within three months after the fiscal year ends. For a March year-end the deadline is the end of June, and filings are timed with the ordinary general meeting. The 45-day figure is a guide for disclosing the earnings summary, not the deadline for the securities report."}},
{"id":"s16x50","dom":"disclosure","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"2023年3月期以降の有価証券報告書で新設された『サステナビリティに関する考え方及び取組』欄には、どの4つの項目の記載が求められるか。","en":"Which four items must be described in the 'Approach to and initiatives on sustainability' section newly added to securities reports from the fiscal year ending March 2023?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ガバナンス、戦略、リスク管理、指標及び目標","en":"Governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics and targets"},{"ja":"環境、社会、人権、腐敗防止の4つの分野","en":"The four areas of environment, society, human rights and anti-corruption"},{"ja":"資金調達、配当政策、役員報酬、監査の状況","en":"Funding, dividend policy, officer compensation and status of audits"},{"ja":"経営理念、事業の内容、設備の状況、株式の状況","en":"Management philosophy, business description, status of facilities and status of shares"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"新設欄では、TCFDの枠組みに沿って、ガバナンス、戦略、リスク管理、指標及び目標の4項目を記載する。人的資本については人材育成方針や社内環境整備方針を戦略に、測定可能な指標と目標を指標及び目標に記載する。ほかの選択肢は従来から別の欄で記載する内容である。","en":"The new section follows the TCFD framework and describes four items: governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics and targets. For human capital, talent development and workplace environment policies go under strategy, and measurable metrics and targets go under metrics and targets. The other choices are content traditionally described in other sections."}}
);
