  _quiz.push(
{"id":"s17x01","dom":"deal","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"株式譲渡契約で、目標運転資本（ペッグ）を30億円と定め、クロージング時点の実際の運転資本との差を価格で精算する条件にした。クロージング時の運転資本が27億円だった場合、株式価格はどう調整されるか。","en":"A share purchase agreement sets a target working capital (peg) of JPY 3.0 billion and settles the price on the gap to actual working capital at closing. If actual working capital at closing is JPY 2.7 billion, how is the share price adjusted?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ペッグとの差の3億円が基本価格に上乗せされ、買い手の支払額が増える","en":"The JPY 300 million gap is added to the base price, so the buyer pays more"},{"ja":"運転資本の差は調整されず、合意した基本価格のまま確定する","en":"The working capital gap is ignored and the agreed base price stays fixed"},{"ja":"実際の運転資本27億円の全額が、基本価格から控除される","en":"The full JPY 2.7 billion of actual working capital is deducted from the base price"},{"ja":"ペッグを3億円下回るため、基本価格から3億円が減額される","en":"Actual working capital is JPY 300 million below the peg, so the base price is reduced by JPY 300 million"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"運転資本調整は、事業の継続に必要な標準水準（ペッグ）と実際の差額を価格に反映する仕組みである。27億円はペッグを3億円下回り、買い手が不足分を補う負担を負うため、その分を減額する。上乗せや無調整では、不足の負担が買い手に残る。","en":"A working capital adjustment reflects the gap between actual working capital and the normal level the business needs (the peg). At JPY 2.7 billion it falls JPY 300 million short, so the buyer would have to fund the shortfall and the price is cut by that amount. Adding the gap or ignoring it leaves the burden with the buyer."}},
{"id":"s17x02","dom":"deal","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"上場のA社が、非上場のB社を株式交換で完全子会社にする。A社はB社株式を保有していない。B社の一部の株主にだけ現金を対価として支払う案が出た。税制適格株式交換の観点で、正しい説明はどれか。","en":"Listed company A will make unlisted company B a wholly owned subsidiary through a share exchange. A holds no B shares. A proposal would pay cash as consideration to some B shareholders only. Which statement is correct from the standpoint of a tax-qualified share exchange?"},"choices":[{"ja":"対価のうち株式の割合が過半であれば、一部が現金でも適格のまま扱われる","en":"As long as shares make up more than half of the consideration, a partly cash deal is still treated as qualified"},{"ja":"完全子会社化であれば、対価の種類にかかわらず、常に適格株式交換として扱われる","en":"Any deal that creates a wholly owned subsidiary is always treated as a qualified share exchange, whatever the consideration"},{"ja":"現金対価は事業関連性の要件にのみ影響し、株主や子会社の課税関係は変わらない","en":"Cash consideration affects only the business-relatedness test and leaves the tax position of shareholders and the subsidiary unchanged"},{"ja":"対価に現金が含まれると、金銭等不交付の要件を原則として満たさず、非適格となる","en":"Including cash generally breaks the no-cash-consideration requirement, so the exchange becomes non-qualified"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"税制適格の株式交換は、対価が親会社株式のみで金銭等が交付されないことが要件の一つである。一部の株主へ現金を払うと原則この要件を欠いて非適格となり、子会社資産の時価評価や株主の譲渡損益課税が生じうる。株式が過半という基準はない。","en":"A tax-qualified share exchange requires that the consideration be only parent company shares, with no cash or other assets. Paying cash to some shareholders generally breaks that rule and makes the deal non-qualified, which can trigger fair-value revaluation of the subsidiary's assets and capital gains tax for shareholders. There is no majority-of-shares test."}},
{"id":"s17x03","dom":"deal","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ロックドボックス方式で、3月末の貸借対照表日を基準日とする株式譲渡契約を結んだ。基準日後、クロージング前に、売り手が対象会社から3億円の配当を受け取っていたことが判明した。買い手が契約上主張すべきことはどれか。","en":"A share purchase agreement uses a locked-box mechanism with the end-of-March balance sheet date as the locked-box date. After that date and before closing, the seller received a JPY 300 million dividend from the target. What should the buyer assert under the contract?"},"choices":[{"ja":"基準日後の価値の流出（リーケージ）として、同額を価格から控除するか補償として請求する","en":"Treat it as leakage after the locked-box date and claim the same amount as a price reduction or indemnity"},{"ja":"ロックドボックス方式では価格が基準日の貸借対照表で固定されているので、基準日後の配当について買い手は何も請求できない","en":"A locked box fixes the price on the locked-box balance sheet, so the buyer cannot claim anything for dividends paid after the locked-box date"},{"ja":"クロージング時点の運転資本を再計算し、その差額で価格を精算し直す","en":"Recalculate working capital at closing and resettle the price on the difference"},{"ja":"配当は売り手の正当な権利なので、配当にかかる税金相当額だけを請求できる","en":"The dividend is the seller's right, so the buyer can claim only the tax on it"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"ロックドボックスは、基準日以降の損益を買い手に帰属させる代わりに、基準日後の配当などの価値の流出（リーケージ）を禁じ、発生時は同額を返還させる。運転資本の再精算はクロージング勘定方式の仕組みである。","en":"A locked box lets the buyer take the economics from the locked-box date, so leakage such as dividends after that date is prohibited and must be repaid in the same amount. Re-settling working capital at closing belongs to the completion accounts method, not the locked box."}},
{"id":"s17x04","dom":"deal","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"IFRSを適用するA社は、B社の買収で、2年後のEBITDAが目標を超えれば追加で20億円を支払う条件付対価を契約した。取得日の公正価値8億円を金融負債として認識したが、1年後に業績が好調で公正価値が14億円に増えた。この6億円の増加分の会計処理はどれか。","en":"IFRS reporter A agreed to pay an additional JPY 2.0 billion if B's EBITDA beats a target in two years, and recognized the acquisition-date fair value of JPY 800 million as a financial liability. A year later, strong performance raised the fair value to JPY 1.4 billion. How is the JPY 600 million increase accounted for?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取得原価に加算して、のれんを6億円増額する","en":"Add it to the cost of acquisition and increase goodwill by JPY 600 million"},{"ja":"その他の包括利益に計上し、純資産の部で繰り延べて処理する","en":"Record it in other comprehensive income and defer it within equity"},{"ja":"支払が確定するまで何も認識せず、注記で開示するだけにとどめる","en":"Recognize nothing until payment is certain and only disclose it in the notes"},{"ja":"公正価値の変動として純損益に認識し、のれんは修正しない","en":"Recognize the change in fair value in profit or loss and leave goodwill unchanged"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"IFRSでは、金融負債に分類した条件付対価は取得日の公正価値で取得対価に含め、以後の公正価値の変動は純損益に認識する。のれんは取得日の評価で確定しており、取得日時点の事実に関する新情報でない限り修正しない。取得原価を追加する処理は日本基準のものである。","en":"Under IFRS, contingent consideration classified as a financial liability is included in the consideration at its acquisition-date fair value, and later fair value changes go to profit or loss. Goodwill is fixed at the acquisition date and is not adjusted unless new information relates to facts at that date. Adding the increase to cost is the Japanese GAAP treatment."}},
{"id":"s17x05","dom":"deal","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"A社が株式取得でB社を500億円で買収した。B社の簿価純資産は300億円で、他の資産・負債の簿価は時価と等しい。取得原価配分で、簿価のない顧客関係を60億円と評価した。この無形資産に課税上の簿価はなく、実効税率は30%とする。のれんはいくらか。","en":"Company A acquired company B in a share deal for JPY 50.0 billion. B's book net assets are JPY 30.0 billion, and other assets and liabilities are at fair value. In the purchase price allocation, a customer relationship with no book value is valued at JPY 6.0 billion. It has no tax basis and the effective tax rate is 30%. What is goodwill?"},"choices":[{"ja":"140億円","en":"JPY 14.0 billion"},{"ja":"158億円","en":"JPY 15.8 billion"},{"ja":"200億円","en":"JPY 20.0 billion"},{"ja":"122億円","en":"JPY 12.2 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"顧客関係60億円には税務上の簿価がなく、差異に実効税率30%を掛けた18億円の繰延税金負債を認識する。識別可能純資産は300＋60−18＝342億円で、のれんは500−342＝158億円となる。繰延税金負債を無視すると140億円と過小になる。","en":"The JPY 6.0 billion customer relationship has no tax basis, so a deferred tax liability of 6.0 x 30% = JPY 1.8 billion is recognized. Identifiable net assets are 30.0 + 6.0 - 1.8 = JPY 34.2 billion, and goodwill is 50.0 - 34.2 = JPY 15.8 billion. Ignoring the deferred tax liability understates goodwill at JPY 14.0 billion."}},
{"id":"s17x06","dom":"deal","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"TOBの結果、A社は上場会社B社の総議決権の68%を取得した。残る少数株主を排除してB社を完全子会社化するため、株主総会で可決できる最も適切な手続はどれか。","en":"After a tender offer, A holds 68% of the total voting rights of listed company B. Which procedure that can be approved at B's shareholders' meeting is most suitable for squeezing out the remaining minority and making B a wholly owned subsidiary?"},"choices":[{"ja":"特別支配株主として、取締役会の承認を得たうえで株式等売渡請求を行い、少数株主の株式を一括して取得する","en":"As a special controlling shareholder, make a demand to sell shares with the board's approval and acquire all minority shares at once"},{"ja":"株主総会の普通決議で、会社が少数株主の全株式を金銭を対価として買い取る旨を決議する","en":"Pass an ordinary resolution at the shareholders' meeting for the company to buy all minority shares for cash"},{"ja":"株主総会の特別決議で株式併合を行い、端数となる少数株主の株式を金銭で処理する","en":"Carry out a share consolidation by special resolution and cash out the minority holdings that become fractions"},{"ja":"取締役会の決議のみで、少数株主の株式を一括して取得する","en":"Acquire the minority shares in one step by a board resolution alone"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"株式併合は株主総会の特別決議（出席議決権の3分の2以上）で行え、68%の議決権があれば可決できる。端数となる少数株主には金銭が支払われる。株式等売渡請求は総議決権の90%以上を持つ場合に限られるため、68%では使えない。","en":"A share consolidation needs a special resolution (two-thirds of votes present), which A can pass with 68% of the voting rights; minority holders receive cash for fractional shares. A demand to sell shares is available only to a holder of 90% or more of total voting rights, so it cannot be used at 68%."}},
{"id":"s17x07","dom":"deal","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"A社（既存のEBITDA 100億円、純有利子負債200億円）は、EBITDA 50億円のB社を株式取得で買収する。買収価格は400億円。融資銀行は、買収後の連結で純有利子負債/EBITDAを3.0倍以内に抑えることを条件とする。B社に有利子負債と現金はない。負債で調達できる上限額と、残りを自己資金や増資で賄う額の組合せはどれか。","en":"Company A (existing EBITDA JPY 10.0 billion, net debt JPY 20.0 billion) will acquire company B (EBITDA JPY 5.0 billion) for JPY 40.0 billion. The lender requires consolidated net debt/EBITDA of no more than 3.0x after the deal. B has no debt or cash. Which pair gives the maximum new debt and the remainder to be funded with cash or new equity?"},"choices":[{"ja":"負債400億円、自己資金・増資0円","en":"Debt JPY 40.0 billion, cash or equity zero"},{"ja":"負債100億円、自己資金・増資300億円","en":"Debt JPY 10.0 billion, cash or equity JPY 30.0 billion"},{"ja":"負債250億円、自己資金・増資150億円","en":"Debt JPY 25.0 billion, cash or equity JPY 15.0 billion"},{"ja":"負債150億円、自己資金・増資250億円","en":"Debt JPY 15.0 billion, cash or equity JPY 25.0 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"買収後の連結EBITDAは150億円で、許容される純有利子負債は3.0×150＝450億円。既存の200億円を引いた250億円が追加の借入余力で、残り150億円は自己資金か増資で賄う。A社だけのEBITDAで計算すると100億円と過小になる。","en":"Post-deal consolidated EBITDA is JPY 15.0 billion, so permitted net debt is 3.0 x 15.0 = JPY 45.0 billion. After deducting the existing JPY 20.0 billion, JPY 25.0 billion of new debt is available and the remaining JPY 15.0 billion comes from cash or equity. Using A's EBITDA alone understates the capacity at JPY 10.0 billion."}},
{"id":"s17x08","dom":"deal","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"A社（株価2,000円）がB社（株価1,500円）を株式交換で完全子会社化する。B社株主に市場株価の20%のプレミアムを付ける場合、B社株1株に対して交付するA社株式の数（交換比率）はいくつか。","en":"Company A (share price JPY 2,000) will acquire company B (share price JPY 1,500) in a share exchange. If B's shareholders get a 20% premium to market price, how many A shares are issued per B share (the exchange ratio)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"0.75株","en":"0.75 shares"},{"ja":"0.95株","en":"0.95 shares"},{"ja":"1.11株","en":"1.11 shares"},{"ja":"0.90株","en":"0.90 shares"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"B社株1株の評価額は1,500×1.2＝1,800円で、A社株価2,000円で割ると0.9株になる。プレミアムは比率ではなく評価額に掛ける。プレミアムを無視すると0.75株、割る向きを逆にすると約1.11株となり、いずれも誤りである。","en":"B's value per share is 1,500 x 1.2 = JPY 1,800, and dividing by A's price of JPY 2,000 gives 0.9 shares. The premium applies to the valuation, not to the ratio. Ignoring the premium gives 0.75 and inverting the division gives about 1.11, both wrong."}},
{"id":"s17x09","dom":"capalloc","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"当期純利益が200億円の会社が、配当60億円と自己株式の取得40億円を実施した。株主還元の水準を示す総還元性向と、配当性向の組合せはどれか。","en":"A company with net income of JPY 20.0 billion paid JPY 6.0 billion in dividends and bought back JPY 4.0 billion of its own shares. Which pair shows the total payout ratio and the dividend payout ratio?"},"choices":[{"ja":"総還元性向30%、配当性向50%","en":"Total payout 30%, dividend payout 50%"},{"ja":"総還元性向50%、配当性向30%","en":"Total payout 50%, dividend payout 30%"},{"ja":"総還元性向20%、配当性向30%","en":"Total payout 20%, dividend payout 30%"},{"ja":"総還元性向30%、配当性向20%","en":"Total payout 30%, dividend payout 20%"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"配当性向は配当60億÷純利益200億＝30%。総還元性向は配当と自己株式取得の合計100億÷200億＝50%である。自己株式取得だけを分子にすると20%となり、配当を含めない誤りになる。","en":"The dividend payout ratio is 6.0 / 20.0 = 30%. The total payout ratio is (6.0 + 4.0) / 20.0 = 50%, including both dividends and buybacks. Using only the buyback gives 20%, which leaves out dividends."}},
{"id":"s17x10","dom":"capalloc","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"PBRが0.7倍の会社のROEは5%、PERは14倍で、株主資本コストは8%と推計される。この会社の状況と、PBR改善の方向性として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"A company trades at a P/B of 0.7x with ROE of 5% and a P/E of 14x, and its cost of equity is estimated at 8%. Which description of its situation and the direction for improving P/B is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ROE5%が株主資本コスト8%に届いておらず、収益性と資本効率の引き上げを改善の中心に据える","en":"ROE of 5% is below the 8% cost of equity, so raising profitability and capital efficiency should be the core of the fix"},{"ja":"PERが14倍あるため市場評価は十分で、ROEを動かさなくても広報の強化だけでPBR1倍を回復できる","en":"A P/E of 14x already shows a sufficient market rating, so stronger publicity alone can restore a P/B of 1x without moving ROE"},{"ja":"ROEが資本コストを下回っていても、PBRは理論上1倍に収れんするので、改善策は不要である","en":"Even with ROE below the cost of capital, P/B converges to 1x in theory, so no action is needed"},{"ja":"PBR1倍割れは成長期待の低さを映すものでROEとは無関係なので、株式分割を行えば解消できる","en":"A P/B below 1x only reflects low growth expectations and is unrelated to ROE, so a stock split can fix it"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"PBR＝ROE×PERで、5%×14倍＝0.7倍。ROE5%は株主資本コスト8%を下回り、株主資本を使うほど価値が減る状態なので、ROEの改善が中心課題になる。ROEと無関係に株式分割やIR強化だけでPBRを1倍に戻すことはできない。","en":"P/B = ROE x P/E, so 5% x 14 = 0.7x. ROE of 5% is below the 8% cost of equity, meaning more equity employed destroys value, so improving ROE is the central task. A stock split or stronger IR cannot restore P/B to 1x on its own while ROE stays low."}},
{"id":"s17x11","dom":"capalloc","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある会社は取引先の上場株式（帳簿価額300億円）を持つ。配当利回りは1.2%で、取引関係による利益への貢献は明確でない。会社の加重平均資本コストは6%である。コーポレートガバナンス・コードの考え方に沿った最も適切な対応はどれか。","en":"A company holds listed shares of business partners with a book value of JPY 30.0 billion. The dividend yield is 1.2%, and the contribution to profit from the business relationship is unclear. The company's weighted average cost of capital is 6%. Which response best follows the Corporate Governance Code?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取引関係の維持が保有の目的である以上、便益と資本コストを比べる検証や縮減の検討は行わず、現在の保有を毎年そのまま継続する","en":"Because the purpose of holding is to maintain the business relationship, run no test of benefits against the cost of capital and no review of reductions, and keep the current positions unchanged every year"},{"ja":"便益とリスクを資本コストに照らして取締役会で検証し、見合わない銘柄は縮減して、資金を高リターンの投資や還元に回す","en":"Have the board test benefits and risks against the cost of capital, reduce holdings that do not pay off, and redeploy the funds into higher-return investments or shareholder returns"},{"ja":"配当利回りが預金金利を上回っていれば、保有は合理的と説明する","en":"Explain that holding is reasonable as long as the dividend yield beats deposit rates"},{"ja":"取引先との関係強化のため、相手にも自社株を持ってもらい、持ち合いを厚くする","en":"Deepen cross-holdings by asking the partners to buy shares of the company in return"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"コードの原則1-4は、取締役会が保有の便益とリスクが資本コストに見合うかを毎年精査し、乏しい銘柄は縮減することを求める。配当利回り1.2%は資本コスト6%に届かず、売却資金を高リターンの投資や還元に回す方が価値が高まる。預金金利との比較は基準にならない。","en":"Principle 1-4 of the Code asks the board to review annually whether the benefits and risks of each holding justify the cost of capital and to reduce weak holdings. A 1.2% yield falls short of the 6% cost of capital, and redeploying sale proceeds into higher-return uses adds more value. Comparison with deposit rates is not the test."}},
{"id":"s17x12","dom":"capalloc","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ROEが10%、配当性向が40%の会社が、増資も負債比率の変更もせず、現在の利益還元方針を続けて成長を賄う場合の持続可能な成長率はいくらか。","en":"A company with ROE of 10% and a dividend payout ratio of 40% will fund growth with no new equity and no change in leverage, keeping the current payout policy. What is its sustainable growth rate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"6%（ROE×内部留保率）","en":"6% (ROE x retention ratio)"},{"ja":"4%（ROEに配当性向を乗じた値）","en":"4% (ROE multiplied by the payout ratio)"},{"ja":"10%","en":"10%"},{"ja":"25%（ROE÷配当性向）","en":"25% (ROE divided by payout ratio)"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"持続可能成長率は、ROE×内部留保率で、10%×(1−0.4)＝6%。新たな外部資金を入れずに成長できる速度の目安である。ROEに配当性向を掛けた4%は、還元に回した側の割合を使った誤りである。","en":"The sustainable growth rate is ROE x retention ratio, so 10% x (1 - 0.4) = 6%. It indicates how fast the company can grow without new external funding. Multiplying ROE by the payout ratio gives 4%, which uses the share paid out rather than retained."}},
{"id":"s17x13","dom":"capalloc","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"会社法上の剰余金の配当を検討している。直近の貸借対照表は、資本準備金50億円、その他資本剰余金100億円、利益準備金20億円、その他利益剰余金50億円、自己株式の帳簿価額30億円である。他の調整項目はないものとして、分配可能額はいくらか。","en":"A company is considering a dividend under the Companies Act. Its latest balance sheet shows capital reserve JPY 5.0 billion, other capital surplus JPY 10.0 billion, legal retained earnings reserve JPY 2.0 billion, other retained earnings JPY 5.0 billion and treasury stock at book value of JPY 3.0 billion. With no other adjustments, what is the distributable amount?"},"choices":[{"ja":"150億円","en":"JPY 15.0 billion"},{"ja":"120億円","en":"JPY 12.0 billion"},{"ja":"220億円","en":"JPY 22.0 billion"},{"ja":"190億円","en":"JPY 19.0 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"剰余金はその他資本剰余金とその他利益剰余金の合計150億円で、資本準備金・利益準備金は含まれない。ここから自己株式の帳簿価額30億円を控除して、分配可能額は120億円となる。準備金も含めた220億円や、自己株式を引かない150億円は誤りである。","en":"Surplus is other capital surplus plus other retained earnings, JPY 15.0 billion; the capital reserve and legal reserve are excluded. Deducting treasury stock at book value of JPY 3.0 billion gives a distributable amount of JPY 12.0 billion. Including the reserves (22.0) or skipping the treasury stock deduction (15.0) is wrong."}},
{"id":"s17x14","dom":"capalloc","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"株主資本コストをCAPMで求める。リスクフリーレート1.0%、beta 1.0、市場リスクプレミアム5.0%である。時価ベースの資本構成は自己資本70%、有利子負債30%で、負債の税引前コストは2.0%、実効税率は30%である。WACCはいくらか。","en":"Cost of equity is estimated by CAPM: risk-free rate 1.0%, beta 1.0, market risk premium 5.0%. The market-value capital structure is 70% equity and 30% debt, pre-tax cost of debt is 2.0% and the effective tax rate is 30%. What is the WACC?"},"choices":[{"ja":"4.80%","en":"4.80%"},{"ja":"4.62%","en":"4.62%"},{"ja":"4.20%","en":"4.20%"},{"ja":"6.00%","en":"6.00%"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"株主資本コストは1.0＋1.0×5.0＝6.0%。WACC＝0.7×6.0%＋0.3×2.0%×(1−0.3)＝4.20＋0.42＝4.62%。税引前の負債コストをそのまま使うと4.80%になり、負債の節税効果を見落とす。","en":"Cost of equity is 1.0 + 1.0 x 5.0 = 6.0%. WACC = 0.7 x 6.0% + 0.3 x 2.0% x (1 - 0.3) = 4.20 + 0.42 = 4.62%. Using the pre-tax cost of debt gives 4.80% and misses the interest tax shield."}},
{"id":"s17x15","dom":"capalloc","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"利益が景気で大きく振れる素材メーカーが、配当政策を見直している。純利益は好況期に400億円、不況期に20億円と変動してきた。株主の安定志向も強い。最も適切な方針はどれか。","en":"A materials maker whose earnings swing with the economy is reviewing its dividend policy. Net income has ranged from JPY 40.0 billion in booms to JPY 2.0 billion in downturns, and its shareholders value stability. Which policy is most suitable?"},"choices":[{"ja":"配当性向を一律50%に固定し、利益の変動をそのまま配当に反映させる","en":"Fix the payout ratio at 50% and pass earnings swings straight through to dividends"},{"ja":"好況期の利益水準に合わせて高めの配当を設定し、不況期には借入を増やしてでも同じ配当の水準を毎期維持する","en":"Set a high dividend based on boom-time earnings and, in downturns, borrow more if necessary to maintain the same dividend level every period"},{"ja":"配当は行わず、利益はすべて内部留保として次の設備投資の原資にあてる","en":"Pay no dividend and retain all profit as a source of funds for the next capital investment"},{"ja":"普通配当は不況期の利益でも賄える水準に抑え、好況期の余剰は自己株式取得や特別配当で柔軟に還元する","en":"Hold the ordinary dividend at a level that downturn earnings can cover, and return boom-time surplus flexibly through buybacks or special dividends"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"利益変動が大きい会社は、普通配当の基準を不況期でも続けられる水準に置き、好況期の余剰は自己株式取得や特別配当で調整すると、減配による悪いシグナルを避けつつ資本効率を保てる。借入で配当を維持すると財務を傷め、性向固定では配当が乱高下する。","en":"A company with volatile earnings should anchor the ordinary dividend at a level it can sustain in a downturn and adjust boom-time surplus through buybacks or special dividends, avoiding the negative signal of a cut while keeping capital efficient. Borrowing to hold the dividend weakens the balance sheet, and a fixed payout ratio makes the dividend swing wildly."}},
{"id":"s17x16","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"初期投資100億円で、5年間にわたり毎年30億円のフリーキャッシュフローを生む設備投資案がある。割引率は8%で、年金現価係数（5年・8%）は3.993として、NPVに最も近い値はどれか。","en":"A capital project requires an initial outlay of JPY 10.0 billion and produces free cash flow of JPY 3.0 billion a year for five years. The discount rate is 8%, and the annuity factor (5 years, 8%) is 3.993. Which value is closest to the NPV?"},"choices":[{"ja":"+50.0億円","en":"+JPY 5.0 billion"},{"ja":"+119.8億円","en":"+JPY 11.98 billion"},{"ja":"+19.8億円","en":"+JPY 1.98 billion"},{"ja":"−19.8億円","en":"-JPY 1.98 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"現在価値は30億×3.993＝119.8億円で、初期投資100億円を引くとNPVは約+19.8億円になる。割り引かずに合計した+50億円は貨幣の時間価値を無視しており、119.8億円は初期投資の控除を忘れた値である。","en":"The present value is 3.0 x 3.993 = JPY 11.98 billion, and subtracting the JPY 10.0 billion outlay gives an NPV of about +JPY 1.98 billion. Summing undiscounted cash flows (+5.0 billion) ignores the time value of money, and 11.98 billion forgets to deduct the outlay."}},
{"id":"s17x17","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"投資予算が200億円に限られる。独立した3案の投資額とNPVは、X案が100億円で20億円、Y案が100億円で15億円、Z案が200億円で30億円である。NPVの合計を最大にする選択はどれか。","en":"The investment budget is capped at JPY 20.0 billion. Three independent projects have these outlays and NPVs: X costs JPY 10.0 billion with NPV 2.0 billion, Y costs 10.0 billion with NPV 1.5 billion, and Z costs 20.0 billion with NPV 3.0 billion. Which choice maximizes total NPV?"},"choices":[{"ja":"X案とY案を実行する（NPV合計35億円）","en":"Do X and Y (total NPV JPY 3.5 billion)"},{"ja":"NPVが最大のZ案だけを実行する（NPV合計30億円）","en":"Do only Z, the project with the largest NPV (total NPV JPY 3.0 billion)"},{"ja":"X案だけを実行し、残る予算は使わずに温存する（NPV合計20億円）","en":"Do only X and leave the rest of the budget unused (total NPV JPY 2.0 billion)"},{"ja":"3案をすべて実行する（NPV合計65億円）","en":"Do all three projects (total NPV JPY 6.5 billion)"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"予算内で実行できる組合せのうち、XとYの合計NPV35億円が最大で、Z単独の30億円を上回る。案件ごとにNPVが最大のZを選ぶと、組合せの最適解を逃す。3案すべての投資額は400億円で、予算を超える。","en":"Among combinations that fit the budget, X plus Y gives the largest total NPV of JPY 3.5 billion, above Z alone at 3.0 billion. Picking the single largest NPV misses the best combination under capital rationing. All three projects would cost JPY 40.0 billion and exceed the budget."}},
{"id":"s17x18","dom":"growth","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"新設備の導入により、ある年の増分EBITDAが20億円、減価償却費が10億円、運転資本の増加が2億円、実効税率が30%と見込まれる。この年の増分フリーキャッシュフロー（設備投資は除く）はいくらか。","en":"A new machine is expected to add EBITDA of JPY 2.0 billion in a given year, with depreciation of JPY 1.0 billion, a working capital increase of JPY 200 million, and a 30% effective tax rate. What is the incremental free cash flow for that year, excluding capital expenditure?"},"choices":[{"ja":"17億円","en":"JPY 1.7 billion"},{"ja":"15億円","en":"JPY 1.5 billion"},{"ja":"12億円","en":"JPY 1.2 billion"},{"ja":"7億円","en":"JPY 0.7 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"税金は(20−10)×30%＝3億円。FCF＝20−3−2＝15億円である。税引後営業利益7億円に減価償却費10億円を足し戻し、運転資本2億円を引いても同じになる。運転資本を無視すると17億円、償却費を足し戻さないと7億円で誤りである。","en":"Tax is (20 - 10) x 30% = 3, so FCF = 20 - 3 - 2 = 15 (in units of JPY 100 million). The same result comes from NOPAT of 7, plus depreciation of 10, less working capital of 2. Ignoring working capital gives 17, and not adding back depreciation gives 7, both wrong."}},
{"id":"s17x19","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"新規事業にすでに50億円を投じたが、成果は想定を下回っている。追加で30億円を投じれば事業を完成させて売却でき、その売却価値は現在価値で20億円と見込まれる。ほかに追加投資の便益はない。最も適切な判断はどれか。","en":"A company has already invested JPY 5.0 billion in a new business and results are below plan. An additional JPY 3.0 billion would complete the business and allow a sale worth JPY 2.0 billion in present value. There are no other benefits from further investment. What is the most appropriate decision?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50億円をすでに投じているので、ここで止めずに追加投資を行い、回収を目指す","en":"Invest further, because JPY 5.0 billion has already been spent, rather than stopping here, and aim to recover it"},{"ja":"追加投資の30億円は売却価値の20億円で一部が戻るので、差額の10億円だけを損失とみなして実行する","en":"Proceed, treating only the JPY 1.0 billion gap as a loss since the sale value would recover part of the extra JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"投下済みの50億円を含む合計80億円を取り戻せるまで、事業の継続を前提に追加投資を重ねる","en":"Keep investing on the premise of continuing the business until the total of JPY 8.0 billion including the sunk JPY 5.0 billion is recovered"},{"ja":"追加の30億円に対し回収は20億円なので、既に投じた50億円に関わらず追加投資は見送る","en":"Skip the extra investment: JPY 3.0 billion more only recovers JPY 2.0 billion, regardless of the JPY 5.0 billion already spent"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"すでに投じた50億円はサンクコストで、判断に含めない。追加の30億円で得られる回収は20億円なので、増分の価値は−10億円となり、見送るのが合理的である。投下済みの額を取り戻すために追加投資を続けると、損失が拡大する。","en":"The JPY 5.0 billion already spent is a sunk cost and should be excluded. The extra JPY 3.0 billion returns only JPY 2.0 billion, so the incremental value is -JPY 1.0 billion and declining is rational. Continuing to invest to recoup sunk money only enlarges the loss."}},
{"id":"s17x20","dom":"growth","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本の会社が、ベトナムの工場投資を評価している。キャッシュフローは現地通貨（ドン）建ての名目値で予測されている。現地の名目金利とインフレ率は、円より高い。割引計算で最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"A Japanese company is evaluating a factory investment in Vietnam. Cash flows are forecast in nominal terms in the local currency (dong). Local nominal interest rates and inflation are higher than in Japan. Which discounting approach is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ドン建ての名目キャッシュフローにはドンの名目割引率を使い、円換算するなら円のキャッシュフローに円の割引率を使う","en":"Use a dong nominal discount rate for nominal dong cash flows, or, if converting to yen, use a yen discount rate for the yen cash flows"},{"ja":"ドン建てのキャッシュフローを、金利が低く安全な円の割引率で割り引き、現地通貨の為替変動やインフレ率の差は計算に入れず無視する","en":"Discount the dong cash flows at the lower, safer yen rate and leave out local currency exchange rate movements and the inflation differential altogether"},{"ja":"国にかかわらず、割引率は日本国債の利回りに統一して、リスクは別に反映しない","en":"Use the Japanese government bond yield as the discount rate regardless of country and do not reflect risk separately"},{"ja":"ドン建てのキャッシュフローを実質値に直したうえで、ドンの名目割引率で割り引く","en":"Convert the dong cash flows to real terms and discount them at the dong nominal rate"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"キャッシュフローと割引率は、通貨と名目・実質の基準を揃える。ドンの名目CFにはドンの名目割引率、円換算するなら予想為替で換算した円CFに円の割引率を使う。高インフレ通貨のCFを円の低い割引率で割ると、価値を過大に評価する。","en":"Cash flows and discount rates must match in currency and in nominal versus real terms. Nominal dong cash flows take a dong nominal rate; if converted to yen at forecast exchange rates, use a yen rate. Discounting high-inflation-currency cash flows at a low yen rate overstates value."}},
{"id":"s17x21","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"3年前に承認した設備投資の事後評価（ポストオーディット）を行う。投資額は計画どおりだったが、売上は計画の80%にとどまり、承認時のNPVは計画上プラスだった。事後評価で最も重視すべきことはどれか。","en":"A post-audit is being done on a capital investment approved three years ago. The spend matched the plan, but sales are only 80% of plan, and the approved NPV was positive on paper. What should the post-audit emphasize most?"},"choices":[{"ja":"未達の責任を担当部門に帰属させることを最優先とし、原因の分析は省く","en":"Make assigning blame to the responsible department the top priority and skip the analysis of causes"},{"ja":"投資額はすでに支出済みで取り戻せないため、サンクコストとして事後評価は行わない","en":"Skip the evaluation because the money is already spent and is a sunk cost"},{"ja":"実績に合わせて計画の売上前提を書き換え、計画の達成度を100%として報告する","en":"Rewrite the sales assumption in the plan to match actuals and report 100% achievement of plan"},{"ja":"乖離の原因を需要・価格・コストなどに分解し、今後の投資案の前提と審査に反映する","en":"Break the gap down into demand, price and cost drivers and feed the findings into the assumptions and review of future proposals"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"事後評価の目的は学習で、乖離を需要・価格・コストなどに分解し、次の投資案の前提や審査に生かすことにある。実績に合わせて計画を書き換えると乖離が見えなくなり、責任追及だけでは前提を低く置く行動を招く。投下済みでも、将来の判断精度を高めるために行う。","en":"A post-audit exists to learn: decompose the gap into demand, price and cost, and use it to improve future assumptions and reviews. Rewriting the plan to match actuals hides the gap, and blame alone encourages low-balled assumptions. Spent money does not make the review pointless, because it sharpens future decisions."}},
{"id":"s17x22","dom":"growth","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"新モデルの発売で年間売上100億円を見込むが、そのうち30億円は既存モデルからの置き換えと見込まれる。両モデルの営業利益率はいずれも20%で、追加の固定費はない。新モデルの投資判断に使うべき年間の増分営業利益はいくらか。","en":"A new model is expected to bring JPY 10.0 billion of annual sales, of which JPY 3.0 billion would cannibalize the existing model. Both models earn a 20% operating margin and there are no extra fixed costs. What annual incremental operating profit should be used in the investment decision?"},"choices":[{"ja":"20億円","en":"JPY 2.0 billion"},{"ja":"6億円","en":"JPY 0.6 billion"},{"ja":"14億円","en":"JPY 1.4 billion"},{"ja":"26億円","en":"JPY 2.6 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"投資判断では増分のキャッシュフローだけを見る。新モデルの売上100億円から食い合い30億円を引いた70億円が純増分で、20%を掛けて14億円になる。食い合いを無視した20億円は効果を過大に見積もっている。","en":"Investment decisions should use incremental cash flow only. Sales of JPY 10.0 billion less JPY 3.0 billion of cannibalization leaves JPY 7.0 billion of net new sales, and 20% of that is JPY 1.4 billion. Ignoring cannibalization (2.0 billion) overstates the benefit."}},
{"id":"s17x23","dom":"risk","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"変動金利（TIBOR＋0.8%）で200億円を借りている会社が、金利上昇に備え、固定金利1.5%を支払いTIBORを受け取る金利スワップを同額で契約した。TIBORが3.0%に上昇した場合の実質的な調達コスト（年率）はいくらか。スワップと銀行借入以外のコストはないものとする。","en":"A company has borrowed JPY 20.0 billion at a floating rate of TIBOR + 0.8%. To guard against rising rates it entered an interest rate swap for the same amount, paying a fixed 1.5% and receiving TIBOR. If TIBOR rises to 3.0%, what is the effective annual funding cost? Assume no costs other than the loan and the swap."},"choices":[{"ja":"3.8%","en":"3.8%"},{"ja":"1.5%","en":"1.5%"},{"ja":"5.3%","en":"5.3%"},{"ja":"2.3%","en":"2.3%"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"銀行にはTIBOR＋0.8%を払い、スワップでTIBORを受け取り1.5%を払うため、TIBORが相殺されて実質1.5＋0.8＝2.3%に固定される。TIBORが動いても変わらない。ヘッジなしの3.8%や、スプレッドを忘れた1.5%は誤りである。","en":"The company pays TIBOR + 0.8% to the bank and, through the swap, receives TIBOR and pays 1.5%, so TIBOR cancels and the cost is fixed at 1.5 + 0.8 = 2.3% whatever TIBOR does. The unhedged 3.8% or a figure that drops the spread (1.5%) is wrong."}},
{"id":"s17x24","dom":"risk","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"売上の35%を占める主要顧客1社に、取引先から信用不安が指摘された。同社向けの売掛金は月商の2か月分にあたる。まず検討すべき対応はどれか。","en":"Credit concerns have been raised about a key customer that accounts for 35% of sales. Receivables from this customer equal two months of sales. Which response should be considered first?"},"choices":[{"ja":"与信限度額の再設定や取引信用保険、売掛債権の譲渡などで回収リスクを抑えつつ、顧客の分散を進める","en":"Contain collection risk through a reset credit limit, trade credit insurance or sale of receivables, while diversifying the customer base"},{"ja":"関係悪化を避けるため、条件は変えずに取引を拡大して、この顧客への売上の比率をさらに高める","en":"Expand business on unchanged terms to avoid straining the relationship, raising this customer's share of sales further"},{"ja":"回収が遅れた時点で貸倒引当金を計上すれば足りるので、与信限度の見直しや保険などの事前の対応は不要とする","en":"Treat advance steps such as revisiting credit limits or buying insurance as unnecessary, since a bad debt allowance can be booked once collection is delayed"},{"ja":"顧客の信用不安は財務情報では確認できないため、対応は営業部門の判断に任せる","en":"Leave the response to sales, since credit concerns cannot be checked from financial information"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"売上の集中と売掛金の大きさは、顧客が破綻したときの損失を大きくする。与信限度や保険・債権譲渡で回収リスクを移転・限定し、中長期には顧客分散を進めるのが基本である。取引を拡大すると集中は強まり、引当は損失の発生後に行うもので事前の対策にならない。","en":"Customer concentration and large receivables enlarge the loss if the customer fails. The basic approach is to transfer or limit collection risk through credit limits, insurance or receivable sales, and diversify over the medium term. Expanding business deepens concentration, and an allowance is booked after a loss, not a preventive step."}},
{"id":"s17x25","dom":"risk","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"工場の火災で生産が止まり、1日あたりの粗利益の損失は1.2億円と見込まれる。復旧まで15日かかる。事業中断（利益）保険は、最初の3日間を免責として補償せず、4日目以降を1日あたり損失額を上限に補償する。保険金はいくらか。","en":"A factory fire halts production, and gross profit lost is JPY 120 million a day. Recovery takes 15 days. The business interruption (profit) insurance excludes the first 3 days and covers day 4 onward, up to the daily loss. How much is the insurance payout?"},"choices":[{"ja":"18.0億円","en":"JPY 1.8 billion"},{"ja":"3.6億円","en":"JPY 0.36 billion"},{"ja":"14.4億円","en":"JPY 1.44 billion"},{"ja":"16.8億円","en":"JPY 1.68 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"補償対象は15日から免責の3日を引いた12日で、1.2億円×12＝14.4億円。免責を引かない18.0億円は条件を無視している。3.6億円は免責の3日分の損失で、補償されない部分である。16.8億円は免責を1日分しか見ていない。","en":"Coverage applies to 15 - 3 = 12 days, so 120 million x 12 = JPY 1.44 billion. Ignoring the waiting period (1.8 billion) disregards the terms, and 0.36 billion is the uncovered loss from the 3 waiting days. The 1.68 billion figure deducts only one waiting day."}},
{"id":"s17x26","dom":"risk","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"3か月後に受け取る予定のドル建て売上（実行がほぼ確実な予定取引）の為替変動を、為替予約でヘッジしている。期末に予約の時価評価損が3億円（税効果は考慮しない）となった。繰延ヘッジ会計の要件を満たす場合の処理はどれか。","en":"A company hedges a highly probable forecast dollar sale, due in three months, with a forward exchange contract. At period end the forward has a fair value loss of JPY 300 million (ignore tax effects). How is it treated if the deferral hedge accounting conditions are met?"},"choices":[{"ja":"評価損3億円を繰延ヘッジ損益として純資産の部に計上し、ヘッジ対象の売上が認識される期に損益へ振り替える","en":"Record the JPY 300 million loss as deferred hedge gains and losses in net assets and reclassify it to profit or loss in the period the hedged sale is recognized"},{"ja":"評価損3億円を当期の営業外費用として損益に計上し、ヘッジ対象の売上が認識される期にも特別な処理は行わない","en":"Recognize the JPY 300 million loss in current profit or loss as a non-operating expense and do nothing special in the period the hedged sale is recognized"},{"ja":"評価損は計上せず、予約の契約内容を注記で開示するだけにとどめる","en":"Recognize no loss and disclose only the contract terms of the forward in the notes"},{"ja":"評価損3億円を、売掛金の減額として直ちに処理する","en":"Treat the JPY 300 million loss immediately as a reduction of accounts receivable"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"繰延ヘッジ会計では、ヘッジ手段の評価差額を損益に出さず、純資産の部の繰延ヘッジ損益として繰り延べ、ヘッジ対象の損益が認識される期に損益へ振り替える。これでヘッジ手段とヘッジ対象の損益が同じ期にそろう。当期の損益に出すと期間がずれる。","en":"Under deferral hedge accounting, the valuation difference on the hedging instrument bypasses profit or loss, is held in net assets as deferred hedge gains and losses, and is reclassified when the hedged item affects profit or loss. This matches the periods of the hedge and the hedged item; booking it now mismatches them."}},
{"id":"s17x27","dom":"risk","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"営業部門で期末に売上計上が集中し、一部の取引では出荷前に売上が立てられていた。調査によると、部門長は予算未達なら降格との強い圧力を受け、売上の検収確認は担当者1人が単独で行っていた。担当者は『期末だけの一時的な処理で、翌月に戻せば問題ない』と考えていた。不正のトライアングルの『機会』にあたるものはどれか。","en":"Sales booked in a sales department were concentrated at period end, and some were recorded before shipment. The investigation found the department head was under strong pressure to meet budget or be demoted, and a single employee verified acceptance of sales alone. The employee believed it was only a temporary period-end step that could be reversed next month. Which element corresponds to 'opportunity' in the fraud triangle?"},"choices":[{"ja":"予算未達なら降格になるという、部門長にかかっていた非常に強い業績達成の圧力","en":"The very strong pressure to hit performance targets on the department head, who would be demoted if the budget was missed"},{"ja":"売上の検収確認を担当者1人が単独で行い、チェックする仕組みがなかったこと","en":"Acceptance of sales was verified by one employee alone, with no mechanism to check it"},{"ja":"『期末だけの一時的な処理で、翌月に戻せば問題ない』という担当者の考え方","en":"The employee's belief that it was a temporary period-end step that could be reversed next month"},{"ja":"売上計上が期末に集中していたという事実","en":"The fact that sales were concentrated at period end"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"不正の3要素は、動機（プレッシャー）、機会（統制の不備）、正当化である。検収確認を1人に任せ、牽制がないことが機会にあたる。降格の圧力は動機、翌月に戻せば問題ないという考えは正当化である。期末集中は兆候であって要素ではない。","en":"The three elements of fraud are motive (pressure), opportunity (control weakness) and rationalization. Leaving acceptance checks to one person with no check on them is the opportunity. The demotion pressure is the motive and the belief that it can be reversed is the rationalization; period-end concentration is a warning sign, not an element."}},
{"id":"s17x28","dom":"risk","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"営業利益が60億円、変動金利の借入が300億円で現在の借入利率は2.0%の会社がある。金利が1ポイント上昇した場合、インタレスト・カバレッジ・レシオ（営業利益÷支払利息、他の利息は無視）は、上昇前に比べてどう変わるか。","en":"A company has operating profit of JPY 6.0 billion and JPY 30.0 billion of floating-rate debt at a current rate of 2.0%. If rates rise by 1 percentage point, how does the interest coverage ratio (operating profit / interest expense, ignoring other interest) change?"},"choices":[{"ja":"10.0倍から9.0倍に低下する","en":"It falls from 10.0x to 9.0x"},{"ja":"10.0倍から約5.0倍に低下する","en":"It falls from 10.0x to about 5.0x"},{"ja":"10.0倍から約6.7倍に低下する","en":"It falls from 10.0x to about 6.7x"},{"ja":"10.0倍から6.0倍に低下する","en":"It falls from 10.0x to 6.0x"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"支払利息は300億円×2.0%＝6億円で、レシオは60÷6＝10.0倍。1ポイント上昇後は利率3.0%で利息9億円、レシオは60÷9＝約6.7倍に低下する。利率の上昇分を単純にレシオから引いても、変化は正しく捉えられない。","en":"Interest is 30.0 billion x 2.0% = JPY 600 million, so coverage is 6.0 / 0.6 = 10.0x. After a 1-point rise the rate is 3.0%, interest is JPY 900 million, and coverage falls to 6.0 / 0.9 = about 6.7x. Subtracting the rate rise directly from the ratio does not capture the change."}},
{"id":"s17x29","dom":"risk","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"業績悪化で将来の課税所得の見積りが下がり、会社は繰延税金資産30億円を取り崩して費用計上することにした。この会計処理が会社に与える影響として正しいものはどれか。","en":"Weaker results lowered the estimate of future taxable income, and a company decided to write off JPY 3.0 billion of deferred tax assets as an expense. Which statement about the effect of this accounting is correct?"},"choices":[{"ja":"現金が30億円減少し、資金繰りが直接悪化する","en":"Cash falls by JPY 3.0 billion, directly worsening liquidity"},{"ja":"営業利益が30億円減り、本業の収益力が悪化したものとして損益計算書の上位で開示され、営業利益ベースの指標も悪化する","en":"Operating profit falls by JPY 3.0 billion and is disclosed in the upper part of the income statement as weaker core earning power, worsening operating-profit-based measures too"},{"ja":"現金は減らないが、純利益と純資産が30億円減り、純資産に連動する財務制限条項に影響しうる","en":"No cash leaves, but net income and net assets fall by JPY 3.0 billion, which can affect covenants tied to net assets"},{"ja":"法人税の納付額が30億円増え、翌期の資金負担となる","en":"Corporate tax payments rise by JPY 3.0 billion, creating a cash burden next year"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"繰延税金資産の取崩しは法人税等調整額として計上され、非現金で、営業利益には影響しないが、純利益と純資産を30億円減らす。純資産維持などの財務制限条項があれば抵触の恐れが出る。納税額は増えず、現金の流出も起きない。","en":"Writing off deferred tax assets is booked as income tax adjustments. It is non-cash and does not affect operating profit, but it cuts net income and net assets by JPY 3.0 billion, which can threaten net-asset maintenance covenants. Tax paid does not rise and no cash leaves."}},
{"id":"s17x30","dom":"perf","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"事業Aの営業利益は12億円、投下資本は150億円、実効税率は30%、WACCは7%である。この事業の経済的付加価値（EVA = NOPAT − 投下資本 × WACC）はいくらか。","en":"Business A has operating profit of JPY 1.2 billion, invested capital of JPY 15.0 billion, an effective tax rate of 30% and a WACC of 7%. What is its EVA (NOPAT - invested capital x WACC)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"+1.5億円","en":"+JPY 150 million"},{"ja":"+8.4億円","en":"+JPY 840 million"},{"ja":"−10.5億円","en":"-JPY 1.05 billion"},{"ja":"−2.1億円","en":"-JPY 210 million"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"NOPAT＝12×(1−0.3)＝8.4億円。資本費用＝150×7%＝10.5億円なので、EVAは−2.1億円で、営業利益は黒字でも資本コストを賄えず価値を減らしている。税引前の営業利益から引くと+1.5億円となり、黒字に見えてしまう。","en":"NOPAT = 1.2 x (1 - 0.3) = JPY 840 million. The capital charge is 15.0 billion x 7% = JPY 1.05 billion, so EVA is -JPY 210 million: profitable on paper but not covering the cost of capital. Subtracting from pre-tax operating profit gives +150 million, which looks profitable."}},
{"id":"s17x31","dom":"perf","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある製品の売上予算は、販売数量10,000個、単価1,000円である。実績は販売数量11,000個、単価950円だった。売上高差異のうち価格差異（実績数量に対する単価の差）はいくらか。","en":"A product's sales budget is 10,000 units at JPY 1,000 each. Actuals were 11,000 units at JPY 950 each. What is the price variance (the unit price gap applied to actual volume)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50万円の不利差異","en":"JPY 500,000 unfavorable"},{"ja":"100万円の有利差異","en":"JPY 1,000,000 favorable"},{"ja":"55万円の不利差異","en":"JPY 550,000 unfavorable"},{"ja":"45万円の有利差異","en":"JPY 450,000 favorable"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"価格差異＝(実績単価950円−予算単価1,000円)×実績数量11,000個＝−55万円で不利差異。予算数量を使うと−50万円になる。数量差異は+100万円（有利）で、両者を合わせた総差異は+45万円である。","en":"Price variance = (950 - 1,000) x 11,000 = -JPY 550,000, unfavorable. Using budget volume would give -500,000. The volume variance is +1,000,000 favorable, and together they make the total variance of +450,000."}},
{"id":"s17x32","dom":"perf","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"固定費が年12億円、変動費率が60%の事業がある。営業利益4億円を達成するために必要な売上高はいくらか。","en":"A business has annual fixed costs of JPY 1.2 billion and a variable cost ratio of 60%. What sales are needed to reach an operating profit of JPY 400 million?"},"choices":[{"ja":"30億円","en":"JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"40億円","en":"JPY 4.0 billion"},{"ja":"26.7億円","en":"JPY 2.67 billion"},{"ja":"34億円","en":"JPY 3.4 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"貢献利益率は1−0.6＝40%。必要な売上高は(固定費12億＋目標利益4億)÷0.4＝40億円。損益分岐点の売上高は12÷0.4＝30億円で、目標利益を含まない。目標利益を売上にそのまま足した34億円は、貢献利益率を考えていない。","en":"The contribution margin ratio is 1 - 0.6 = 40%. Required sales are (1.2 + 0.4) / 0.4 = JPY 4.0 billion. Break-even sales are 1.2 / 0.4 = 3.0 billion, which excludes the target profit. Adding profit directly to break-even sales (3.4 billion) ignores the contribution margin ratio."}},
{"id":"s17x33","dom":"perf","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"貢献利益が40億円、営業利益が10億円の事業がある。売上が5%減少し、変動費率が一定で固定費も変わらないとき、営業利益は何%減少するか。","en":"A business has contribution margin of JPY 4.0 billion and operating profit of JPY 1.0 billion. If sales fall 5% with a constant variable cost ratio and unchanged fixed costs, by what percentage does operating profit fall?"},"choices":[{"ja":"20%","en":"20%"},{"ja":"5%","en":"5%"},{"ja":"1.25%","en":"1.25%"},{"ja":"25%","en":"25%"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"営業レバレッジ（DOL）＝貢献利益÷営業利益＝40÷10＝4倍。売上が5%減ると営業利益は5%×4＝20%減る。売上と同率の5%減とするのは、固定費の存在を無視している。逆数を掛けた1.25%は過小になる。","en":"Operating leverage (DOL) = contribution margin / operating profit = 40 / 10 = 4x. A 5% sales drop cuts operating profit by 5% x 4 = 20%. Assuming a 5% fall ignores fixed costs, and multiplying by the inverse (1.25%) is far too small."}},
{"id":"s17x34","dom":"perf","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"製造部門は販売部門に部品を社内で供給できる。部品の変動費は1個600円で、製造部門には遊休能力があり、外部へは販売しない。販売部門は外部の業者から1個750円で調達できる。全社の利益を最大にする判断として正しいものはどれか。","en":"A manufacturing division can supply a component to the sales division internally. Its variable cost is JPY 600 per unit, it has idle capacity, and it sells nothing externally. The sales division can buy the component from an outside supplier at JPY 750 per unit. Which judgment maximizes company-wide profit?"},"choices":[{"ja":"社内調達とし、振替価格は変動費600円以上、外部価格750円以下の範囲で設定する","en":"Source internally, with a transfer price set between the variable cost of JPY 600 and the outside price of JPY 750"},{"ja":"外部から750円で調達し、製造部門の遊休能力は活用しない","en":"Buy from the outside supplier at JPY 750 and leave the division's idle capacity unused"},{"ja":"製造部門の固定費を配賦した完全原価が750円を超えるなら、外部調達を選ぶ","en":"Buy externally if the division's full cost with allocated fixed costs exceeds JPY 750"},{"ja":"振替価格は製造部門の希望どおり1,000円に設定し、販売部門が受け入れなければ外部調達に切り替える","en":"Set the transfer price at JPY 1,000 as the manufacturing division wants, and switch to external purchasing if the sales division does not accept it"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"遊休能力があるなら、社内で作る追加コストは変動費600円だけで、外部調達の750円より安く、全社では1個150円有利になる。振替価格は600円以上750円以下の水準で設定する。固定費を含む完全原価で判断すると、全社最適に反する外部調達を選びかねない。","en":"With idle capacity, the extra cost of making the part internally is only the JPY 600 variable cost, below the outside price of 750, so the company gains JPY 150 per unit. The transfer price should sit between 600 and 750. Judging by full cost with fixed costs could lead to an external purchase that hurts the company as a whole."}},
{"id":"s17x35","dom":"perf","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"ある事業部は、毎年、達成しやすい低めの売上目標を予算として提出し、達成すると賞与が支給される。実際には毎期、予算を10〜15%上回って達成している。経営企画が予算の質を高めるために最も有効な施策はどれか。","en":"A business unit submits an easily met, low sales target as its budget every year and receives a bonus when it is achieved. In practice it beats budget by 10-15% every period. Which action would most improve the quality of the budget?"},"choices":[{"ja":"達成率が高い事業部の賞与を一律に減額し、提出された予算額に関わらず支給を抑える","en":"Cut bonuses across the board for units with high achievement rates, regardless of the submitted budget"},{"ja":"外部ベンチマークや先行指標で目標を検証し、前年実績や事業部の提示額に依存しない目標設定に改める","en":"Test targets against external benchmarks and leading indicators, and set them without relying on last year's actuals or the unit's own submission"},{"ja":"予算の提出を廃止して、経営陣がすべての事業部の目標を一方的に決める","en":"Abolish budget submissions and have senior management dictate every unit's targets"},{"ja":"予算を達成した事業部は、翌期の目標を前期の実際の達成額の2倍へ自動的に引き上げ、例外を一切認めない","en":"Automatically raise a unit's next-year target to twice the previous year's actual result whenever it meets its budget, with absolutely no exceptions"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"低めに目標を出す予算スラックは、情報を持つ現場と、報酬が目標に連動する仕組みから生まれる。外部ベンチマークや先行指標で目標を検証し、前期実績に機械的に依存しない設定にすると、余裕を縮められる。達成額を自動で倍にする仕組みは、さらに実力を隠す行動を促す。","en":"Budget slack arises from information held by the front line and from pay tied to targets. Testing targets against external benchmarks and leading indicators, without mechanical reliance on prior actuals, narrows the slack. Automatically doubling next year's target would push units to hide performance even more."}},
{"id":"s17x36","dom":"perf","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"間接費のうち段取作業の費用が3,000万円で、年間の段取回数は300回である。製品Xは段取を50回行い、直接作業時間は全体の10%である。段取費用を段取回数を基準とするABC（活動基準原価計算）で配賦する場合と、直接作業時間で配賦する従来方式の場合について、製品Xへの配賦額の組合せはどれか。","en":"Setup costs within overhead are JPY 30 million, with 300 setups a year. Product X needs 50 setups and accounts for 10% of direct labor hours. Which pair shows the setup cost allocated to X under ABC (activity-based costing, by number of setups) and under the traditional method (by direct labor hours)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ABCで500万円、従来方式で300万円","en":"JPY 5 million under ABC and JPY 3 million under the traditional method"},{"ja":"ABCで300万円、従来方式で500万円","en":"JPY 3 million under ABC and JPY 5 million under the traditional method"},{"ja":"ABCで500万円、従来方式でも500万円","en":"JPY 5 million under ABC and also JPY 5 million under the traditional method"},{"ja":"ABCで300万円、従来方式でも300万円","en":"JPY 3 million under ABC and also JPY 3 million under the traditional method"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"ABCでは1回あたり3,000万÷300回＝10万円に、製品Xの50回を掛けて500万円。直接作業時間で配賦すると3,000万×10%＝300万円で、段取の多い製品Xの原価が過小になる。多品種少量の製品の採算を見誤る原因になる。","en":"Under ABC, the rate is 30 million / 300 = JPY 100,000 per setup, and 50 setups give JPY 5 million. Allocating by direct labor hours gives 30 million x 10% = JPY 3 million, understating the cost of setup-heavy product X and distorting the profitability of low-volume, high-mix products."}},
{"id":"s17x37","dom":"stakeholder","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"個人投資家のX氏は、上場会社の株式を4.6%保有していたが、市場で買い増して6.2%になった。X氏に求められる最も適切な対応はどれか。","en":"Individual investor X held 4.6% of a listed company and bought more on the market to reach 6.2%. Which action is required of X?"},"choices":[{"ja":"5%を超えた日から5営業日以内に、大量保有報告書を提出する","en":"File a large shareholding report within five business days of crossing 5%"},{"ja":"6.2%に達したあと、決算期末までに有価証券報告書に記載すれば足りる","en":"Disclose the holding in the annual securities report by the fiscal year end after reaching 6.2%"},{"ja":"10%を超えるまでは報告義務がないので、提出は不要である","en":"No filing is needed until the holding exceeds 10%"},{"ja":"取引所に適時開示を行い、対象会社の取締役会の承認を得る","en":"Make a timely disclosure to the exchange and obtain approval from the target's board of directors"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"上場株式等の保有割合が5%を超えた者は、その日から5営業日以内に大量保有報告書を提出する義務がある（金融商品取引法）。10%などの基準はなく、有価証券報告書での記載では代替できない。取引所への適時開示や対象会社の承認も要件ではない。","en":"Anyone whose holding of listed shares exceeds 5% must file a large shareholding report within five business days (Financial Instruments and Exchange Act). There is no 10% threshold, an annual securities report cannot substitute, and neither exchange disclosure nor the target's approval is required."}},
{"id":"s17x38","dom":"stakeholder","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"上場会社のIR担当役員が、アナリストとの個別面談で、未公表の業績下方修正につながる数値を、意図せず口にしてしまった。フェア・ディスクロージャー・ルールのもとで、会社に求められる対応はどれか。","en":"An investor relations executive at a listed company unintentionally mentioned numbers pointing to an unannounced earnings downgrade in a one-on-one meeting with an analyst. Under the fair disclosure rule, what must the company do?"},"choices":[{"ja":"意図的でなかったため公表の義務は生じないとして、社内で再発防止策だけを講じる","en":"Treat it as having no disclosure duty because it was unintentional and take only internal steps to prevent recurrence"},{"ja":"速やかに、当該情報をホームページや適時開示などで公表する","en":"Promptly publish the information, for example on its website or by timely disclosure"},{"ja":"次の決算発表のときに、他の情報とあわせて公表すれば足りる","en":"Wait and publish it together with other information at the next earnings announcement"},{"ja":"公平性を保つため、他のアナリストにも個別に同じ内容を伝える","en":"Pass the same content individually to other analysts to keep things even"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"フェア・ディスクロージャー・ルールは、未公表の重要情報を証券会社や投資家などに伝えたとき、情報を公平に行き渡らせるために公表を求める。意図的な場合は同時に、意図せずに伝えた場合は速やかに公表する。意図がなくても義務はなくならず、次の決算まで待つのも不十分である。","en":"The fair disclosure rule requires material non-public information given to brokers or investors to be made public so everyone gets it fairly: at the same time if intentional, promptly if unintentional. Lack of intent does not remove the duty, and waiting until the next earnings release is not enough."}},
{"id":"s17x39","dom":"stakeholder","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"ROEが4%で、現金・預金が総資産の40%を占める会社に、アクティビスト・ファンドが株式の3%を取得し、「1,000億円の自社株買いと社外取締役の増員」を書簡で要求してきた。同社の資本コストは7%である。取締役会の対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"An activist fund bought 3% of a company with ROE of 4% and cash and deposits equal to 40% of total assets, and demanded in a letter a JPY 100 billion share buyback and more outside directors. The company's cost of capital is 7%. What is the most appropriate board response?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ROEや現金の水準への指摘は短期志向の株主の主張にすぎないとみなし、書簡への返答も面談の申し入れも断る","en":"Dismiss the comments on ROE and cash as the claims of a short-term holder and decline both a reply to the letter and any request for a meeting"},{"ja":"株価を上げるため、財務の健全性や成長投資との比較は行わず、要求どおり1,000億円の自社株買いをただちに実行する","en":"Carry out the JPY 100 billion buyback right away as requested to lift the share price, without comparing it with financial soundness or growth investment"},{"ja":"要求の内容を独立して検討し、成長投資・財務・還元を比べた最適な資本配分を整理して、採否の理由を株主に説明する","en":"Review the demands independently, work out the best capital allocation across growth investment, finances and returns, and explain the decision and reasons to shareholders"},{"ja":"要求の撤回を求め、応じなければただちに買収防衛策を発動する","en":"Demand that the request be withdrawn and trigger a takeover defense immediately if it is not"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"資本コストを下回るROEや過剰な現金など、提案には一定の合理性がある論点が含まれることが多い。内容を独立に検討し、成長投資・財務の健全性・還元を比較した最適な配分を整理して、採否の理由を説明するのが原則である。一律の拒否も要求の丸呑みも、検討を欠く。","en":"Activist proposals often raise points with some merit, such as ROE below the cost of capital and excess cash. The board should assess the demands independently, work out the best balance of growth investment, financial soundness and returns, and explain its decision. Blanket rejection or wholesale acceptance both skip real analysis."}},
{"id":"s17x40","dom":"stakeholder","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"プライム市場の上場会社が、非公開で、株価に40%のプレミアムを付けた買収提案を同業の事業会社から受領した。社長は『独立経営を続けたいので断る』と述べている。経済産業省の『企業買収における行動指針』の考え方に沿った対応はどれか。","en":"A Prime Market company received a non-public acquisition proposal at a 40% premium to its share price from a business competitor. The president says, 'We want to remain independent, so we will decline.' Which response follows the approach of the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry's Takeover Guidelines?"},"choices":[{"ja":"非公開で受けた提案に応じる法的な義務はないので、取締役会にも社外取締役にも諮らず、社長の判断だけで断る","en":"Decline on the president's judgment alone without consulting the board or outside directors, since there is no legal duty to respond to a proposal received privately"},{"ja":"プレミアムが40%あれば株主の利益になるので、検討を省いて受け入れを決める","en":"Decide to accept without further study, since a 40% premium is by itself good for shareholders"},{"ja":"真摯な提案なら取締役会で誠実に検討し、社外役員が関与して提案の価値と単独の企業価値を比べて決める","en":"If the proposal is bona fide, have the board consider it in good faith with outside directors involved and compare its value with standalone value"},{"ja":"提案の存在は誰にも知らせず、買収防衛策の導入だけを急いで進める","en":"Tell no one of the proposal and rush only to adopt a takeover defense"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"行動指針は、真摯な買収提案に対し取締役会が誠実に検討し、必要に応じて独立社外取締役を中心とする体制で、提案が株主価値に資するかを単独の企業価値と比較して判断することを求める。社長の判断だけで門前払いにするのも、検討なしの受入れも、この考え方に反する。","en":"The Guidelines call on the board to consider a bona fide proposal in good faith, using independent outside directors where appropriate, and to judge whether it serves shareholder value against standalone value. Turning it away on the president's say-so, or accepting with no review, both go against this approach."}},
{"id":"s17x41","dom":"stakeholder","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"親会社が上場子会社を完全子会社化するため、TOB（公開買付け）を予定している。少数株主の利益を守る公正性担保措置として、最も有効な組合せはどれか。","en":"A parent company plans a tender offer to make its listed subsidiary wholly owned. Which combination is most effective as fairness safeguards protecting minority shareholders?"},"choices":[{"ja":"独立社外取締役による特別委員会の設置、独立した第三者の価格評価書の取得、マジョリティ・オブ・マイノリティ条件の設定","en":"Set up a special committee of independent outside directors, obtain a valuation report from an independent third party, and adopt a majority-of-the-minority condition"},{"ja":"親会社の役員で構成する委員会での検討、親会社が選んだ算定機関だけの利用、買付期間の短縮","en":"Review by a committee of parent company officers, use only an appraiser chosen by the parent, and a shortened offer period"},{"ja":"買付価格を直近の市場株価と同額にして、プレミアムは付けない","en":"Set the offer price equal to the latest market price with no premium"},{"ja":"対象会社の取締役会による賛同決議は避け、買付けの内容は買付者のウェブサイトのみで開示し、少数株主への説明は最小限にとどめる","en":"Avoid a board resolution of support by the target, disclose the offer terms only on the bidder's website, and keep explanations to minority shareholders to a minimum"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"構造的な利益相反がある取引では、特別委員会、独立した第三者の価格評価、マジョリティ・オブ・マイノリティ条件などで少数株主を保護する。親会社側の関係者だけで判断を完結させたり、プレミアムなしで情報も限られる取引は、公正性が疑われる。","en":"In a deal with structural conflicts of interest, minority holders are protected through a special committee, independent third-party valuation and a majority-of-the-minority condition. Decisions made only by parent-side people, or offers with no premium and limited information, invite doubts about fairness."}},
{"id":"s17x42","dom":"stakeholder","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"会社で売上の不適切な計上が疑われ、第三者委員会を設置することにした。調査の信頼性を最も高める委員の人選はどれか。","en":"Improper sales recognition is suspected at a company, and it decides to set up a third-party committee. Which choice of members best strengthens the credibility of the investigation?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営陣が日頃から全幅の信頼を置いている顧問弁護士を委員長とし、事情に詳しい社内の取締役も委員に加える","en":"The regular lawyer whom management trusts completely as chair, with internal directors who know the facts added as members"},{"ja":"会社と利害関係のない弁護士や公認会計士などで構成し、顧問弁護士や会計監査人の関係者は含めない","en":"Members with no ties to the company, such as lawyers and certified public accountants, excluding anyone from the company's regular law firm or its auditor"},{"ja":"会計監査を担当している監査法人の会計士を中心に構成する","en":"Mainly accountants from the audit firm that audits the company"},{"ja":"社内の内部監査部長を委員長とし、調査の範囲は経営陣が決める","en":"The head of internal audit as chair, with the scope of the investigation decided by management"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"第三者委員会は、依頼者である会社から独立して調査することが信頼の前提である。顧問弁護士や会計監査人は会社と日常的な関係があり、自らの業務をチェックする立場にもなるため、委員から外す。社内者が委員長を務め範囲を経営陣が定めると、独立性が失われる。","en":"A third-party committee is credible only if it investigates independently of the client company. The regular lawyer and the auditor have day-to-day ties and would be reviewing their own work, so they are excluded. An insider chair and a scope set by management destroy independence."}},
{"id":"s17x43","dom":"stakeholder","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"東京証券取引所は、プライム市場とスタンダード市場の会社に、資本コストや株価を意識した経営の実現に向けた対応を要請している。PBR1倍割れの会社が行う開示として、要請の趣旨に最も沿うものはどれか。","en":"The Tokyo Stock Exchange has asked Prime and Standard Market companies to manage with awareness of the cost of capital and share price. Which disclosure by a company with a P/B below 1x best fits the intent of the request?"},"choices":[{"ja":"自社のPBRが1倍を超えた時点で、初めて対応方針を開示する","en":"Disclose a response policy only once its P/B has risen above 1x"},{"ja":"現状（ROE・資本コスト・PBR等）の分析と評価、改善の方針・目標・期間、取組みの進捗を開示し、見直す","en":"Disclose the analysis and assessment of the current position (ROE, cost of capital, P/B and so on), the policy, targets and timeline for improvement and progress, and review it"},{"ja":"競合他社の株価水準と並ぶまで、自社の資本コストの推計は開示しない","en":"Withhold its cost of capital estimate until its share price level matches that of competitors"},{"ja":"改善の具体策は競争上の機密情報にあたるため、方針や目標は文書で開示せず、株主総会での口頭の説明のみにとどめる","en":"Treat the specific measures as confidential competitive information, publish no policy or targets in writing, and explain orally at the shareholders' meeting only"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"東証の要請は、現状の分析・評価、改善の方針・目標・期間、取組みの状況を開示し、継続して見直すことを求める。株価が改善してから動いたり、方針を非開示とする対応は趣旨に合わない。","en":"The exchange's request calls for disclosing the analysis and assessment of the current position, the policy, targets and timeline for improvement, and progress, with continuing review. Acting only after the share price improves, or withholding the policy, does not fit its intent."}},
{"id":"s17x44","dom":"cfo","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"回収に15年かかる工場の新設を、全額、1年更新の短期借入金で賄う案が出ている。足元の金利は低い。CFOとしての判断として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"A proposal would fund a new factory that takes 15 years to pay back entirely with one-year renewable short-term loans. Rates are currently low. Which judgment is most appropriate for the CFO?"},"choices":[{"ja":"短期金利が低い間は短期借入で賄い、金利が上がってから対応を考える","en":"Fund it short-term while short-term rates are low and think about action once rates rise"},{"ja":"短期借入を毎年借り換えれば実質的に長期資金になるので、問題はない","en":"Treat it as fine because rolling short-term loans each year is effectively long-term funding"},{"ja":"返済期間の短い資金ほど貸し手に好まれて信用力の評価も高まるため、投資の回収期間にかかわらず短期借入を優先して調達する","en":"Raise money short-term first regardless of the payback period, because shorter funding is preferred by lenders and lifts the credit assessment"},{"ja":"投資の回収期間に見合う長期・固定の資金（長期借入・社債・自己資金）で賄い、借換えと金利上昇のリスクを抑える","en":"Fund it with long-term, fixed-rate money matched to the payback period (long-term loans, bonds or own funds) to limit refinancing and rate risk"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"長期の資産を短期資金で賄うと、借換え時に貸し手が応じないリスクや、金利上昇リスクを負う。資金の期間は投資の回収期間に合わせる。毎年の借換えは長期資金の代わりにはならず、短期で賄うと、金利上昇時に利払いが急増する。","en":"Funding a long-lived asset short-term exposes the company to the risk that lenders refuse to roll the loan and to rising rates. Funding maturity should match the payback period. Annual rollovers are not a substitute for long-term funding, and short-term funding makes interest costs jump when rates rise."}},
{"id":"s17x45","dom":"cfo","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"日本基準を適用する会社が、IFRSの任意適用を検討している。過去の買収で生じたのれんがあり、日本基準では年40億円を20年間で償却し、販管費に計上している。他の差異は考えないものとして、IFRSへ移行した場合の影響として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"A Japanese GAAP reporter is considering voluntary adoption of IFRS. Goodwill from past acquisitions is amortized at JPY 4.0 billion a year over 20 years and charged to SG&A. Ignoring other differences, which statement best describes the effect of moving to IFRS?"},"choices":[{"ja":"のれんは移行時に全額を費用処理するため、移行後の営業利益は変わらず、減損テストも毎年は求められなくなり、注記も簡素になる","en":"Goodwill is fully expensed at transition, so operating profit after transition is unchanged, annual impairment tests are no longer required, and the notes become simpler"},{"ja":"のれんの償却がなくなり営業利益は年40億円改善するが、毎年の減損テストで大きな減損損失が出るリスクを負う","en":"Amortization of goodwill stops, improving operating profit by JPY 4.0 billion a year, but the company bears the risk of large impairment losses in annual impairment tests"},{"ja":"のれんの償却がなくなるため営業利益は改善し、減損テストも不要になる","en":"Operating profit improves because amortization stops, and impairment testing also becomes unnecessary"},{"ja":"のれんの償却期間が10年に短縮されて償却費が倍の年80億円となり、営業利益は年40億円悪化する","en":"The amortization period shortens to 10 years, doubling the charge to JPY 8.0 billion a year and worsening operating profit by JPY 4.0 billion a year"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"IFRSではのれんを償却せず、毎期（年1回以上）の減損テストで評価する。償却費40億円がなくなる分、営業利益は改善するが、買収後の業績が悪化すれば一度に大きな減損損失を計上する。減損テスト自体は不要にならない。","en":"Under IFRS goodwill is not amortized but tested for impairment at least annually. Operating profit improves by the JPY 4.0 billion of amortization no longer charged, but if the acquired business deteriorates a large impairment loss can hit at once. The impairment test itself is not removed."}},
{"id":"s17x46","dom":"cfo","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"グループ通算制度を適用している会社が、100%子会社を持つ。親会社の所得が50億円、子会社が20億円の欠損のとき、通算後の課税所得の考え方と法人税等（実効税率30%）として正しいものはどれか。他の調整は考えない。","en":"A company applying the group tax sharing system has a wholly owned subsidiary. The parent has income of JPY 5.0 billion and the subsidiary has a loss of JPY 2.0 billion. Which statement about taxable income after consolidation and the tax (30% effective rate) is correct? Ignore other adjustments."},"choices":[{"ja":"親会社の所得50億円に課税され、税額は約15億円で、子会社の欠損は切り捨てられる","en":"The parent's JPY 5.0 billion of income is taxed for about JPY 1.5 billion, and the subsidiary's loss is discarded"},{"ja":"子会社の欠損20億円は、翌期以降の繰越欠損金としてのみ使える","en":"The subsidiary's JPY 2.0 billion loss can be used only as a carryforward from next year onward"},{"ja":"通算の効果で、グループ全体の税額は0円になる","en":"Netting reduces the group's tax to zero"},{"ja":"所得と欠損が通算されて課税所得は30億円となり、税額は約9億円である","en":"Income and loss are netted to a taxable income of JPY 3.0 billion, and the tax is about JPY 900 million"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"グループ通算制度では、完全支配関係にある法人間で所得と欠損を同じ事業年度に通算できる。50億円と△20億円を通算した30億円に30%を掛けて約9億円となり、通算しない場合の約15億円より約6億円少ない。欠損の翌期以降への持越しだけに限る見方は誤りである。","en":"The group tax sharing system lets companies in a full-control relationship net income and losses in the same fiscal year. JPY 5.0 billion less 2.0 billion is 3.0 billion, and 30% of that is about 900 million, roughly 600 million less than the 1.5 billion without netting. Limiting the loss to carryforward only is wrong."}},
{"id":"s17x47","dom":"cfo","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"日本の親会社が、持株比率100%で保有する海外子会社から、100億円の配当を受け取った。外国子会社配当益金不算入制度の要件は満たしており、外国源泉税は考慮せず、実効税率を30%とする。親会社の日本での追加の税負担はおよそいくらか。","en":"A Japanese parent received a JPY 10.0 billion dividend from a wholly owned foreign subsidiary. It meets the requirements of the foreign subsidiary dividend exclusion system. Ignoring foreign withholding tax and assuming a 30% effective rate, roughly how much additional tax does the parent bear in Japan?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約30億円","en":"About JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"約0円","en":"About zero"},{"ja":"約28.5億円","en":"About JPY 2.85 billion"},{"ja":"約1.5億円","en":"About JPY 150 million"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"この制度では、外国子会社から受けた配当の95%が益金に算入されず、残る5%が課税対象となる（2026年10月時点）。100億円の5%は5億円で、30%を掛けると約1.5億円になる。全額課税の30億円は制度を使わない場合であり、全額非課税とする見方は5%の課税を見落としている。","en":"Under this system, 95% of the dividend from a foreign subsidiary is excluded from taxable income and the remaining 5% is taxed (as of October 2026). 5% of JPY 10.0 billion is 500 million, and 30% of that is about 150 million. Full taxation (3.0 billion) applies without the system, and treating the dividend as fully exempt misses the taxed 5%."}},
{"id":"s17x48","dom":"cfo","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"定額法（耐用年数10年、残存価額ゼロ）で償却している取得価額100億円の設備について、4年経過後に、技術的な評価に基づき総耐用年数を15年に見直した。会計上の見積りの変更として、変更後の年間償却費はいくらか。","en":"Equipment with an acquisition cost of JPY 10.0 billion is depreciated by the straight-line method (10-year life, zero residual value). After four years, a technical review extends the total useful life to 15 years. Treating this as a change in accounting estimate, what is the annual depreciation after the change?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約5.5億円","en":"About JPY 550 million"},{"ja":"約10億円","en":"About JPY 1.0 billion"},{"ja":"約10億円（変更前のまま）","en":"About JPY 1.0 billion (unchanged from before)"},{"ja":"約4.0億円","en":"About JPY 400 million"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"耐用年数の変更は会計上の見積りの変更で、過去に遡らず、変更時点の帳簿価額60億円を残存年数11年（15−4）で割った約5.5億円を以後の償却費とする。取得価額を15年で割った約6.7億円や、帳簿価額を15年で割った4.0億円は、遡及や年数の取り違えである。","en":"A change in useful life is a change in accounting estimate and is applied prospectively: the book value of JPY 6.0 billion is spread over the remaining 11 years (15 - 4), giving about JPY 550 million a year. Dividing cost by 15 (670 million) or book value by 15 (400 million) mixes up retroactivity or the years."}},
{"id":"s17x49","dom":"cfo","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"中期経営計画の最終年度の目標がEPS成長だけで、役員の業績連動報酬もEPSだけで決まる。結果として、投資を抑え、自社株買いを最大化して目標を達成する行動が見られる。CFOとして報酬制度の見直しで最も適切な策はどれか。","en":"A medium-term plan sets its final-year target only on EPS growth, and executives' performance-linked pay depends on EPS alone. As a result, they hold back investment and maximize buybacks to hit the target. What is the CFO's most appropriate remedy in the pay design?"},"choices":[{"ja":"EPSの目標水準をさらに高く引き上げて、役員により高い成長を、より短い期間で求める","en":"Raise the EPS target level even higher to demand faster, higher growth from executives in a shorter period"},{"ja":"業績連動報酬をすべてやめて、固定報酬だけの設計にすることで、短期的な行動の歪みを根本からなくし、投資判断の質も高める","en":"Abolish all performance-linked pay and use fixed pay only, removing short-term distortions of behavior at the root and improving the quality of investment decisions"},{"ja":"長期インセンティブにROICやTSRなど資本効率や株主価値の指標を加え、EPSだけに偏らない設計にする","en":"Add capital efficiency and shareholder value measures such as ROIC and TSR to long-term incentives so the design does not lean on EPS alone"},{"ja":"自社株買いを全面的に禁止し、株主還元は安定した配当だけで行う方針に切り替える","en":"Ban buybacks entirely and switch to a policy of returning capital to shareholders through stable dividends only"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"EPSは自社株買いや投資の抑制で改善でき、資本コストを考慮しない。ROICやTSRなど資本効率や株主価値の指標を長期報酬に加えると、価値を生む投資と規律ある還元に誘導できる。EPS目標の引上げは歪みを強め、固定報酬だけでは業績への動機づけを失う。","en":"EPS can be lifted by buybacks or cutting investment and ignores the cost of capital. Adding ROIC and TSR to long-term pay steers management toward value-creating investment and disciplined returns. Raising the EPS target intensifies the distortion, and fixed pay alone removes the performance incentive."}},
{"id":"s17x50","dom":"cfo","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"連結売上高3,000億円の会社が、財務報告に係る内部統制の評価範囲を決める。売上高の大きい順に、拠点Pが1,200億円、拠点Qが500億円、拠点Rが400億円、拠点Sが300億円、ほかに小規模な拠点が合計600億円である。連結売上高の概ね3分の2に達するまでを重要な事業拠点とする目安のとき、重要な事業拠点はどこまでか。","en":"A company with consolidated sales of JPY 300.0 billion is defining the scope of its assessment of internal control over financial reporting. In descending order of sales, site P has JPY 120.0 billion, site Q 50.0 billion, site R 40.0 billion, site S 30.0 billion, and small sites total 60.0 billion. If the guideline is to include sites until roughly two-thirds of consolidated sales are reached, which sites are significant?"},"choices":[{"ja":"拠点P・Qの2拠点","en":"The two sites P and Q"},{"ja":"拠点P・Q・R・Sの4拠点","en":"The four sites P, Q, R and S"},{"ja":"拠点P・Q・Rの3拠点","en":"The three sites P, Q and R"},{"ja":"拠点Pの1拠点のみ","en":"Site P alone"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"実施基準では、売上高などの金額が大きい拠点から合算し、連結売上高の概ね3分の2程度に達するまでを重要な事業拠点とする。必要額は2,000億円で、P・Qの1,700億円では足りず、Rを加えた2,100億円で達する。Sは目安に達した後なので含めない。","en":"The implementation standards add up sites in descending order of sales until about two-thirds of consolidated sales are covered. The target is JPY 200.0 billion; P and Q give 170.0 billion, which falls short, and adding R reaches 210.0 billion. S comes after the guideline is met and is not included."}}
);
