  _quiz.push(
{"id":"s18x01","dom":"mnacase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】製造業のA社が、非上場のB社の全株式を、企業価値（EV）400億円で買収する交渉を進めている。B社の貸借対照表には、借入金80億円、現金30億円、買掛金60億円（通常の取引条件）、通常の締め日に基づく未払給与10億円、退職給付の積立不足25億円がある。株式価格の算定で、買い手が債務類似項目として価格からの控除を主張すべきものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Manufacturer A is negotiating to buy all shares of unlisted company B at an enterprise value (EV) of JPY 40.0 billion. B's balance sheet shows borrowings of JPY 8.0 billion, cash of 3.0 billion, accounts payable of 6.0 billion on normal terms, accrued wages of 1.0 billion based on the regular payroll cutoff, and an unfunded pension shortfall of 2.5 billion. Which item should the buyer insist on deducting from the price as a debt-like item?"},"choices":[{"ja":"退職給付の積立不足25億円（将来の現金拠出が見込まれる）","en":"The unfunded pension shortfall of JPY 2.5 billion (future cash contributions expected)"},{"ja":"買掛金60億円（通常の取引条件の営業債務）","en":"Accounts payable of JPY 6.0 billion (an ordinary trade payable on normal terms)"},{"ja":"通常の締め日に基づく未払給与10億円（毎月発生する営業上の負債）","en":"Accrued wages of JPY 1.0 billion (an operating liability arising every month)"},{"ja":"現金30億円（純有利子負債に加算すべき項目）","en":"Cash of JPY 3.0 billion (an item to add to net debt)"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"EVから株式価値を求めるとき、借入金のほか、将来の現金流出が見込まれる退職給付の積立不足などの債務類似項目を控除する。買掛金や未払給与は通常の運転資本で、EVの前提に含まれる。現金は純有利子負債から差し引く側で、加算する対象ではない。","en":"To move from EV to equity value, borrowings and debt-like items with expected future cash outflows, such as an unfunded pension shortfall, are deducted. Accounts payable and regular accrued wages are ordinary working capital already reflected in EV. Cash is subtracted in arriving at net debt, not added."}},
{"id":"s18x02","dom":"mnacase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】日本の商社A社が、米国企業の買収で、2か月後に3億ドルの対価を支払う予定である。契約は米国当局の承認が得られることが条件で、承認の確率は6割程度とされる。足元は1ドル150円で、円安が進むと円換算の支払額が増える。A社の為替リスクへの対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Japanese trading company A will pay USD 300 million in two months to acquire a US company. The contract is conditional on US regulatory approval, which is judged about 60% likely. The rate is JPY 150 per dollar, and a weaker yen raises the yen cost of payment. Which response to A's currency risk is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"ドルを先物予約で全額買い、承認が出なかった場合も、約定どおりに決済する","en":"Buy the full dollar amount forward and settle as contracted even if approval is not granted"},{"ja":"円安が進んだときは円換算の対価を引き下げるよう売り手に請求できる条項を契約に加えれば、為替の手当ては不要になる","en":"Add a clause letting A demand a lower yen-equivalent price from the seller if the yen weakens, so that no currency arrangement is needed"},{"ja":"承認の確率が6割にとどまるので、まず承認の結果が出るまでは為替の手当ては一切行わず、承認後に対応を検討する","en":"Since approval is only about 60% likely, make no currency arrangements at all until the approval result is known, and consider action afterward"},{"ja":"通貨オプションでドルのコールを買い、承認されなかった場合の損失を、支払ったプレミアムに限定する","en":"Buy a dollar call option so that, if approval is not granted, the loss is limited to the premium paid"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"取引が不成立になる可能性があるとき、先物予約だと不成立でも売買義務が残り、反対の為替変動で損失が出かねない。ドルのコールオプションなら、不成立時の損失は支払ったプレミアムに限られ、成立時は円安の影響を抑えられる。承認後に動く方針は、円安進行のリスクを放置する。","en":"When the deal may fail, a forward leaves an obligation to settle even then and can produce a loss if rates move the other way. A dollar call option caps the loss at the premium if the deal fails and still protects against a weaker yen if it closes. Waiting for approval leaves the yen risk unhedged in the meantime."}},
{"id":"s18x03","dom":"mnacase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】日本基準を適用するA社が、3年前に買収したB社の事業で、減損の兆候を認識した。のれんを含む資産グループの帳簿価額は800億円で、割引前の将来キャッシュ・フローの総額は850億円、使用価値は700億円、正味売却価額は650億円である。日本基準での減損損失の取扱いとして正しいものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Company A, which applies Japanese GAAP, sees signs of impairment in the business of B, bought three years ago. The carrying amount of the asset group including goodwill is JPY 80.0 billion; undiscounted future cash flows total 85.0 billion, value in use is 70.0 billion and net selling price is 65.0 billion. Which statement on the impairment loss under Japanese GAAP is correct?"},"choices":[{"ja":"使用価値700億円との差額100億円を、減損損失として認識する","en":"A loss of JPY 10.0 billion, the gap to the value in use of 70.0 billion, is recognized"},{"ja":"帳簿価額と正味売却価額650億円との差額150億円を、直ちに減損損失として計上して認識する","en":"Immediately recognize a loss of JPY 15.0 billion, the gap between the carrying amount and the net selling price of 65.0 billion"},{"ja":"割引前の将来キャッシュ・フローの総額が帳簿価額を上回るため、減損損失は認識しない","en":"No impairment loss is recognized because undiscounted future cash flows exceed the carrying amount"},{"ja":"減損の兆候がある以上、のれんの全額を一括して費用処理する","en":"Since there are signs of impairment, all goodwill is expensed at once"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"日本基準の減損は二段階で、まず割引前の将来キャッシュ・フロー総額（850億円）が帳簿価額（800億円）を下回るかを判定する。下回らないため損失は認識しない。回収可能価額（700億円）との差100億円を直ちに損失とするのは、IFRSの考え方である。","en":"Impairment under Japanese GAAP has two steps: first test whether undiscounted future cash flows (JPY 85.0 billion) fall below the carrying amount (80.0 billion). They do not, so no loss is recognized. Booking the JPY 10.0 billion gap to recoverable amount (70.0 billion) straight away is the IFRS approach."}},
{"id":"s18x04","dom":"mnacase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社は、ソフトウェア会社B社の株式の100%を取得する。デューデリジェンスで、B社の売上の40%を占める最大顧客との契約に、株主の変更があれば顧客が契約を解除できるチェンジ・オブ・コントロール条項があると判明した。クロージングまでの対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Company A will acquire 100% of software company B. Due diligence reveals that the contract with B's largest customer, which accounts for 40% of sales, has a change-of-control clause letting the customer terminate if the shareholder changes. Which step before closing is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"価格はすでに合意済みなので、買収後に顧客が契約を解除しても、売り手に価格調整などの追加の対応は求めない","en":"Ask nothing more of the seller, such as a price adjustment, if the customer terminates after closing, because the price has already been agreed"},{"ja":"顧客への連絡はクロージング後に行い、条項の存在は先方に伝えない","en":"Contact the customer only after closing and say nothing about the clause beforehand"},{"ja":"当該顧客から解除権を行使しない旨の同意を取得することを、クロージングの前提条件に盛り込む","en":"Make obtaining the customer's consent not to exercise its termination right a condition precedent to closing"},{"ja":"顧客との守秘義務を理由に、条項の存在を無視して、予定どおり進める","en":"Ignore the clause and proceed as scheduled, citing confidentiality obligations to the customer"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"売上の4割を占める顧客に解除権がある以上、買い手はその同意をクロージングの前提条件にして、価値の毀損を防ぐのが基本である。同意が得られない場合に備え、価格調整や撤退の条項も交渉できる。クロージング後に知らせる方法は、解除のリスクを買い手が丸ごと負う。","en":"With a customer worth 40% of sales holding a termination right, the buyer should make that customer's consent a condition to closing to protect value. If consent is not obtained, price adjustment or walk-away terms can also be negotiated. Telling the customer only after closing leaves the buyer with the full risk of termination."}},
{"id":"s18x05","dom":"mnacase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社が上場会社B社のTOB（公開買付け）を計画している。B社の直近の終値は1,000円、過去1か月の平均は950円、過去3か月の平均は900円、過去6か月の平均は850円である。買付価格を1,260円とする場合、直近の終値に対するプレミアム率と、6か月平均に対するプレミアム率の組合せはどれか（小数点以下を四捨五入）。","en":"[Case] Company A plans a tender offer for listed company B. B's latest closing price is JPY 1,000; the one-month average is 950, the three-month average is 900 and the six-month average is 850. With an offer price of JPY 1,260, which pair gives the premium over the latest close and the premium over the six-month average (rounded to the nearest percent)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"48%と26%","en":"48% and 26%"},{"ja":"26%と33%","en":"26% and 33%"},{"ja":"26%と48%","en":"26% and 48%"},{"ja":"40%と48%","en":"40% and 48%"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"直近終値比は1,260÷1,000−1＝26%、6か月平均比は1,260÷850−1＝約48%である。基準の期間が長いほど平均株価が低く、プレミアム率は高く見える。TOBでは複数の期間の平均に対するプレミアムを示すのが通例である。","en":"The premium over the latest close is 1,260 / 1,000 - 1 = 26%, and over the six-month average it is 1,260 / 850 - 1 = about 48%. The longer the averaging period, the lower the average price and the higher the premium looks. Tender offers customarily show premiums over averages for several periods."}},
{"id":"s18x06","dom":"mnacase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社は、親会社のグループから切り出される事業部門（売上200億円）を買収する。この事業の基幹システム、経理、人事給与は、現在、売り手のグループ共通基盤で運用されており、A社には代替環境がない。クロージング直後の運営を確保する手段として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Company A will buy a business unit (sales JPY 20.0 billion) being carved out of a parent group. Its core systems, accounting and payroll currently run on the seller group's shared platform, and A has no replacement environment. Which measure best secures operations right after closing?"},"choices":[{"ja":"一定期間は売り手に従来のサービスを提供させる移行期間サービス契約（TSA）を結び、その間に自社の環境へ移行する","en":"Sign a transition services agreement (TSA) under which the seller keeps providing the services for a set period while A moves to its own environment"},{"ja":"クロージング日にすべてのシステムを停止して、新しい基盤を即日で構築する","en":"Shut down all systems on the closing date and build a new platform the same day"},{"ja":"従業員だけを移管し、システムは使わずに紙の運用に切り替える","en":"Transfer only the employees and switch to paper-based operations without systems"},{"ja":"売り手との関係を早期に断つため、買収価格を下げさせたうえで、システム移行の費用や追加の人件費もすべて売り手に負担させる","en":"Cut ties with the seller early by pushing down the price and having the seller bear all costs of the system migration and any additional personnel costs"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"カーブアウトでは、切り出される事業が売り手の共通基盤に依存することが多く、移行期間サービス契約（TSA）で一定期間、システムや事務を売り手に提供させ、その間に自社環境へ段階移行する。即日の切替えは業務停止のリスクが大きい。","en":"A carved-out business often depends on the seller's shared platform, so a transition services agreement (TSA) has the seller keep providing systems and back-office services for a period while the buyer migrates in stages. A same-day switchover risks halting operations."}},
{"id":"s18x07","dom":"mnacase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】ソフトウェア企業のA社は、成長が頭打ちの主力事業を補うため、AI技術に強い非上場のB社を200億円で全株取得する方向で最終交渉に入った。B社の技術はほぼすべて創業者3名のエンジニアが握っており、後継の技術者は育っていない。創業者には売却代金が一括で入るため、買収後に退職して競合に移る懸念がある。価値を守るための最も適切な設計はどれか。","en":"[Case] Software company A is in final talks to acquire all shares of unlisted AI specialist B for JPY 20.0 billion to support its main business, whose growth has stalled. Nearly all of B's technology sits with its three founder-engineers, and no successors have been trained. The founders would receive the sale proceeds in one lump sum, so there is concern they will leave after the deal and join a competitor. Which design best protects the value?"},"choices":[{"ja":"代金は全額をクロージング時に支払い、退職を防ぐための契約上の仕組みは設けない","en":"Pay the whole price at closing and put no contractual mechanism in place to prevent departures"},{"ja":"対価の一部を繰延払いとし、在籍や業績の条件を付け、株式報酬なども併用して買収後の定着を図る","en":"Defer part of the consideration with conditions on continued service and performance, and combine it with equity awards to keep the founders after closing"},{"ja":"創業者全員を即時に取締役から外し、技術に関する意思決定はA社の役員が行う","en":"Remove all founders from the board immediately and let A's executives make the technology decisions"},{"ja":"創業者との契約は退職後3年間の競業禁止だけを定め、在籍や業績に連動する報酬面の条件は設けず、代金も即時に払う","en":"Limit the founder agreements to a three-year post-departure non-compete, set no pay conditions tied to service or performance, and pay the price at once"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"価値が人に集中する買収では、対価の一部を繰延払いにして在籍・業績の条件を付け、株式報酬なども組み合わせて定着を促す。在籍を条件とする支払は、会計上は買収対価ではなく報酬費用として扱われうる点にも注意する。全額を即時払いにすると、退職しても取り戻せない。","en":"Where value sits with people, defer part of the price subject to service and performance conditions and add equity awards to retain them. Note that payments conditional on continued service may be treated as compensation expense rather than purchase consideration. Paying everything up front leaves no recourse if they leave."}},
{"id":"s18x08","dom":"mnacase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社は競争入札でB社の買収を目指す。B社の単独での企業価値（EV）は800億円、実現可能なシナジーの現在価値は150億円、統合コストの現在価値は30億円と評価している。2次入札で、他社が950億円を示したとの情報がある。A社が示せる価格の上限と、950億円を提示した場合の判断はどれか。","en":"[Case] Company A is bidding for company B in a competitive auction. A values B's standalone enterprise value at JPY 80.0 billion, the present value of achievable synergies at 15.0 billion and the present value of integration costs at 3.0 billion. A hears that a rival has offered 95.0 billion in the second round. What is A's price ceiling, and how should A judge a 95.0 billion bid?"},"choices":[{"ja":"上限は950億円で、シナジーの全額を払っても価値は減らないため、950億円の提示は妥当である","en":"The ceiling is JPY 95.0 billion; paying away all the synergies destroys no value, so a 95.0 billion bid is reasonable"},{"ja":"上限は920億円で、950億円を示せば30億円分、A社の株主価値を毀損するため、価格を上げず撤退も選択肢とする","en":"The ceiling is JPY 92.0 billion; bidding 95.0 billion would destroy 3.0 billion of A's shareholder value, so A should not raise its price and may walk away"},{"ja":"上限は800億円で、単独価値を超える提示はシナジーを売り手に渡すだけなので、避けるべきである","en":"The ceiling is JPY 80.0 billion; bidding above standalone value only hands synergies to the seller and should be avoided"},{"ja":"上限は定められず、他社に勝つことが最優先なので、950億円を超える金額も含めて、競合が示す水準に合わせて価格を上げ続ける","en":"There is no ceiling; beating the rival is the top priority, so keep raising the price to match whatever level competitors show, including above 95.0 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"買い手が払ってよい上限は、単独価値＋シナジーの現在価値−統合コスト＝800＋150−30＝920億円である。950億円を払えば30億円分、買い手の株主価値を失う。統合コストを忘れると上限を950億円と誤認する。入札に勝つこと自体を目的化すると勝者の呪いに陥る。","en":"The most a buyer should pay is standalone value + synergy PV - integration cost = 80.0 + 15.0 - 3.0 = JPY 92.0 billion. Paying 95.0 billion gives up 3.0 billion of the buyer's shareholder value. Forgetting integration costs makes the ceiling look like 95.0 billion, and treating victory as the goal invites the winner's curse."}},
{"id":"s18x09","dom":"pecase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】PEファンドが、EBITDA 50億円の会社を8.0倍の企業価値400億円で買収した。資金は借入250億円とエクイティ150億円である。5年後、EBITDAは70億円に成長し、出口の倍率は入口と同じ8.0倍、返済により純有利子負債は150億円に減った。手数料や中間配当を考えない場合、エクイティのMOIC（投資倍率）はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A PE fund bought a company with EBITDA of JPY 5.0 billion at 8.0x, an enterprise value of JPY 40.0 billion, funded with JPY 25.0 billion of debt and 15.0 billion of equity. Five years later EBITDA has grown to 7.0 billion, the exit multiple is the same 8.0x, and repayments have cut net debt to 15.0 billion. Ignoring fees and interim dividends, what is the equity MOIC (multiple on invested capital)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約3.7倍","en":"About 3.7x"},{"ja":"約1.4倍","en":"About 1.4x"},{"ja":"約2.7倍","en":"About 2.7x"},{"ja":"約2.0倍","en":"About 2.0x"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"出口の企業価値は70億円×8.0＝560億円で、純有利子負債150億円を引いたエクイティは410億円。これを投資額150億円で割ると約2.7倍になる。出口の企業価値を150億円で割る約3.7倍は、返済すべき負債を引いていない誤りである。","en":"Exit enterprise value is 7.0 x 8.0 = JPY 56.0 billion, and less net debt of 15.0 billion the equity is 41.0 billion. Dividing by the 15.0 billion invested gives about 2.7x. Dividing exit enterprise value by 15.0 billion (3.7x) forgets the debt that must be repaid."}},
{"id":"s18x10","dom":"pecase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】PEファンドが、EBITDA 30億円の会社を7.0倍（企業価値210億円）で買収し、借入120億円、エクイティ90億円で出資した。数年後、EBITDAは36億円、出口の倍率は8.0倍（企業価値288億円）、純有利子負債は90億円になった。価値創造を『EBITDA成長（入口の倍率で評価）』『倍率拡大（出口のEBITDAで評価）』『純有利子負債の減少』に分解したとき、倍率拡大の寄与額はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A PE fund bought a company with EBITDA of JPY 3.0 billion at 7.0x (enterprise value 21.0 billion), investing 9.0 billion of equity alongside 12.0 billion of debt. Some years later EBITDA is 3.6 billion, the exit multiple is 8.0x (enterprise value 28.8 billion) and net debt is 9.0 billion. Value creation is split into EBITDA growth (valued at the entry multiple), multiple expansion (valued on exit EBITDA) and net debt reduction. What is the contribution of multiple expansion?"},"choices":[{"ja":"30億円","en":"JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"36億円","en":"JPY 3.6 billion"},{"ja":"42億円","en":"JPY 4.2 billion"},{"ja":"108億円","en":"JPY 10.8 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"EBITDA成長は(36−30)×7.0＝42億円、倍率拡大は(8.0−7.0)×36＝36億円、純有利子負債の減少は120−90＝30億円で、合計108億円（エクイティ198億円−出資90億円）になる。倍率拡大を入口のEBITDAで測ると30億円となり、合計が合わない。","en":"EBITDA growth is (3.6 - 3.0) x 7.0 = JPY 4.2 billion, multiple expansion is (8.0 - 7.0) x 3.6 = 3.6 billion, and net debt reduction is 12.0 - 9.0 = 3.0 billion, totaling 10.8 billion (equity of 19.8 billion less 9.0 billion invested). Measuring expansion on entry EBITDA gives 3.0 billion and the parts no longer add up."}},
{"id":"s18x11","dom":"pecase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】PEの保有会社は、融資契約で純有利子負債/EBITDAを6.0倍以内に保つ財務制限条項を負う。業績悪化でEBITDAが40億円、純有利子負債が260億円（6.5倍）となり、抵触が見込まれる。PEが追加出資で純有利子負債を減らして条項に収める場合、最低限必要な追加出資額はいくらか。EBITDAは変わらないものとする。","en":"[Case] A PE-owned company is bound by a loan covenant to keep net debt/EBITDA within 6.0x. After a downturn, EBITDA is JPY 4.0 billion and net debt is 26.0 billion (6.5x), so a breach is expected. If the PE sponsor injects equity to cut net debt and meet the covenant, what is the minimum injection? Assume EBITDA does not change."},"choices":[{"ja":"20億円","en":"JPY 2.0 billion"},{"ja":"40億円","en":"JPY 4.0 billion"},{"ja":"10億円","en":"JPY 1.0 billion"},{"ja":"240億円","en":"JPY 24.0 billion"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"条項を満たす純有利子負債の上限は、6.0×40億＝240億円。現在の260億円との差の20億円が最低限の追加出資（エクイティ・キュア）となる。許容上限の240億円そのものを払う必要はなく、貸し手が条項の適用を放棄（ウェーバー）する選択肢もある。","en":"The net debt ceiling consistent with the covenant is 6.0 x JPY 4.0 billion = 24.0 billion. The 2.0 billion gap to the current 26.0 billion is the minimum equity cure. There is no need to pay the 24.0 billion ceiling itself, and lenders may alternatively grant a waiver."}},
{"id":"s18x12","dom":"pecase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】出資総額1,000億円のPEファンドは、運用期間があと1年で満了する。保有する最後の優良企業（年商300億円）は成長の途上にあるが、現在の市況ではIPOも売却も望ましい価格にならない。運用会社（GP）は今後2〜3年でさらに価値が高まると見込んでいる。既存の出資者（LP）に配慮した対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] A PE fund with JPY 100.0 billion in commitments has one year left in its term. Its last strong portfolio company (annual sales of JPY 30.0 billion) is still growing, but in current markets neither an IPO nor a sale would achieve a good price. The manager (GP) expects further value gains over the next two to three years. Which response best takes the existing investors (LPs) into account?"},"choices":[{"ja":"運用期間の満了日に、市況やその時点の評価額にかかわらず、最初に買い手が現れた価格で保有分をすべて売却して清算する","en":"Sell everything at the term end at whatever price the first buyer offers, regardless of market conditions or the current valuation, and wind up the fund"},{"ja":"GP主導のセカンダリー（コンティニュエーション・ファンド）に資産を移し、既存LPには現金化か持越しを選ばせる","en":"Move the asset to a GP-led secondary (continuation fund) and let existing LPs choose between cashing out and rolling over"},{"ja":"LPに知らせずに、ファンドの運用期間を一方的に延長し、報酬体系も変更しない","en":"Extend the fund term unilaterally without informing the LPs and leave the fee structure unchanged"},{"ja":"保有会社の株式をGPが個人資産として買い取り、LPには簿価で精算する","en":"Have the GP buy the shares personally and settle with the LPs at book value"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"運用期間の終わりが近い優良資産は、コンティニュエーション・ファンドに移すと、既存LPは評価額で現金化するか、新ファンドへ持ち越すかを選べる。GPに利益相反があるため、独立した価格評価などの手続が欠かせない。市況を無視した投げ売りや、LPに無断の延長は、受託者としての義務に反する。","en":"Moving a strong asset near the end of the fund term into a continuation fund lets existing LPs either cash out at the assessed value or roll into the new fund. Because the GP is conflicted, procedures such as an independent valuation are essential. A fire sale ignoring markets, or an extension without telling LPs, breaches fiduciary duties."}},
{"id":"s18x13","dom":"pecase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】創業3年のスタートアップが、シリーズAの投資家から5億円の出資を受けた。投資家の普通株転換後の持株比率は25%で、優先株には1倍の非参加型の残余財産優先分配権が付いている。事業が思うように伸びず、会社は8億円での売却を打診された（ほかに優先株はない）。売却が実行された場合、シリーズA投資家の受取額はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A three-year-old startup raised JPY 500 million from a Series A investor, who holds 25% on an as-converted basis. The preferred stock carries a 1x non-participating liquidation preference. Business has grown more slowly than hoped, and the company has been offered a sale for JPY 800 million (there is no other preferred stock). If the sale goes through, how much does the Series A investor receive?"},"choices":[{"ja":"2億円","en":"JPY 200 million"},{"ja":"5.75億円","en":"JPY 575 million"},{"ja":"5億円","en":"JPY 500 million"},{"ja":"8億円","en":"JPY 800 million"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"非参加型の優先株は、優先分配（出資額5億円）と、普通株に転換して受け取る額（8億円×25%＝2億円）のうち大きい方を選ぶ。優先分配の5億円が上回るため5億円となる。優先分配に加えて残りの分配にも参加する参加型なら5.75億円だが、本件は非参加型である。","en":"A non-participating preferred holder takes the larger of the liquidation preference (JPY 500 million, the amount invested) or the as-converted value (800 million x 25% = 200 million). The 500 million preference is larger. A participating preferred would receive 575 million, but this stock is non-participating."}},
{"id":"s18x14","dom":"pecase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】創業2年のスタートアップが資金調達ラウンドを行い、あるVCが3億円を出資することになった。出資後のVCの持株比率は20%になる。この出資で決まる出資後評価額（ポストマネー）と出資前評価額（プレマネー）の組合せはどれか。オプションプールの影響は考えない。","en":"[Case] A two-year-old startup is raising a funding round, and a VC will invest JPY 300 million. After the investment the VC will hold 20%. Which pair gives the post-money and pre-money valuations implied by this investment? Ignore any option pool."},"choices":[{"ja":"ポストマネー12億円、プレマネー15億円","en":"Post-money JPY 1.2 billion, pre-money JPY 1.5 billion"},{"ja":"ポストマネー15億円、プレマネー12億円","en":"Post-money JPY 1.5 billion, pre-money JPY 1.2 billion"},{"ja":"ポストマネー15億円、プレマネー18億円","en":"Post-money JPY 1.5 billion, pre-money JPY 1.8 billion"},{"ja":"ポストマネー12億円、プレマネー9億円","en":"Post-money JPY 1.2 billion, pre-money JPY 900 million"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"3億円で20%を得るので、出資後評価額は3÷0.2＝15億円。出資前評価額は15億円から出資額3億円を引いた12億円である。出資前と出資後を取り違えたり、出資額を足してしまうと、持株比率が20%にならない。","en":"Getting 20% for JPY 300 million implies a post-money valuation of 300 / 0.2 = JPY 1.5 billion. The pre-money valuation is 1.5 billion less the 300 million invested, or 1.2 billion. Swapping the two or adding the investment would not give a 20% stake."}},
{"id":"s18x15","dom":"pecase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】PEファンドが存続期間を終え、投資の清算を完了した。LPの出資総額は100億円で、投資の回収は合計180億円だった。ファンド契約では、成功報酬（キャリー）は利益の20%で、ハードルレートを超えており、フルキャッチアップが適用される。運用報酬や費用を無視した場合、LPの総受取額はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A PE fund has reached the end of its term and completed liquidating its investments. Total LP commitments were JPY 10.0 billion, and total recoveries from the investments were JPY 18.0 billion. Under the fund agreement the carried interest is 20% of profit, the hurdle rate has been cleared and full catch-up applies. Ignoring management fees and expenses, what is the LPs' total receipt?"},"choices":[{"ja":"144億円","en":"JPY 14.4 billion"},{"ja":"180億円","en":"JPY 18.0 billion"},{"ja":"160億円","en":"JPY 16.0 billion"},{"ja":"164億円","en":"JPY 16.4 billion"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"利益は180−100＝80億円。キャリーは80×20%＝16億円で、LPの受取は180−16＝164億円（元本100億円と利益の80%にあたる64億円）である。回収総額の20%を引くと144億円になり、元本にまで成功報酬を掛ける誤りである。","en":"Profit is 18.0 - 10.0 = JPY 8.0 billion. Carry is 8.0 x 20% = 1.6 billion, so the LPs receive 18.0 - 1.6 = 16.4 billion (principal of 10.0 billion plus 80% of profit, 6.4 billion). Taking 20% of total proceeds gives 14.4 billion, wrongly charging carry on principal."}},
{"id":"s18x16","dom":"turnaround","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】従業員1,000人の機械メーカーが、売上の3年連続の減少で営業赤字が続いている。経営陣は人件費の削減を急ぎ、事務部門（250人）の20%にあたる50人の解雇を検討している。労働組合との協議はまだ始まっていない。日本の労働法の考え方（整理解雇の判断要素）に沿って、解雇の前にまず行うべきことはどれか。","en":"[Case] A machinery maker with 1,000 employees has run operating losses as sales fell for three years in a row. Management wants to cut labor costs quickly and is considering dismissing 50 people, 20% of its 250-person office department. Talks with the labor union have not yet begun. Following Japanese labor law's approach to redundancy dismissals, what should it do first before dismissing anyone?"},"choices":[{"ja":"役員報酬の削減、採用の停止、配置転換、希望退職の募集など、解雇を避けるための努力を尽くす","en":"Exhaust efforts to avoid dismissals, such as cutting executive pay, freezing hiring, reassigning staff and inviting voluntary retirement"},{"ja":"経営状況を従業員に説明せず、対象者を直ちに選定して一方的に通知する","en":"Select the staff at once and notify them unilaterally without explaining the company's situation"},{"ja":"人員削減の必要性が認められれば、人選や手続の合理性は問われないので、解雇回避の努力を省いて直ちに解雇する","en":"Dismiss immediately without efforts to avoid dismissal, since once the need to cut staff is accepted the reasonableness of selection and procedure is not examined"},{"ja":"人件費削減の効果が大きい勤続年数の長い従業員から順に、一律に解雇の対象とする","en":"Make employees with the longest service the targets in order, since they yield the largest labor cost savings"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"整理解雇は、人員削減の必要性、解雇回避努力、人選の合理性、手続の妥当性の4つの要素から有効性を判断する（裁判例）。解雇の前に、役員報酬の削減、採用停止、配置転換、希望退職の募集などを尽くす必要がある。必要性があれば直ちに解雇できるという考えは誤りである。","en":"Courts judge the validity of a redundancy dismissal on four elements: the necessity of cutting staff, efforts to avoid dismissal, the reasonableness of selection, and the fairness of procedure. Before dismissing, the company must exhaust steps such as cutting executive pay, freezing hiring, reassignment and voluntary retirement. Necessity alone does not permit immediate dismissal."}},
{"id":"s18x17","dom":"turnaround","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】取引先の中小企業を約300社抱える食品メーカーが、売上の減少で金融機関への返済が困難になった。債務は借入金200億円のみで、商取引債権（買掛金）は約定どおり支払い、事業の信用を保ちたい。また、法的整理による風評は避けたい。最も適した手段はどれか。","en":"[Case] A food manufacturer that deals with about 300 small suppliers can no longer service its bank debt as sales decline. Its only debt is JPY 20.0 billion of borrowings, and it wants to keep paying trade payables on schedule to preserve business credibility. It also wants to avoid the stigma of formal proceedings. Which approach is most suitable?"},"choices":[{"ja":"金融債権者だけを対象とし、商取引債権は対象外とする私的整理（事業再生ADRなど）で返済猶予や減免を協議する","en":"Negotiate payment deferral or reduction through a private workout (such as business turnaround ADR) covering financial creditors only and excluding trade claims"},{"ja":"民事再生を申し立て、取引先を含むすべての債権者に債権の一部カットと支払猶予を求めて、法的な手続で一律に処理する","en":"File for civil rehabilitation and ask all creditors, including suppliers, for a partial haircut and payment deferral, handling everything uniformly through formal proceedings"},{"ja":"買掛金の支払を止め、取引先に支払猶予を求めて、資金を確保する","en":"Stop paying trade payables and ask suppliers for payment extensions to secure cash"},{"ja":"破産を申し立てて事業を終了し、取引先への債務をまとめて整理する","en":"File for bankruptcy, end the business and settle supplier obligations all at once"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"私的整理（事業再生ADRなど）は金融債権者のみを対象にでき、商取引債権を通常どおり払うので、取引先の信用や風評を保てる。民事再生では商取引債権も原則として再生債権になり、取引先への影響が大きい。買掛金の支払猶予は、仕入先の信用を失い事業を止めかねない。","en":"A private workout such as business turnaround ADR can cover financial creditors only while trade claims are paid as usual, preserving supplier confidence and reputation. In civil rehabilitation trade claims generally become rehabilitation claims too, hitting suppliers hard. Delaying payables could cost the company its suppliers' trust and stop operations."}},
{"id":"s18x18","dom":"turnaround","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】債務超過30億円に陥った機械部品メーカーが、メインバンクを含む金融機関と再建計画を協議している。計画では、金融機関が借入金40億円の債権放棄を行い、会社は事業の黒字化に取り組む。債務免除益への課税は考えないものとして、放棄後の純資産はどうなるか。","en":"[Case] A machinery parts maker with a JPY 3.0 billion balance sheet deficit is negotiating a turnaround plan with its financial institutions, including its main bank. Under the plan the lenders waive JPY 4.0 billion of loans while the company works to return to profit. Ignoring tax on the debt forgiveness gain, what is net assets after the waiver?"},"choices":[{"ja":"30億円の債務超過のままである","en":"Still a deficit of JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"10億円の資産超過になる","en":"A surplus of JPY 1.0 billion"},{"ja":"10億円の債務超過になる","en":"A deficit of JPY 1.0 billion"},{"ja":"70億円の資産超過になる","en":"A surplus of JPY 7.0 billion"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"債権放棄を受けた会社は、免除された40億円を債務免除益として計上し、純資産が同額増える。−30億円に+40億円で、10億円の資産超過になる。実務では債務免除益への課税が生じうるので、欠損金の利用などを事前に整理する必要がある。","en":"A company receiving a waiver books the JPY 4.0 billion forgiven as a debt forgiveness gain, raising net assets by the same amount: -3.0 billion + 4.0 billion = a 1.0 billion surplus. In practice the gain can be taxed, so use of tax losses and similar items should be worked out in advance."}},
{"id":"s18x19","dom":"turnaround","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】事業再生中の総合メーカーで、財務部門が赤字のX事業の撤退を提案している。X事業は、売上20億円、変動費14億円、X事業固有の固定費4億円（撤退すれば全額なくなる）、全社共通費の配賦5億円（撤退しても共通費は減らない）で、配賦後は3億円の営業赤字である。X事業を撤退した場合の全社の営業利益への影響はどれか。","en":"[Case] In a diversified manufacturer under restructuring, the finance department proposes closing loss-making business X. X has sales of JPY 2.0 billion, variable costs of 1.4 billion, fixed costs specific to X of 400 million (eliminated entirely if X is closed) and allocated corporate overhead of 500 million (not reduced by closing X), leaving an operating loss of 300 million after allocation. What is the effect of closing X on company-wide operating profit?"},"choices":[{"ja":"3億円改善する","en":"It improves by JPY 300 million"},{"ja":"6億円悪化する","en":"It worsens by JPY 600 million"},{"ja":"影響はなく、全社の営業利益は変わらない","en":"There is no effect and company-wide operating profit is unchanged"},{"ja":"2億円悪化する","en":"It worsens by JPY 200 million"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"撤退で失う貢献利益は20−14＝6億円で、減らせる固有の固定費は4億円なので、差し引き2億円の利益が失われる。共通費の配賦5億円は撤退しても他の事業が負担するため、配賦後の3億円の赤字がそのまま解消されるわけではない。","en":"Closing X loses contribution margin of 20 - 14 = JPY 600 million and saves 400 million of X's own fixed costs, so profit falls by 200 million net. The 500 million of allocated overhead stays and is borne by other businesses, so the 300 million post-allocation loss does not simply disappear."}},
{"id":"s18x20","dom":"turnaround","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】再生中の卸売会社は、年間売上が365億円（1日あたり1億円）で、売掛金の回収日数が75日と長く、資金繰りが逼迫している。主要顧客との条件見直しで、回収日数を60日にできる見通しが立った。この改善で生じる資金の解放額はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A wholesaler under restructuring has annual sales of JPY 36.5 billion (JPY 100 million a day) and a long receivables collection period of 75 days, which strains its cash flow. Revised terms with key customers should cut the collection period to 60 days. How much cash does the improvement release?"},"choices":[{"ja":"75億円","en":"JPY 7.5 billion"},{"ja":"60億円","en":"JPY 6.0 billion"},{"ja":"15億円","en":"JPY 1.5 billion"},{"ja":"135億円","en":"JPY 13.5 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"売掛金残高は1日あたり売上×回収日数である。75日なら75億円、60日なら60億円で、差の15億円が現金として解放される。残高そのものの75億円や60億円は解放額ではなく、2つを足した135億円は意味を持たない。","en":"The receivables balance is daily sales times collection days: 75 days gives JPY 7.5 billion and 60 days gives 6.0 billion, so the 1.5 billion difference is released as cash. The balances themselves are not the released amount, and their sum (13.5 billion) has no meaning."}},
{"id":"s18x21","dom":"turnaround","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】再生計画を策定中の会社が、メインバンクに返済条件の見直しを求めている。年間の返済原資（償却前の営業キャッシュ・フロー）は12億円で、年間の元金返済が10億円、利息が4億円である。返済原資を元利返済額で割った比率（DSCR）と、取るべき対応の組合せとして最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] A company drawing up a turnaround plan is asking its main bank to revisit repayment terms. It generates JPY 1.2 billion a year of cash flow available for debt service (operating cash flow before depreciation), against annual principal repayments of 1.0 billion and interest of 400 million. Which pair of the ratio of cash available to total debt service (DSCR) and the action to take is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約1.20倍で年間の元金返済額を上回るため、返済の原資に問題はなく、現行の返済条件をそのまま維持する","en":"About 1.20x, above annual principal repayments, so there is no problem with the repayment source and the current repayment terms are kept as they are"},{"ja":"約0.86倍だが、不足する2億円は新規の借入を重ねて賄う方針とする","en":"About 0.86x, but the JPY 200 million shortfall is to be covered by repeatedly raising new borrowings"},{"ja":"約3.0倍で支払利息を営業キャッシュ・フローで十分に賄えるため、元金返済を含めて返済に問題はない","en":"About 3.0x, which covers interest expense comfortably out of operating cash flow, so there is no repayment problem including principal"},{"ja":"約0.86倍で1倍を下回り返済原資が不足するため、元金の返済猶予など条件変更を金融機関と協議する","en":"About 0.86x, below 1x so cash available is short; negotiate changed terms such as a deferral of principal with the banks"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"DSCR＝12÷(10＋4)＝約0.86倍で、返済原資が元利返済額に2億円足りない。1倍を下回るため、元金の返済猶予や条件変更を協議する必要がある。元金だけで割った1.2倍や、利息だけで割った3.0倍は、元利合計を見ていない。","en":"DSCR = 1.2 / (1.0 + 0.4) = about 0.86x, leaving cash flow JPY 200 million short of debt service. Below 1x, deferral of principal or changed terms must be negotiated. The 1.2x (principal only) and 3.0x (interest only) ignore the combined repayment."}},
{"id":"s18x22","dom":"turnaround","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】資本金100億円の大法人が、過去の赤字で100億円の繰越欠損金を持つ。再生が進み、当期の課税所得（繰越欠損金控除前）は60億円となった。再生手続中ではなく、実効税率は30%で、繰越欠損金の控除は所得の50%が上限とする。当期の法人税等の概算はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A large corporation with JPY 10.0 billion of capital has JPY 10.0 billion of tax loss carryforwards from past losses. Its recovery is progressing and taxable income this year, before loss deduction, is 6.0 billion. It is not in rehabilitation proceedings, the effective tax rate is 30%, and the deduction of loss carryforwards is capped at 50% of income. What is the approximate corporate tax for the year?"},"choices":[{"ja":"9億円","en":"JPY 900 million"},{"ja":"18億円","en":"JPY 1.8 billion"},{"ja":"0円","en":"Zero"},{"ja":"6.3億円","en":"JPY 630 million"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"繰越欠損金の控除は、大法人では所得の50%が上限である（2026年10月時点）。60億円の50%の30億円を控除し、残る課税所得30億円に30%を掛けた9億円が税額となる。欠損金が100億円あっても全額は使えず、黒字転換の直後でも納税が生じるため、資金繰りに織り込む。","en":"For large corporations, deduction of loss carryforwards is capped at 50% of income (as of October 2026). Deducting 50% of 6.0 billion, or 3.0 billion, leaves taxable income of 3.0 billion, and 30% of that is JPY 900 million in tax. Despite 10.0 billion of losses they cannot all be used, so tax arises right after a return to profit and must be built into cash planning."}},
{"id":"s18x23","dom":"growthcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】法人向けSaaS事業のA社は、月額2万円の契約で粗利率は80%、月次の解約率は2%である。新規顧客1社の獲得費用（CAC）は25万円で、広告費と営業費用の合計から算出している。解約率から顧客の平均継続月数を50か月としたとき、LTV（粗利ベース）とLTV/CACの組合せはどれか。","en":"[Case] SaaS company A sells to businesses at JPY 20,000 a month per contract with an 80% gross margin and monthly churn of 2%. Acquiring one new customer (CAC) costs JPY 250,000, calculated from total advertising and sales expenses. Taking the average customer lifetime from churn as 50 months, which pair gives the LTV (gross-profit basis) and LTV/CAC?"},"choices":[{"ja":"80万円で3.2倍","en":"JPY 800,000 and 3.2x"},{"ja":"100万円で4.0倍","en":"JPY 1,000,000 and 4.0x"},{"ja":"40万円で1.6倍","en":"JPY 400,000 and 1.6x"},{"ja":"64万円で2.6倍","en":"JPY 640,000 and 2.6x"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"1顧客の月次粗利は2万×80%＝1.6万円で、50か月分のLTVは80万円。CAC25万円で割ると3.2倍で、目安の3倍を上回る。粗利率を無視すると100万円（4.0倍）と過大になる。解約率2%は平均継続月数が1÷0.02＝50か月に対応する。","en":"Monthly gross profit per customer is 20,000 x 80% = JPY 16,000, so 50 months gives an LTV of JPY 800,000. Divided by the 250,000 CAC, that is 3.2x, above the usual rule of thumb of 3x. Ignoring the margin overstates LTV at 1,000,000 (4.0x). Churn of 2% corresponds to an average lifetime of 1 / 0.02 = 50 months."}},
{"id":"s18x24","dom":"growthcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】国内で40店舗を展開する小売業のA社は、国内の成長に限界を感じ、ある新興国市場へ店舗網を速く広げたいと考えている。この国では外国企業の出資比率に上限があり、許認可や不動産の取得には現地の人脈が欠かせない。A社に現地の運営ノウハウは乏しい。参入形態として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Japanese retailer A, which runs 40 stores at home, feels its domestic growth is capped and wants to expand its store network quickly in an emerging market. In that country foreign ownership is capped, and local connections are essential for permits and real estate. A has little local operating know-how. Which mode of entry is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"現地の有力企業との合弁（JV）で出資比率の規制を満たしつつ、許認可と運営のノウハウを補う","en":"A joint venture (JV) with a strong local company, meeting the ownership cap while supplying permits and operating know-how"},{"ja":"規制にかかわらず、100%出資の子会社を設立し、自社の人材だけで運営する","en":"Set up a wholly owned subsidiary regardless of the rules and run it with its own people only"},{"ja":"規制を回避するため、名義だけの現地企業に出資比率を持たせ、実質的な支配と運営は自社が完全に行う","en":"Avoid the rules by giving a nominal local entity the ownership share while A exercises full control and operation in substance"},{"ja":"輸出のみを行い、現地には店舗も法人も設けない","en":"Only export and set up neither stores nor a local entity"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"外資の出資比率に上限があり、許認可や運営に現地の知見が要る市場では、現地有力企業との合弁が、規制を満たしながら速度を確保しやすい。規制を無視した100%出資は認められず、名義だけの出資で実質支配とする方法は違法性や契約の無効リスクが高い。","en":"Where foreign ownership is capped and local knowledge is needed for permits and operations, a JV with a strong local partner best combines speed with compliance. Wholly owned entry ignoring the cap is not allowed, and nominee structures for control in substance carry high risk of illegality and contract invalidity."}},
{"id":"s18x25","dom":"growthcase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】産業機械メーカーのA社は、原材料費の高騰を受け、売上100億円、粗利率30%（変動費率70%）の主力製品の価格を5%上げる方針である。固定費は変わらない。販売数量の減少が何%を超えると、値上げ後の粗利益は値上げ前を下回るか。最も近いものを選べ。","en":"[Case] Industrial machinery maker A plans to raise the price of its main product by 5% because of rising material costs. The product has sales of JPY 10.0 billion and a 30% gross margin (70% variable cost ratio), and fixed costs do not change. Beyond what percentage decline in sales volume does gross profit fall below its pre-increase level? Choose the closest."},"choices":[{"ja":"約5.0%","en":"About 5.0%"},{"ja":"約30.0%","en":"About 30.0%"},{"ja":"約16.7%","en":"About 16.7%"},{"ja":"約14.3%","en":"About 14.3%"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"値上げ前は価格100に対し粗利30。5%上げると価格105、変動費70で粗利は35になる。粗利益が同額となる数量は30÷35＝約85.7%で、減少率が約14.3%を超えると粗利益は減る。5÷30＝16.7%は、値上げ後の粗利が35に増える効果を見ていない。","en":"Before the increase, gross profit is 30 on a price of 100. After a 5% rise the price is 105 against variable cost of 70, so gross profit per unit is 35. Gross profit stays equal at 30 / 35 = about 85.7% of volume, so a decline beyond about 14.3% reduces gross profit. Dividing 5 by 30 (16.7%) ignores that the new unit margin is 35."}},
{"id":"s18x26","dom":"growthcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】新規の業務SaaSを検討するA社の事業計画では、国内の対象企業全体の年間支出は1,000億円、A社の製品が対応する機能と企業規模に限った市場は300億円、販売体制から5年で獲得できると見込むシェアはその10%である。5年後に見込める売上（SOM）はいくらか。","en":"[Case] In company A's plan for a new business SaaS product, total annual spending by target companies in Japan is JPY 100.0 billion, the market limited to the functions and company sizes A's product serves is 30.0 billion, and the share achievable within five years given its sales capacity is 10% of that. What is the revenue expected in year five (SOM)?"},"choices":[{"ja":"30億円","en":"JPY 3.0 billion"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10.0 billion"},{"ja":"300億円","en":"JPY 30.0 billion"},{"ja":"3億円","en":"JPY 300 million"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"市場規模は、全体のTAM（1,000億円）、自社の製品・顧客層で狙えるSAM（300億円）、実際に獲得できるSOM（SAMの10%で30億円）の順に絞る。事業計画の売上はSOMで置くべきで、TAMの10%（100億円）やSAM全体を計画に使うと過大になる。","en":"Market size narrows from TAM (JPY 100.0 billion), to SAM, what the product and customer segment can address (30.0 billion), to SOM, what can actually be won (10% of SAM, or 3.0 billion). A plan's revenue should be built on SOM; using 10% of TAM (10.0 billion) or all of SAM would be too high."}},
{"id":"s18x27","dom":"growthcase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】複合企業のA社は、事業X（EBITDA 100億円、同業の倍率8倍）と事業Y（EBITDA 50億円、同業の倍率12倍）を持ち、本社コストが年10億円（8倍で資本化）かかる。純有利子負債は300億円、時価総額は800億円である。事業ごとの価値を合算（SOTP）して求めた株式価値と、現在の時価総額との関係はどれか。","en":"[Case] Conglomerate A owns business X (EBITDA JPY 10.0 billion, peer multiple 8x) and business Y (EBITDA 5.0 billion, peer multiple 12x) and bears corporate costs of 1.0 billion a year (capitalized at 8x). Net debt is 30.0 billion and market capitalization is 80.0 billion. How does the equity value from a sum-of-the-parts (SOTP) valuation compare with the market capitalization?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1,100億円で、時価総額を300億円上回る","en":"JPY 110.0 billion, which is 30.0 billion above market capitalization"},{"ja":"1,020億円で、時価総額を220億円上回る","en":"JPY 102.0 billion, which is 22.0 billion above market capitalization"},{"ja":"1,320億円で、時価総額を520億円上回る","en":"JPY 132.0 billion, which is 52.0 billion above market capitalization"},{"ja":"1,400億円で、時価総額を600億円上回る","en":"JPY 140.0 billion, which is 60.0 billion above market capitalization"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"X事業の価値は100×8＝800億円、Y事業は50×12＝600億円で合計1,400億円。本社コストの資本化額80億円（10×8）と純有利子負債300億円を引くと、株式価値は1,020億円となる。時価総額の800億円を220億円上回り、複合企業の割引が示唆される。","en":"Business X is worth 10.0 x 8 = JPY 80.0 billion and Y is worth 5.0 x 12 = 60.0 billion, a total of 140.0 billion. Deducting capitalized corporate costs of 8.0 billion (1.0 x 8) and net debt of 30.0 billion leaves equity value of 102.0 billion, 22.0 billion above the 80.0 billion market capitalization, which suggests a conglomerate discount."}},
{"id":"s18x28","dom":"growthcase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】SaaS企業のA社の期初のARR（年間経常収益）は100億円。1年間で、既存顧客のアップセルが+15億円、解約が−8億円、ダウングレードが−2億円、新規顧客の獲得が+30億円だった。NRR（ネット・レベニュー・リテンション）と、成長の質についての評価として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] SaaS company A started the year with ARR (annual recurring revenue) of JPY 10.0 billion. Over the year, upsell from existing customers added 1.5 billion, churn removed 800 million, downgrades removed 200 million, and new customers added 3.0 billion. Which statement on NRR (net revenue retention) and the quality of growth is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"NRRは145%で、新規獲得を含めた成長率が高く、成長の質は非常に高い","en":"NRR is 145%; growth including new customers is high, so growth quality is very high"},{"ja":"NRRは105%で、新規を除いても既存顧客だけで拡大しており、既存基盤の質は良い","en":"NRR is 105%; the existing base grows even without new customers, so its quality is good"},{"ja":"NRRは90%で、解約とダウングレードがあるため、既存顧客だけでは縮小している","en":"NRR is 90%; with churn and downgrades the existing base alone is shrinking"},{"ja":"NRRは115%で、アップセルだけを数えれば足りるので、解約は成長の質に影響しない","en":"NRR is 115%; only upsell needs counting, so churn does not affect the quality of growth"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"NRRは新規を除いた既存顧客の売上推移で、(100＋15−8−2)÷100＝105%。新規獲得の30億円を含めた145%は成長率であってNRRではない。90%は解約とダウングレードだけを見たグロス・リテンションで、アップセルを無視している。","en":"NRR tracks revenue from existing customers only, excluding new customers: (100 + 15 - 8 - 2) / 100 = 105%. The 145% that includes JPY 3.0 billion of new business is a growth rate, not NRR. The 90% is gross retention, which looks only at churn and downgrades and ignores upsell."}},
{"id":"s18x29","dom":"growthcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】外食チェーンを運営するA社が、飲食店と利用客を結ぶ予約プラットフォームを新規事業として立ち上げる。現状は、店舗が少ないと利用客が来ず、利用客が少ないと店舗が参加しない状態にある。初期の予算は年5億円に限られる。参入初期の施策として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Restaurant chain operator A is launching a reservation platform linking restaurants and diners as a new business. At present, with few restaurants diners do not come, and with few diners restaurants do not join. The initial budget is limited to JPY 500 million a year. Which initial-stage measure is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"利用客と店舗の両方に高い手数料を課し、初期から黒字を確保する","en":"Charge high fees to both diners and restaurants to be profitable from the start"},{"ja":"利用客が増えれば店舗は自然に集まると考え、店舗の募集は行わず、利用客向けの広告だけを大幅に増やして認知度を高める","en":"Assume restaurants will gather naturally as diners grow, skip recruiting restaurants and sharply increase advertising to diners to raise awareness"},{"ja":"店舗を集めたあと、利用客向けの機能は設けず、店舗向けの管理機能の販売だけで収益を得る","en":"After gathering restaurants, build no diner-facing features and earn revenue only by selling management tools to restaurants"},{"ja":"参加のハードルが高い側の店舗の手数料を無料にするなど補助して先に集め、品ぞろえが整ってから利用客を増やす","en":"Subsidize the side with the higher barrier to joining, for example by waiving fees for restaurants, gather them first, and grow the diners once the selection is in place"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"両サイドの規模が互いに必要なプラットフォームでは、どちらかを補助で先に確保する必要がある。この例では、利用客が来る理由になる店舗を先に集めるため、手数料の無料化などで参加を促す。両側に高い手数料を課すと、どちらも集まらず、ネットワーク効果が働かない。","en":"On a platform where each side needs the other, one side must be secured first with subsidies. Here restaurants give diners a reason to come, so fee waivers help recruit them first. Charging both sides high fees keeps both away, and the network effect never takes hold."}},
{"id":"s18x30","dom":"capitalcase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】発行済株式1億株、株価1,000円（時価総額1,000億円）の会社が、成長投資の資金を賄うため、2,000万株の公募増資を、5%のディスカウントとなる1株950円で実施する。調達資金によって事業価値は変わらないとした場合、増資後の理論株価に最も近いのはどれか。","en":"[Case] A company with 100 million shares outstanding at JPY 1,000 each (market capitalization JPY 100.0 billion) issues 20 million new shares in a public offering at JPY 950, a 5% discount, to fund growth investment. Assuming the proceeds do not change the value of the business, which is closest to the theoretical share price after the offering?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約950円","en":"About JPY 950"},{"ja":"約992円","en":"About JPY 992"},{"ja":"約1,000円","en":"About JPY 1,000"},{"ja":"約975円","en":"About JPY 975"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"増資前の時価総額1,000億円に調達額190億円を足した1,190億円を、増資後の1.2億株で割ると約992円になる。新株を安く発行した分だけ既存株主の1株価値が薄まる（希薄化）。1,000円のままや950円とするのは、株数と調達額の影響を見ていない。","en":"Market capitalization of JPY 100.0 billion plus proceeds of 19.0 billion makes 119.0 billion, and dividing by the 120 million shares after the offering gives about JPY 992. Issuing new shares at a discount dilutes the value per existing share. Keeping 1,000 or moving to 950 ignores the effect of share count and proceeds."}},
{"id":"s18x31","dom":"capitalcase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】上場のA社が、取締役会で、ある事業会社への第三者割当増資を決議する。決議の前日の終値は1,000円で、割当先との交渉で払込金額を850円とする案が出ている。日本証券業協会の指針は払込金額を前日の終値などの90%以上とすることを求めている。この案への対応として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Listed company A's board is resolving on a third-party allotment to a business company. The closing price the day before the resolution was JPY 1,000, and negotiations with the allottee point to an issue price of JPY 850. The Japan Securities Dealers Association's guidelines call for an issue price of at least 90% of the prior day's closing price and similar benchmarks. What is the most appropriate response?"},"choices":[{"ja":"取締役会の決議があれば、払込金額が時価より何%低くても会社法上有効なので、株主総会には諮らず案のまま進める","en":"Proceed as proposed without going to the shareholders' meeting, since a board resolution is valid under the Companies Act however far below market the issue price is"},{"ja":"有利発行の可能性が高いので、900円以上に見直すか、株主総会の特別決議で理由を説明して発行する","en":"A favorable issuance is likely, so revise the price to JPY 900 or more, or explain the reasons at a special resolution of the shareholders' meeting and issue"},{"ja":"有利発行にあたるかどうかは割当先が判断することなので、A社は払込金額を見直す必要はない","en":"A need not revisit the price, because whether it is a favorable issuance is for the allottee to decide"},{"ja":"払込金額が850円でも、発行後に株価が上がれば問題がないので、案のまま進める","en":"Proceed as proposed, since a price of JPY 850 is not a problem if the share price rises after issuance"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"時価を大きく下回る払込金額は「特に有利な金額」とされうるため、日本証券業協会の指針は直前日価額の90%以上を目安とする。85%の850円は目安を下回り、会社法上、株主総会の特別決議で有利発行の理由を説明する必要がある。取締役会の決議だけで進めることはできない。","en":"An issue price far below market can be a 'particularly favorable' price, so the JSDA guidelines use 90% of the prior day's price as a benchmark. At 85%, JPY 850 falls below it, and under the Companies Act the reasons for a favorable issue must be explained at a special resolution of the shareholders' meeting. A board resolution alone is not enough."}},
{"id":"s18x32","dom":"capitalcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】成長投資の資金を探している株価1,000円の会社が、利率0%で転換価額1,250円（プレミアム25%）の転換社債型新株予約権付社債を100億円発行することにした。株主への希薄化を試算するため、全額が株式に転換された場合に増える株式数を求めたい。それはどれか。","en":"[Case] A company with a share price of JPY 1,000 that is looking for growth funding decides to issue JPY 10.0 billion of zero-coupon convertible bonds with a conversion price of JPY 1,250 (a 25% premium). To estimate dilution for shareholders, it wants to know how many shares are added if all of the bonds convert. Which figure is it?"},"choices":[{"ja":"1,000万株","en":"10 million shares"},{"ja":"1,250万株","en":"12.5 million shares"},{"ja":"80万株","en":"0.8 million shares"},{"ja":"800万株","en":"8 million shares"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"転換で増える株数は、社債額÷転換価額＝100億円÷1,250円＝800万株である。時価の1,000円で割った1,000万株は、転換価額を取り違えている。利率が0%の分、将来の希薄化を受け入れる代わりに調達コストを抑えられる。","en":"Shares added on conversion equal the bond amount divided by the conversion price: JPY 10.0 billion / 1,250 = 8 million shares. Dividing by the market price of 1,000 (10 million) uses the wrong price. A zero coupon is traded off against future dilution, which lowers funding cost."}},
{"id":"s18x33","dom":"capitalcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】創業から15年のメーカーが、東京証券取引所への上場（IPO）を準備している。IPOでは、会社が発行する公募500万株と、創業者による売出し300万株を、公開価格2,000円で実施する。引受手数料など発行諸費用を無視する場合、会社が受け取る資金はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A 15-year-old manufacturer is preparing an IPO on the Tokyo Stock Exchange. In the IPO, 5 million shares are offered by the company and 3 million shares are sold by the founder, all at an offer price of JPY 2,000. Ignoring underwriting fees and other issuance costs, how much does the company receive?"},"choices":[{"ja":"160億円","en":"JPY 16.0 billion"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10.0 billion"},{"ja":"60億円","en":"JPY 6.0 billion"},{"ja":"0円","en":"Zero"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"公募は会社が新株を発行して資金を得るため、500万株×2,000円＝100億円が会社に入る。売出しは創業者が持ち株を売る取引で、売却代金は創業者に入り、会社の資金調達にはならない。総額160億円は会社の手取りではない。","en":"In the primary offering the company issues new shares, so 5 million x JPY 2,000 = JPY 10.0 billion goes to the company. The secondary sale is the founder selling existing shares, so the proceeds go to the founder, not to the company. The total of 16.0 billion is not the company's take."}},
{"id":"s18x34","dom":"capitalcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】有利子負債600億円の素材メーカーで、来期に400億円の借入が一斉に満期を迎える。業績は安定し、財務制限条項への抵触の恐れもないが、金融引締めが進んでおり、借換え条件の悪化が懸念される。財務部長が資金調達の計画を見直すとき、最も適切な対応はどれか。","en":"[Case] A materials maker with JPY 60.0 billion of interest-bearing debt has JPY 40.0 billion of loans all maturing next year. Results are stable and no covenant is near a breach, but monetary tightening is under way and refinancing terms may worsen. As the finance head reviews the funding plan, which response is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"借換えを前倒しで進め、社債や長期借入、複数の金融機関に分散して、返済の満期を年度ごとに平準化する","en":"Refinance ahead of schedule, spreading across bonds, long-term loans and several banks to even out maturities year by year"},{"ja":"満期の直前に、メインバンクへ全額の借換えを依頼する","en":"Ask the main bank to refinance the full amount just before maturity"},{"ja":"手元の現金を全額返済に充て、運転資金は売掛金の回収だけで賄う","en":"Use all cash on hand for repayment and fund working capital from receivable collections only"},{"ja":"短期借入を何度も重ねて借換えの頻度を高め、金利が下がる局面を見計らって有利な条件で借換えを行い、満期の集中は気にしない","en":"Roll short-term loans repeatedly to refinance more often, timing it for when rates fall to get favorable terms, and not worry about concentrated maturities"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"満期が一部の年度に集中すると、その時期の市況や貸し手の姿勢に調達条件が左右される。前倒しの借換えや、社債・長期借入・複数行への分散で満期を平準化し、借換えリスクを抑える。直前に1行へ全額を依頼する方法や、現金を使い切る方法は、流動性の危険を高める。","en":"When maturities are concentrated in one year, funding terms depend on market conditions and lender attitudes at that time. Early refinancing and spreading across bonds, long-term loans and several banks evens out maturities and cuts refinancing risk. Asking one bank at the last minute or using up all cash raises liquidity risk."}},
{"id":"s18x35","dom":"capitalcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】PEファンドが、EBITDA 100億円の会社をLBOで買収する計画を立てている。資金計画では、シニアローンの上限が純有利子負債/EBITDAで4.0倍までと決まったが、買収価格にはさらにEBITDAの1.5倍分の資金が足りない。ファンドはエクイティの増額を最小限に抑えたい。最も適切な資金調達はどれか。","en":"[Case] A PE fund is planning an LBO of a company with EBITDA of JPY 10.0 billion. In the financing plan the senior loan is capped at 4.0x net debt/EBITDA, but funding equal to a further 1.5x EBITDA is still needed for the purchase price. The fund wants to minimize additional equity. Which financing is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"シニアローンの上限を、貸し手の同意なしに5.5倍へ引き上げる","en":"Raise the senior loan cap to 5.5x without the lenders' consent"},{"ja":"新たに、シニアローンより返済順位が高い優先ローンを追加して借りる","en":"Borrow an additional priority loan ranking ahead of the senior loan"},{"ja":"運転資金のコミットメントラインを引き出して、買収代金の不足分に充てる","en":"Draw on the working capital commitment line and use it for the purchase price shortfall"},{"ja":"返済順位がシニアより劣後し金利が高いメザニン・ローンで不足分を補う","en":"Fill the gap with a mezzanine loan, which ranks below senior debt and carries a higher interest rate"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"シニアの上限を超える不足分は、返済順位が劣後し金利は高いがエクイティより低コストのメザニン・ローンで補うのが一般的である。貸し手の同意なしに上限を引き上げることはできず、運転資金枠を買収代金に充てると資金使途や財務制限条項に反する。","en":"A gap above the senior cap is typically filled with a mezzanine loan, which ranks lower and costs more than senior debt but less than equity. The cap cannot be raised without lender consent, and using the working capital line for the purchase price breaches its permitted use and covenants."}},
{"id":"s18x36","dom":"capitalcase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】個人株主の少ない会社が、株価の高さが個人投資家の投資の障壁になっていると考えている。現在の株価は50,000円、発行済株式数は200万株で、買いやすさを高めるため、1株を5株にする株式分割を行う。分割後の理論株価と発行済株式数、時価総額の組合せはどれか。他の条件は変わらないものとする。","en":"[Case] A company with few individual shareholders believes its high share price is a barrier to investment. The current price is JPY 50,000 and 2 million shares are outstanding, and it splits each share into five to make the stock easier for individual investors to buy. Which combination gives the theoretical share price, shares outstanding and market capitalization after the split? Assume all else is unchanged."},"choices":[{"ja":"10,000円、1,000万株で、時価総額は5倍の5,000億円","en":"JPY 10,000, 10 million shares, and market capitalization up fivefold to JPY 500.0 billion"},{"ja":"株価は50,000円のまま、1,000万株に増え、時価総額は5倍の5,000億円になる","en":"The share price stays at JPY 50,000, shares rise to 10 million, and market capitalization rises fivefold to JPY 500.0 billion"},{"ja":"10,000円、1,000万株で、時価総額は変わらず1,000億円","en":"JPY 10,000, 10 million shares, and market capitalization unchanged at JPY 100.0 billion"},{"ja":"10,000円、200万株で、時価総額は200億円","en":"JPY 10,000, 2 million shares, and market capitalization of JPY 20.0 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"1株を5株にする分割で株数は1,000万株に増え、理論株価は50,000÷5＝10,000円となり、時価総額は1,000億円のまま変わらない。分割は企業価値を増やさず、少額から買えるようになって流動性を高める効果が主である。","en":"Splitting each share into five raises the share count to 10 million and the theoretical price to 50,000 / 5 = JPY 10,000, leaving market capitalization unchanged at JPY 100.0 billion. A split creates no value; its main effect is better liquidity from a lower entry price."}},
{"id":"s18x37","dom":"crisiscase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】食品卸のA社は、売掛金12億円を持つ主要取引先が、破産手続の開始を申し立てたとの連絡を受けた。この取引先はA社の売上の約1割を占める。A社が取得している担保の処分で、4億円の回収が見込まれる。日本基準での貸倒引当金（破産更生債権等の財務内容評価法）の額はいくらか。","en":"[Case] Food wholesaler A learns that a key customer, owing it JPY 1.2 billion in receivables, has filed for bankruptcy. The customer accounts for about 10% of A's sales. Disposal of collateral held by A is expected to recover JPY 400 million. Under Japanese GAAP, what is the allowance for doubtful accounts using the financial condition method for bankruptcy and similar claims?"},"choices":[{"ja":"8億円","en":"JPY 800 million"},{"ja":"12億円","en":"JPY 1.2 billion"},{"ja":"4億円","en":"JPY 400 million"},{"ja":"6億円（債権額の50%）","en":"JPY 600 million (50% of the receivable)"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"破産手続の申立てを受けた債権は、担保などで回収が見込まれる額を除いた残額を貸倒引当金とする。12億円−4億円＝8億円である。債権の全額12億円を引き当てると担保の回収見込みを無視し、50%の6億円は貸倒懸念債権の扱いと混同している。","en":"For a claim against a debtor that has filed for bankruptcy, the allowance covers the balance after the amount expected from collateral: 1.2 billion - 400 million = JPY 800 million. Reserving the whole 1.2 billion ignores collateral, and 50% (600 million) mixes this up with the treatment of doubtful claims."}},
{"id":"s18x38","dom":"crisiscase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】売上1,000億円、原材料費400億円、営業利益80億円の食品メーカーで、原油高と円安を受けて、原材料価格が20%上昇した。他のコストは変わらず、価格を上げても販売数量は変わらないとする。営業利益の金額を元の80億円に保つために必要な値上げ率はいくらか。","en":"[Case] A food manufacturer with sales of JPY 100.0 billion, raw material costs of 40.0 billion and operating profit of 8.0 billion sees raw material prices rise 20% on higher oil prices and a weaker yen. Other costs are unchanged, and sales volume would not change even if prices rise. What price increase is needed to keep operating profit at the original JPY 8.0 billion?"},"choices":[{"ja":"20%","en":"20%"},{"ja":"4%","en":"4%"},{"ja":"40%","en":"40%"},{"ja":"8%","en":"8%"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"原材料費は400億円×20%＝80億円増え、営業利益は0になる。数量が変わらなければ売上を80億円増やせば利益は戻り、必要な値上げ率は80÷1,000＝8%である。原材料の上昇率と同じ20%の値上げは過大で、売上に占める原材料費の割合を考えていない。","en":"Raw material costs rise by 40.0 billion x 20% = JPY 8.0 billion, wiping out operating profit. With volume unchanged, 8.0 billion more in sales restores it, so the required increase is 8.0 / 100.0 = 8%. Matching the 20% input rise overshoots because it ignores that raw materials are only part of sales."}},
{"id":"s18x39","dom":"crisiscase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】日本基準の自動車部品メーカーA社は、製品の欠陥によるリコールの費用を合理的に50億円と見積もれる。A社はリコールに備える保険を契約しており、保険会社との協議では30億円の保険金が支払われる見込みだが、保険会社の確定回答はまだ出ていない。当期の財務諸表での処理として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] Auto parts maker A, which uses Japanese GAAP, can reasonably estimate the cost of a recall caused by a product defect at JPY 5.0 billion. A has recall insurance and, in talks with the insurer, expects a payout of 3.0 billion, but the insurer has not yet given a final answer. Which treatment in this period's financial statements is most appropriate?"},"choices":[{"ja":"50億円の費用（引当金）を当期に計上し、保険金は受領が確定した時点で収益として認識する","en":"Record the JPY 5.0 billion cost (provision) in the current period and recognize the insurance proceeds as income when receipt is confirmed"},{"ja":"保険金30億円を差し引いた20億円だけを、当期に引当金として計上する","en":"Record only JPY 2.0 billion as a provision this period, net of the 3.0 billion insurance proceeds"},{"ja":"保険金の支払が確定するまでは、リコール費用についても引当金を計上せず、注記での開示だけにとどめる","en":"Until the insurance payout is confirmed, book no provision for the recall cost either and limit the treatment to disclosure in the notes"},{"ja":"リコール費用は実際に支出した期に費用計上し、当期は何も計上しない","en":"Expense the recall cost in the period it is actually paid and record nothing this period"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"損失が発生する可能性が高く金額を合理的に見積れる場合、費用・引当金は当期に計上する。一方、保険金は確定するまで収益を認識しない。見込みでネットした20億円とするのは、確定していない収入を先取りする。支出時まで繰り延べるのも、費用の計上時期が誤りである。","en":"When a loss is probable and reasonably estimable, the cost and provision are recorded in the current period. Insurance proceeds, however, are recognized as income only once confirmed. Netting an expected 3.0 billion anticipates unconfirmed income, and deferring the expense until payment gets the timing of the cost wrong."}},
{"id":"s18x40","dom":"crisiscase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】上場会社のA社に不正会計の疑いが生じ、監査法人が監査意見を表明できず、決算発表と有価証券報告書の提出が遅れる見込みである。主要な借入契約には、決算書を期限内に提出する義務と、違反時に期限の利益を失う条項がある。借入残高は300億円である。CFOが最優先で行うべき対応はどれか。","en":"[Case] Listed company A is suspected of accounting fraud, its auditor cannot yet give an opinion, and the earnings release and annual securities report are likely to be late. Its main loan agreement obliges it to deliver financial statements on time and says that a breach causes loss of the benefit of the term. Outstanding borrowings are JPY 30.0 billion. What should the CFO do first?"},"choices":[{"ja":"決算が確定するまで貸し手には知らせず、調査の結果を待ってから報告する","en":"Tell lenders nothing until the accounts are final and report after the investigation results"},{"ja":"貸し手に事情と調査の見通しを早期に説明し、提出期限の猶予（ウェーバー）を事前に取り付ける","en":"Explain the circumstances and investigation outlook to lenders early and obtain a waiver extending the delivery deadline in advance"},{"ja":"借入契約の条項は金融商品取引法上の提出期限とは別のものなので、貸し手に対する特段の説明や手続は不要と考える","en":"Consider no special explanation or procedure with lenders necessary, since the loan clause is separate from the filing deadline under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act"},{"ja":"期限の利益の喪失に備え、手元資金を使って借入を直ちに全額返済する","en":"Prepare for loss of the benefit of the term by immediately repaying all borrowings out of cash on hand"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"決算書の提出遅延は融資契約上の期限の利益喪失事由になりうるため、遅れが確実となる前に貸し手へ説明し、提出期限の猶予を書面で取り付けるのが最優先である。黙って待つと違反が先に確定し、全額の返済請求や取引停止を招く。全額の繰上げ返済は、資金繰りを自ら悪化させる。","en":"Late delivery of financial statements can be an event causing loss of the benefit of the term, so the first priority is to brief lenders before the delay becomes certain and obtain a written extension. Waiting silently lets the breach occur first and invites demands for full repayment or loss of banking relationships. Repaying everything early would itself damage liquidity."}},
{"id":"s18x41","dom":"crisiscase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】ある会社は、短期借入金とコマーシャル・ペーパー（CP）が合計500億円あり、3か月以内に満期を迎える。手元の現預金は150億円、未使用のコミットメントラインは200億円である。金融市場が混乱してCP市場が閉じ、借換えができなくなった場合、追加で必要な資金額はいくらか。ほかの資金の出入りは考えない。","en":"[Case] A company has short-term borrowings and commercial paper (CP) totaling JPY 50.0 billion due within three months. It holds 15.0 billion in cash and deposits and an unused commitment line of 20.0 billion. If financial markets are disrupted, the CP market closes and refinancing becomes impossible, how much additional funding is needed? Ignore other cash flows."},"choices":[{"ja":"350億円","en":"JPY 35.0 billion"},{"ja":"300億円","en":"JPY 30.0 billion"},{"ja":"150億円","en":"JPY 15.0 billion"},{"ja":"500億円","en":"JPY 50.0 billion"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"満期の500億円のうち、手元の現預金150億円と未使用のコミットメントライン200億円で350億円を賄えるため、不足は150億円となる。財務制限条項への抵触などでコミットメントラインが使えなくなる場合は、不足が350億円に膨らむため、その場合の対策も立てておく。","en":"Of the JPY 50.0 billion maturing, cash of 15.0 billion and the unused commitment line of 20.0 billion cover 35.0 billion, leaving a 15.0 billion shortfall. If the line becomes unavailable, for example through a covenant breach, the shortfall swells to 35.0 billion, so contingency plans should cover that case too."}},
{"id":"s18x42","dom":"crisiscase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】IFRSを適用する製造業の会社が、米国で提起された製品訴訟について、顧問弁護士の意見などから、敗訴の可能性が高いと判断している。損害賠償額は80億円から120億円の範囲で、範囲内のどの金額も同程度に起こりうる。引当金の測定額として最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] An IFRS-reporting manufacturer judges, based on its outside counsel's opinion, that it is likely to lose a product liability lawsuit filed in the United States. Damages fall in a range of JPY 8.0 billion to 12.0 billion, and every amount in the range is about equally likely. What is the most appropriate measurement of the provision?"},"choices":[{"ja":"80億円","en":"JPY 8.0 billion"},{"ja":"120億円","en":"JPY 12.0 billion"},{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10.0 billion"},{"ja":"0円（確定するまで注記で開示するだけにとどめる）","en":"Zero (disclose in the notes only until the amount is settled)"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"IAS第37号は、可能性の範囲内のどの金額も同程度に起こりうる場合、中間点を引当金の額とすると定める。80億円と120億円の中間の100億円となる。最低額や最高額の選択は基準の考え方ではなく、敗訴の可能性が高いのに引当を計上しない処理も誤りである。","en":"IAS 37 says that when every amount in a range is about equally likely, the midpoint is used for the provision, here JPY 10.0 billion between 8.0 and 12.0 billion. Choosing the minimum or maximum is not the standard's approach, and booking nothing when a loss is probable is also wrong."}},
{"id":"s18x43","dom":"crisiscase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】IFRSを適用する資源商社が、事業の選択と集中の一環として、ブラジルの子会社の全株式を売却することを決めた。この子会社に関する累積の為替換算差額（その他の包括利益累計額）は、貸方残高で15億円ある。売却時の会計処理はどれか。","en":"[Case] An IFRS-reporting trading company decides, as part of focusing its business portfolio, to sell all shares of its subsidiary in Brazil. The accumulated foreign currency translation differences for this subsidiary (accumulated other comprehensive income) carry a credit balance of JPY 1.5 billion. How is it treated on the sale?"},"choices":[{"ja":"15億円は売却後もその他の包括利益として純資産に残り、損益に振り替えることは一切ない","en":"Leave the JPY 1.5 billion in other comprehensive income within net assets even after the sale and never reclassify it to profit or loss"},{"ja":"15億円を、売却による資本剰余金の増加として処理する","en":"Treat the JPY 1.5 billion as an increase in capital surplus resulting from the sale"},{"ja":"15億円を、売却価額から控除して子会社株式の取得原価に加算する","en":"Deduct the JPY 1.5 billion from the sale price and add it to the acquisition cost of the subsidiary shares"},{"ja":"累積している15億円を純損益に組み替え、子会社の売却損益に反映する","en":"Reclassify the accumulated JPY 1.5 billion to profit or loss and reflect it in the gain or loss on sale of the subsidiary"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"IFRSでは、在外営業活動体を処分するとき、その他の包括利益に累積した為替換算差額を純損益に組み替える。貸方残高15億円は売却益を増やす。為替差額を資本に残したままにすると、処分時点で実現した為替損益が損益計算書に現れなくなる。","en":"Under IFRS, when a foreign operation is disposed of, the translation differences accumulated in other comprehensive income are reclassified to profit or loss. A credit balance of JPY 1.5 billion increases the gain on sale. Leaving it in equity would keep the exchange gain realized on disposal out of the income statement."}},
{"id":"s18x44","dom":"cfocase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】新任CFOのA社は、ROEを現在の8%から3年後に10%へ引き上げる目標を掲げる。現状は純利益率5%、総資産回転率0.8回、財務レバレッジ2.0倍である。財務レバレッジを2.0倍に保ち、回転率も0.8回のままで目標を達成するための純利益率はいくらか。","en":"[Case] The new CFO of company A sets a goal of lifting ROE from 8% to 10% in three years. Today the net margin is 5%, asset turnover is 0.8x and financial leverage is 2.0x. Holding leverage at 2.0x and turnover at 0.8x, what net margin is needed to reach the goal?"},"choices":[{"ja":"6.25%","en":"6.25%"},{"ja":"5.50%","en":"5.50%"},{"ja":"7.50%","en":"7.50%"},{"ja":"12.50%","en":"12.50%"}],"ans":0,"exp":{"ja":"ROE＝純利益率×総資産回転率×財務レバレッジ。10%＝純利益率×0.8×2.0で、純利益率は10%÷1.6＝6.25%となる。12.5%はレバレッジを無視した値であり、5.5%などの小さな改善では目標に届かない。","en":"ROE = net margin x asset turnover x financial leverage. With 10% = margin x 0.8 x 2.0, the margin must be 10% / 1.6 = 6.25%. The 12.5% figure ignores leverage, and a small gain such as 5.5% falls short of the target."}},
{"id":"s18x45","dom":"cfocase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】グループ会社のX社には余剰資金20億円（預金金利0.1%）があり、同じグループのY社は銀行から15億円を金利1.5%で借りている。親会社がグループ内で資金を融通（キャッシュ・プーリング）し、Y社の借入を、X社の余剰資金で返済する場合、グループ全体の年間の金利負担の削減額はおよそいくらか。","en":"[Case] Group company X holds JPY 2.0 billion of surplus cash earning 0.1% on deposit, while group company Y has borrowed 1.5 billion from a bank at 1.5%. If the parent pools funds within the group so that Y repays its loan with X's surplus cash, roughly how much does the group's annual interest burden fall?"},"choices":[{"ja":"約2,250万円","en":"About JPY 22.5 million"},{"ja":"約2,100万円","en":"About JPY 21 million"},{"ja":"約3,000万円","en":"About JPY 30 million"},{"ja":"約150万円","en":"About JPY 1.5 million"}],"ans":1,"exp":{"ja":"Y社が支払っていた利息は15億円×1.5%＝2,250万円、X社の預金利息の逸失は15億円×0.1%＝150万円で、差し引き約2,100万円がグループ全体の削減額になる。逸失利息を引かない2,250万円は、プーリングのコストを見落としている。","en":"Y was paying 1.5 billion x 1.5% = JPY 22.5 million in interest, and X loses deposit interest of 1.5 billion x 0.1% = JPY 1.5 million, so the group saves about 21 million. Ignoring the lost deposit interest (22.5 million) misses the cost of pooling."}},
{"id":"s18x46","dom":"cfocase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】IFRSを適用する日本の親会社が、米国子会社（純資産2億ドル）を持つ。子会社の業績は好調だが、円高が進むと連結の為替換算調整勘定が悪化し、自己資本比率が低下する。取締役会から換算リスクの抑制策を求められたCFOが選ぶ方法として、最も適切なものはどれか。","en":"[Case] A Japanese parent that applies IFRS owns a US subsidiary with net assets of USD 200 million. The subsidiary is performing well, but a stronger yen worsens the consolidated foreign currency translation reserve and lowers the equity ratio. Asked by the board to limit this translation risk, which method should the CFO choose?"},"choices":[{"ja":"米国子会社の売上を円建てに変更し、取引通貨を円にそろえることで純資産の円換算も不要になり、換算調整勘定の変動を完全になくす","en":"Change the subsidiary's sales to yen-denominated so that, with the trading currency aligned to yen, translating net assets becomes unnecessary and movements in the translation reserve disappear entirely"},{"ja":"米国子会社の純資産を、毎期、円に両替して日本へ送金する","en":"Convert the subsidiary's net assets to yen every period and remit them to Japan"},{"ja":"同額規模のドル建て借入を純投資ヘッジに指定し、為替差損益の有効部分をその他の包括利益に計上して換算差額と相殺する","en":"Designate dollar borrowings of a similar size as a net investment hedge and take the effective portion of the exchange gains and losses to other comprehensive income to offset the translation difference"},{"ja":"円高に動いた時点で、米国子会社を売却する","en":"Sell the US subsidiary once the yen strengthens"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"海外子会社の純資産は期末レートで円換算され、その差額が為替換算調整勘定になる。同額規模の外貨建て借入を純投資ヘッジに指定すると、円高で純資産の円換算が減る分を借入の為替差益で相殺でき、有効部分はその他の包括利益で処理される。取引通貨を変えても、純資産の換算は変わらない。","en":"A foreign subsidiary's net assets are translated at the period-end rate, and the difference goes to the translation reserve. Designating similar-size foreign currency borrowings as a net investment hedge offsets the lower yen value of net assets from a stronger yen with exchange gains on the debt, with the effective portion in other comprehensive income. Changing the sales currency does not change how net assets are translated."}},
{"id":"s18x47","dom":"cfocase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】日本の機械メーカーである親会社が、100%子会社の米国販売会社に製品を年間200億円分販売している。販売価格の妥当性について両国の税務当局から否認され、二重課税となるリスクが高いとCFOは見ている。事前に最も有効な手続はどれか。","en":"[Case] A Japanese machinery maker sells JPY 20.0 billion of products a year to its wholly owned US sales subsidiary. The CFO sees a high risk that both countries' tax authorities will challenge the pricing, resulting in double taxation. Which advance procedure is most effective?"},"choices":[{"ja":"税務調査で否認されてから、その時点で相互協議を申し立てれば足りるので、事前の確認手続や当局との協議は行わない","en":"Skip advance confirmation procedures and consultation with the authorities, since seeking mutual agreement procedure after a challenge in an audit is enough"},{"ja":"子会社への販売価格を、第三者との取引価格より常に低く設定する","en":"Always set the sale price to the subsidiary lower than the price charged to third parties"},{"ja":"国税庁と相手国の税務当局に、価格の算定方法を事前に確認してもらう二国間の事前確認（APA）を申請する","en":"Apply for a bilateral advance pricing arrangement (APA), having the National Tax Agency and the other country's authority confirm the pricing method in advance"},{"ja":"米国販売会社の所在地を法人税率の低い第三国に移し、税務当局の関心を避ける","en":"Move the US sales company to a third country with a lower corporate tax rate to avoid the authorities' attention"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"移転価格税制のリスクは、独立企業間価格の算定方法を事前確認制度（APA）で両国の当局と合意しておけば大きく下げられ、二重課税も避けやすい。事後の相互協議は時間がかかる。低い価格設定やタックスヘイブンへの移転は、否認や追徴のリスクを高める。","en":"Transfer pricing risk falls sharply if the arm's-length pricing method is agreed with both authorities in advance under an advance pricing arrangement (APA), which also helps avoid double taxation. After-the-fact mutual agreement procedures take time. Setting prices low or moving to a tax haven raises the risk of challenge and assessments."}},
{"id":"s18x48","dom":"cfocase","diff":3,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社は、借入契約で『各期末の純資産を前期末の75%以上に維持する』財務制限条項を負う。前期末の純資産は400億円。当期は純利益20億円、配当10億円を見込む。ほかの純資産の変動は考えず、この条項を守る範囲で、当期に実行できる自社株買いの上限はいくらか。","en":"[Case] Company A's loan agreement contains a covenant to keep net assets at each period end at 75% or more of the prior year-end. Net assets at the prior year end were JPY 40.0 billion. This year it expects net income of 2.0 billion and dividends of 1.0 billion. Ignoring other changes in net assets, what is the maximum share buyback it can do this year while keeping the covenant?"},"choices":[{"ja":"100億円","en":"JPY 10.0 billion"},{"ja":"120億円","en":"JPY 12.0 billion"},{"ja":"130億円","en":"JPY 13.0 billion"},{"ja":"110億円","en":"JPY 11.0 billion"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"下限は400億円×75%＝300億円。純資産は400＋20−10−自社株買いで、これを300億円以上に保つには自社株買いは110億円までとなる。配当を引かない120億円、利益と配当を無視した100億円は、条項の計算とずれている。","en":"The floor is JPY 40.0 billion x 75% = 30.0 billion. Net assets end at 40.0 + 2.0 - 1.0 - buyback, so staying at or above 30.0 billion allows a buyback of up to 11.0 billion. Not deducting dividends (12.0 billion) or ignoring income and dividends (10.0 billion) does not match the covenant calculation."}},
{"id":"s18x49","dom":"cfocase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】A社は、10億円規模の海外子会社の買収を取締役会で決議した。時間の制約を理由にデューデリジェンスを省略し、外部専門家の意見も取らなかったところ、買収した子会社の価値がのちに大きく毀損した。株主から取締役の責任を問う声が上がっている。取締役の善管注意義務に関する、経営判断の原則の観点で最も適切な説明はどれか。","en":"[Case] Company A's board approved the acquisition of an overseas subsidiary worth JPY 1.0 billion, skipping due diligence because of time pressure and seeking no outside expert advice. The acquired subsidiary's value later fell sharply, and shareholders are asking whether the directors are responsible. Which explanation is most appropriate from the standpoint of the business judgment rule and directors' duty of care?"},"choices":[{"ja":"経営判断には広い裁量が認められているので、必要な手続や調査を省略しても責任を問われることはない","en":"Management decisions are allowed wide discretion, so skipping necessary procedures or investigation never gives rise to liability"},{"ja":"取締役は経営の結果に対して無限定に責任を負うため、会社に損失が出れば自動的に賠償責任を負うことになる","en":"Directors are liable without limit for management results, so whenever the company suffers a loss they automatically become liable for damages"},{"ja":"結果が悪いだけでは責任を問われないが、情報収集や検討の過程が不合理なら、善管注意義務違反とされうる","en":"Directors are not liable merely for a bad outcome, but if the information gathering and deliberation were unreasonable, they may be found in breach of the duty of care"},{"ja":"外部専門家の意見を取りさえすれば、検討の内容に関係なく、常に責任は免除される","en":"Obtaining outside expert advice always exempts directors from liability, whatever the substance of their deliberation"}],"ans":2,"exp":{"ja":"経営判断の原則では、取締役の判断は、事実認識の過程と意思決定の内容に不合理がなければ尊重される。ただし、必要なデューデリジェンスや専門家の意見を省略すると、判断過程が不合理とされ、善管注意義務違反を問われうる。結果の悪さだけで責任が生じるのではなく、専門家の意見を取るだけで責任が免れるわけでもない。","en":"Under the business judgment rule, a director's decision is respected if the process of establishing the facts and the substance of the decision are not unreasonable. Skipping necessary due diligence or expert advice can make the process unreasonable and expose directors to a breach of duty of care. A bad outcome alone does not create liability, and merely obtaining expert advice does not guarantee immunity."}},
{"id":"s18x50","dom":"cfocase","diff":2,"q":{"ja":"【ケース】店舗の賃借が多い小売業のA社は、リースの会計基準の改正により、これまで費用処理していた賃借契約を、使用権資産とリース負債として貸借対照表に計上することになった。有利子負債のEBITDA倍率を財務制限条項としている貸し手との関係で、CFOが事前に行うべきことはどれか。","en":"[Case] Retailer A, which leases many stores, must under a revised lease accounting standard record lease contracts previously expensed as right-of-use assets and lease liabilities on its balance sheet. Its lenders use a debt/EBITDA multiple as a covenant. What should the CFO do beforehand?"},"choices":[{"ja":"基準の変更は経済実態そのものを変えないので、貸し手とは協議せず、改正後の数値で財務制限条項の判定も行う","en":"Hold no discussion with lenders because the standard change does not alter economic reality itself, and test the covenants on the revised figures"},{"ja":"指標を改善するため、店舗の賃借契約を解約して、リース負債を減らす","en":"Cancel store lease contracts to reduce lease liabilities and improve the measure"},{"ja":"基準変更に合わせて、リース負債を有利子負債から除くことを貸し手に一方的に通知する","en":"Unilaterally notify lenders that lease liabilities will be excluded from interest-bearing debt to match the standard change"},{"ja":"リース負債が指標に含まれるかなど、財務制限条項の定義が変わるかを貸し手と協議し、必要なら定義を改める","en":"Discuss with lenders whether covenant definitions change, such as whether lease liabilities count in the measure, and amend the definitions if necessary"}],"ans":3,"exp":{"ja":"新しいリース基準でリース負債が貸借対照表に載ると、財務制限条項の指標（有利子負債/EBITDAなど）の定義次第で数値が大きく変わりうる。抵触を避けるため、事前に貸し手と指標の定義を協議して契約を改める。協議なしに報告したり、一方的に除外を通知すると、契約違反のリスクがある。","en":"Once lease liabilities reach the balance sheet under the new standard, covenant measures such as debt/EBITDA can change a lot depending on how they are defined. To avoid a breach, discuss definitions with lenders beforehand and amend the agreement. Reporting without discussion or unilaterally excluding the liabilities risks breach of contract."}}
);
